(79, '16 Channel Relay Controller Board -12V', 78, 'Active', '<p>Numato 16 Relay breakout module is a smart choice for controlling higher current loads from your microcontroller development board, PC parallel port or your favourite Arduino. This board has sixteen on-board relays which can switch up to 10A. All relay terminals (C, NC, NO) are accessible through screw terminals which makes wiring up the board very easy. The relays are driven by popular darlington array ULN2803. Relay coil is rated for 12VDC.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Features</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>Very compact and easy to wire up</li>\r\n	<li>1.6mm FR4 PCB with Green solder mask and white silk screen</li>\r\n	<li>Connects directly to TTL devices (Microcontrollers, Arduino etc..)</li>\r\n	<li>Sixteen Relays with&nbsp;three pin screw terminals for easy connectivity</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Applications</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>Home Automation</li>\r\n	<li>Industrial Automation</li>\r\n	<li>Lighting Control</li>\r\n	<li>Garden Equipment Control</li>\r\n	<li>Test Fixtures</li>\r\n	<li>DIY and Hobby</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n', '<table class=\"shop_attributes\">\r\n	<tbody>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Weight</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>0.70 lbs</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Dimensions</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>10.00 x 5.00 x 2.00 in</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Number Of Relays</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>16</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Relay Type</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p><a href=\"https://numato.com/relay-type/mechanical\" rel=\"tag\">Mechanical</a></p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Max Relay Current Rating</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>10A</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Communication</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>TTL Compatible Input</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>RoHS</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>Yes</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Relay Driver</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>ULN2803</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n	</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n', 1, 'Yes', '2018-02-13', '<p>Numato 16 Relay breakout module is a smart choice for controlling higher current loads from your microcontroller development board, PC parallel port or your favourite Arduino.<br />\r\n<strong>Features</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>16 on board SPDT Relays.</li>\r\n	<li>7A Maximum Switching Current.</li>\r\n	<li>Very compact and easy to wire up.</li>\r\n	<li>Connects directly to TTL devices (Microcontrollers, Arduino etc..).</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Applications</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>Home Automation</li>\r\n	<li>Industrial Automation</li>\r\n	<li>Lighting Control</li>\r\n	<li>Garden Equipment Control</li>\r\n	<li>Test Fixtures</li>\r\n	<li>DIY and Hobby</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n', 'SKU: RL40003', 31.99, 0, 0, 2, 63, 62, 1),
(80, '2 Channel Programmable Relay Module', 78, 'Active', '<p>Numato Lab`s 2 Channel Programmable Relay Module is a feature rich product that can be programmed with Arduino IDE. The USB to Serial Chip FT232RL helps uploading sketches quickly to the board. This programmability gives this board ultimate flexibility compared to other relay modules where features depend on the pre-programmed firmware. The onboard programmable relays, digital I/O&rsquo;s, analog inputs, Real Time Clock(RTC) and Micro SD memory card slot makes this module useful for learning as well as making sophisticated applications.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Features</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>Atmega328p Micro controller with 32KBytes flash memory</li>\r\n	<li>Arduino IDE Compatible</li>\r\n	<li>FT232RL chip for USB &ndash; Serial Interface</li>\r\n	<li>2 SPDT 12V Mechanical Relays</li>\r\n	<li>4 Digital I/O&rsquo;s</li>\r\n	<li>2 PWM outs</li>\r\n	<li>4 Analog Inputs</li>\r\n	<li>I2C Interface</li>\r\n	<li>Real Time Clock(RTC)</li>\r\n	<li>Battery backup for RTC</li>\r\n	<li>Micro SD Card Slot</li>\r\n	<li>LED indicators for Power, TX, RX and Relays</li>\r\n	<li>ISP for programming custom boot loader/ firmware</li>\r\n	<li>16 MHz Crystal</li>\r\n	<li>USB mini Connector for host communication</li>\r\n	<li>Based on Arduino Duemilanove at arduino.cc</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Applications</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>Home Automation</li>\r\n	<li>Lighting Control</li>\r\n	<li>Garden Equipment Control</li>\r\n	<li>Industrial Automation</li>\r\n	<li>Test Fixtures</li>\r\n	<li>DIY and Hobby</li>\r\n	<li>Real Time Clock</li>\r\n	<li>Data logging</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n', '<table class=\"shop_attributes\">\r\n	<tbody>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Weight</th>\r\n			<td>0.20 lbs</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Dimensions</th>\r\n			<td>5.00 x 3.00 x 2.00 in</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Number Of Relays</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>2</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Relay Type</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p><a href=\"https://numato.com/relay-type/mechanical\" rel=\"tag\">Mechanical</a></p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Max Relay Current Rating</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>10A</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Number Of GPIOs (Max)</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>10</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Analog Inputs</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>4(Multiplexed with IOs)</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Analog Input Resolution</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>10 Bits</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n	</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n', 11, 'Yes', '2018-02-13', '<p>Numato Lab`s 2 Channel Programmable Relay Module is a feature rich product that can be programmed with Arduino IDE. The USB to Serial Chip FT232RL helps uploading sketches quickly to the board. This programmability gives this board ultimate flexibility compared to other relay modules where features depend on the pre-programmed firmware.<br />\r\n<strong>Features</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>2 on board SPDT Relays .</li>\r\n	<li>7A Maximum Switching Current.</li>\r\n	<li>Atmega328p Micro controller with 32KBytes flash memory.</li>\r\n	<li>Arduino IDE Compatible.</li>\r\n	<li>FT232RL chip for USB to Serial Interface.</li>\r\n	<li>4 Digital I/O&rsquo;s, 4 Analog Inputs, 2 PWM outs</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n', 'SKU: PRLY001', 56.99, 0, 0, 1, 2, 1, 1),
(82, '2 Channel Relay Controller Board', 78, 'Active', '								<p>Numato 2 Relay breakout module is a smart choice for controlling higher current loads from your microcontroller development board or a PC parallel port. This board has two on-board relays which can switch up to 10A. All relay terminals (C, NC, NO) are accessible through screw terminals which makes wiring up the board very easy.  The relays are driven by popular darlington array ULN2003. Relay coil is rated for 12VDC.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Features</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>Very compact and easy to wire up</li>\r\n	<li>1.6mm FR4 PCB with black solder mask and white silk screen</li>\r\n	<li>Connects directly to TTL devices (Microcontrollers, Arduino etc..)</li>\r\n	<li>Two Relays with one three pin screw terminals for easy connectivity</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Applications</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>Home Automation</li>\r\n	<li>Industrial Automation</li>\r\n	<li>Lighting Control</li>\r\n	<li>Garden Equipment Control</li>\r\n	<li>Test Fixtures</li>\r\n	<li>DIY and Hobby</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n', '								 <table class=\"shop_attributes\">\r\n	<tbody>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Weight</th>\r\n			<td>0.15 lbs</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Dimensions</th>\r\n			<td>5.00 x 3.00 x 2.00 in</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Number Of Relays</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>2</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Relay Type</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p><a href=\"https://numato.com/relay-type/mechanical\" rel=\"tag\">Mechanical</a></p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Max Relay Current Rating</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>10A</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Communication</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>TTL Compatible Input</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n	</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n', 3, 'Yes', '2018-02-13', '								<p>Numato 2 Relay breakout module is a smart choice for controlling higher current loads from your microcontroller development board or a PC parallel port.<br />\r\n<strong>Features</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>2 on board SPDT Relays .</li>\r\n	<li>7A Maximum Switching Current.</li>\r\n	<li>ULN2003 Relay Driver.</li>\r\n	<li>Very compact and easy to wire up</li>\r\n	<li>Connects directly to TTL devices (Microcontrollers, Arduino etc..).</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Applications</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>Home Automation</li>\r\n	<li>Industrial Automation</li>\r\n	<li>Lighting Control</li>\r\n	<li>Garden Equipment Control</li>\r\n	<li>Test Fixtures</li>\r\n	<li>DIY and Hobby</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n', 'SKU: RL20002', 14.99, 0, 0, 2, 9, 7, 2),
(84, '2 Channel Solid State Relay Controller Board', 78, 'Active', '<p>Numato 2 Channel Solid State Relay breakout module is a smart choice for controlling higher current loads from your microcontroller development board, PC parallel port or your favorite Arduino. This board has two on-board Solid State Relays which can switch up to 3A. All relay terminals are accessible through screw terminals which makes wiring up the board very easy. The relays are driven by popular darlington array ULN2003. This product is available for purchase with AC or DC Solid State Relays.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Features</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>Very compact and easy to wire up</li>\r\n	<li>1.6mm FR4 PCB with black solder mask and white silk screen</li>\r\n	<li>Connects directly to TTL devices (Microcontrollers, Arduino etc..)</li>\r\n	<li>Two Solid State Relays with&nbsp;one two pin screw terminals for easy connectivity</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Applications</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>Home Automation</li>\r\n	<li>Industrial Automation</li>\r\n	<li>Lighting Control</li>\r\n	<li>Garden Equipment Control</li>\r\n	<li>Test Fixtures</li>\r\n	<li>DIY and Hobby</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n', '<table class=\"shop_attributes\">\r\n	<tbody>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Weight</th>\r\n			<td>0.20 lbs</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Dimensions</th>\r\n			<td>5.00 x 3.00 x 2.00 in</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Relay Type</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>Solid State AC, Solid State DC</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Number of Relays</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>2</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Max Relay Current Rating</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>3A</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Relay driver</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>ULN2003</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n	</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n', 4, 'Yes', '2018-02-13', '<p>Numato 2 Channel Solid State Relay breakout module is a smart choice for controlling higher current loads from your microcontroller development board, PC parallel port or your favorite Arduino. This board has two on-board Solid State Relays which can switch up to 3A. All relay terminals are accessible through screw terminals which makes wiring up the board very easy. The relays are driven by popular darlington array ULN2003. This product is available for purchase with AC or DC Solid State Relays.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Features</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>2 on board Solid State Relays .</li>\r\n	<li>3A Maximum Switching Current.</li>\r\n	<li>ULN2003 Relay Driver.</li>\r\n	<li>Very compact and easy to wire up</li>\r\n	<li>LED indication for Power and individual relay status.</li>\r\n	<li>Connects directly to TTL devices (Microcontrollers, Arduino etc..).</li>\r\n	<li>Fuses are provided for over current protection for each relay.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n', 'SKU: SSRC20001', 41.95, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0),
(86, 'CS4344 Audio Expansion Module', 88, 'Active', '<p>This module features CS4344, a 24-Bit, 192 kHz Stereo D/A Converter which enables producing high &nbsp;quality stereo audio from a digital source. It supports all major audio data interface formats. This &nbsp;module is designed to be used with Numato Lab&rsquo;s FPGA/Microcontroller boards featuring a 2&times;6 pin &nbsp;Expansion connector. It can also be used with other boards and connector types by using manual wiring.This product is compatible with most of&nbsp;Numato Lab&rsquo;s FPGA boards.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Features</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>Fourth-order Multi-bit Delta-Sigma Modulator with a linear analog low-pass filter</li>\r\n	<li>Automatically Detects Sample Rates up to 192 kHz</li>\r\n	<li>24-bit Conversion</li>\r\n	<li>105 dB Dynamic Range</li>\r\n	<li>Dimension: 41mm X 19mm</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Applications</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>Product prototyping</li>\r\n	<li>Gaming consoles</li>\r\n	<li>Audio playback devices</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n', '<table class=\"shop_attributes\">\r\n	<tbody>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Weight</th>\r\n			<td>0.10 lbs</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Dimensions</th>\r\n			<td>5.00 x 3.00 x 2.00 in</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Audio Out</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>Analog</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>CODEC Device</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>CS4344</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Resolution</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>24 Bit</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Power Supply</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>3.3V</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n	</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n', 3, 'Yes', '2018-02-13', '<p>This module features CS4344, a 24-Bit, 192 kHz Stereo D/A Converter which enables producing high quality stereo audio from a digital source. It supports all major audio data interface formats. This module is designed to be used with Numato Lab&rsquo;s FPGA/Microcontroller boards featuring a 2&times;6 pin Expansion connector. It can also be used with other boards and connector types by using manual wiring.This product is compatible with most of Numato Lab&rsquo;s FPGA boards.<br />\r\n<strong>Features</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>Fourth-order Multi-bit Delta-Sigma Modulator with a linear analog low-pass filter</li>\r\n	<li>Automatically Detects Sample Rates up to 192 kHz</li>\r\n	<li>24-bit Conversion</li>\r\n	<li>105 dB Dynamic Range</li>\r\n	<li>Dimension: 41mm X 19mm</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n', 'SKU: EXPAUD002', 19.99, 0, 0, 0, 3, 2, 1),
(88, '4 Channel Programmable Relay Module', 78, 'Active', '<p>Numato Lab`s 4 Channel Programmable Relay Module is a feature rich product that can be programmed with Arduino IDE. The USB to Serial Chip FT232RL helps uploading sketches quickly to the board. This programmability gives this board ultimate flexibility compared to other relay modules where features depend on the pre-programmed firmware. The onboard programmable relays, digital I/O`s, analog inputs, Real Time Clock(RTC) and Micro SD memory card slot makes this module useful for learning as well as making sophisticated applications.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Features</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>Atmega328p Micro controller with 32KBytes flash memory</li>\r\n	<li>Arduino IDE Compatible</li>\r\n	<li>FT232RL chip for USB &ndash; Serial Interface</li>\r\n	<li>4 SPDT 12V Mechanical Relays</li>\r\n	<li>3 Digital I/O&rsquo;s</li>\r\n	<li>2 PWM outs</li>\r\n	<li>4 Analog Inputs</li>\r\n	<li>I2C Interface</li>\r\n	<li>Real Time Clock(RTC)</li>\r\n	<li>Battery backup for RTC</li>\r\n	<li>Micro SD Card Slot</li>\r\n	<li>LED indicators for Power, TX, RX and Relays</li>\r\n	<li>ISP for programming custom boot loader/ firmware</li>\r\n	<li>16 MHz Crystal</li>\r\n	<li>USB mini Connector for host communication</li>\r\n	<li>Based on Arduino Duemilanove at arduino.cc</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Applications</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>Home Automation</li>\r\n	<li>Lighting Control</li>\r\n	<li>Garden Equipment Control</li>\r\n	<li>Industrial Automation</li>\r\n	<li>Test Fixtures</li>\r\n	<li>DIY and Hobby</li>\r\n	<li>Real Time Clock</li>\r\n	<li>Data logging</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n', '<table class=\"shop_attributes\">\r\n	<tbody>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Weight</th>\r\n			<td>0.25 lbs</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Dimensions</th>\r\n			<td>5.00 x 3.00 x 2.00 in</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Number Of Relays</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>4</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Relay Type</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p><a href=\"https://numato.com/relay-type/mechanical\" rel=\"tag\">Mechanical</a></p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Max Relay Current Rating</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>10A</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Analog Inputs</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>4(Multiplexed with IOs)</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Analog Input Resolution</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>10 Bits</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Number Of GPIOs (Max)</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>7</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n	</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n', 6, 'Yes', '2018-02-13', '<p>Numato Lab`s 4 Channel Programmable Relay Module is a feature rich product that can be programmed with Arduino IDE. The USB to Serial Chip FT232RL helps uploading sketches quickly to the board. This programmability gives this board ultimate flexibility compared to other relay modules where features depend on the pre-programmed firmware. The onboard programmable relays, digital I/O`s, analog inputs, Real Time Clock(RTC) and Micro SD memory card slot makes this module useful for learning as well as making sophisticated applications.<br />\r\n<strong>Features</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>4 on board SPDT Relays .</li>\r\n	<li>7A Maximum Switching Current.</li>\r\n	<li>Atmega328p Micro controller with 32KBytes flash memory.</li>\r\n	<li>Arduino IDE Compatible.</li>\r\n	<li>FT232RL chip for USB to Serial Interface.</li>\r\n	<li>3 Digital I/O&rsquo;s, 4 Analog Inputs, 2 PWM outs</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n', 'SKU: PRLY002', 74.99, 0, 0, 1, 1, 0, 1),
(89, 'LM4550 AC’97 Stereo Audio Codec Expansion Module', 88, 'Active', '<p>This module features LM4550, an AC&rsquo;97 Rev 2.1 compliant audio codec which enables producing and recording high quality stereo audio. This &nbsp;module is designed to be used with Numato Lab&rsquo;s FPGA/Microcontroller boards featuring a 2&times;6 pin &nbsp;Expansion connector. It can also be used with other boards and connector types by using manual wiring. This product is compatible with many Numato Lab&rsquo;s FPGA boards.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Features</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>One 2&times;6 pin Expansion connector</li>\r\n	<li>AC&rsquo;97 Rev 2.1 compliant</li>\r\n	<li>90 dB Dynamic Range</li>\r\n	<li>Stereo Headphone Amp With Separate Gain Control</li>\r\n	<li>Dimension: 50mm x 46mm</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Applications</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>Product Prototype Development</li>\r\n	<li>Audio Record/Playback Systems</li>\r\n	<li>Media players</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n', '<table class=\"shop_attributes\">\r\n	<tbody>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Weight</th>\r\n			<td>0.10 lbs</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Dimensions</th>\r\n			<td>5.00 x 3.00 x 2.00 in</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Audio Codec</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>AC97</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Audio Out</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>Analog</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Codec Device</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>LM4550</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n	</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n', 4, 'Yes', '2018-02-13', '<p>this module features LM4550, an AC&rsquo;97 Rev 2.1 compliant audio codec which enables producing and recording high quality stereo audio. This &nbsp;module is designed to be used with Numato Lab&rsquo;s FPGA/Microcontroller boards featuring a 2&times;6 pin &nbsp;Expansion connector. It can also be used with other boards and connector types by using manual wiring. This product is compatible with many Numato Lab&rsquo;s FPGA boards.<br />\r\n<strong>Features</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>One 2&times;6 pin Expansion connector</li>\r\n	<li>AC&rsquo;97 Rev 2.1 compliant</li>\r\n	<li>90 dB Dynamic Range</li>\r\n	<li>Stereo Headphone Amp With Separate Gain Control</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Applications</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>Product Prototype Development</li>\r\n	<li>Audio Record/Playback Systems</li>\r\n	<li>Media players</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n', 'SKU: EXPAUD003', 37.99, 0, 0, 0, 3, 3, 0),
(90, '4 Channel Relay Controller Board', 78, 'Active', '								<p>Numato 4 Relay breakout module is a smart choice for controlling higher current loads from your microcontroller development board, PC parallel port or your favorite Arduino. This board has four on-board relays which can switch up to 10A. All relay terminals (C, NC, NO) are accessible through screw terminals which makes wiring up the board very easy. The relays are driven by popular darlington array ULN2003. Relay coil is rated for 12VDC.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Features</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>Very compact and easy to wire up</li>\r\n	<li>1.6mm FR4 PCB with black solder mask and white silk screen</li>\r\n	<li>Connects directly to TTL devices (Microcontrollers, Arduino etc..)</li>\r\n	<li>Four Relays with one three pin screw terminals for easy connectivity</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Applications</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>Home Automation</li>\r\n	<li>Industrial Automation</li>\r\n	<li>Lighting Control</li>\r\n	<li>Garden Equipment Control</li>\r\n	<li>Test Fixtures</li>\r\n	<li>DIY and Hobby</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n', '								 <table class=\"shop_attributes\">\r\n	<tbody>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Weight</th>\r\n			<td>0.20 lbs</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Dimensions</th>\r\n			<td>5.00 x 3.00 x 2.00 in</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Number Of Relays</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>4</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Relay Type</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p><a href=\"https://numato.com/relay-type/mechanical\" rel=\"tag\">Mechanical</a></p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Max Relay Current Rating</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>10A</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Communication</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>TTL Compatibe Input</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n	</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n', 6, 'Yes', '2018-02-13', '								<p>Numato 4 Relay breakout module is a smart choice for controlling higher current loads from your microcontroller development board, PC parallel port or your favorite Arduino.<br />\r\n<strong>Features</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>4 on board SPDT Relays .</li>\r\n	<li>7A Maximum Switching Current.</li>\r\n	<li>ULN2003 Relay Driver.</li>\r\n	<li>Very compact and easy to wire up</li>\r\n	<li>Connects directly to TTL devices (Microcontrollers, Arduino etc..).</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Applications</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>Home Automation</li>\r\n	<li>Industrial Automation</li>\r\n	<li>Lighting Control</li>\r\n	<li>Garden Equipment Control</li>\r\n	<li>Test Fixtures</li>\r\n	<li>DIY and Hobby</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n', 'SKU: RL40002', 19.99, 0, 0, 2, 7, 4, 3),
(91, '4 Channel Solid State Relay Controller Board', 78, 'Active', '<p>Numato 4 Channel Solid State Relay breakout module is a smart choice for controlling higher current loads from your microcontroller development board, PC parallel port or your favorite Arduino. This board has four on-board Solid State Relays which can switch up to 3A. All relay terminals are accessible through screw terminals which makes wiring up the board very easy. The relays are driven by popular darlington array ULN2003. This product is available for purchase with AC or DC Solid State Relays.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Features</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>Very compact and easy to wire up</li>\r\n	<li>1.6mm FR4 PCB with black solder mask and white silk screen</li>\r\n	<li>Connects directly to TTL devices (Microcontrollers, Arduino etc..)</li>\r\n	<li>Four Solid State Relays with&nbsp;one two pin screw terminals for easy connectivity</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Applications</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>Home Automation</li>\r\n	<li>Industrial Automation</li>\r\n	<li>Lighting Control</li>\r\n	<li>Garden Equipment Control</li>\r\n	<li>Test Fixtures</li>\r\n	<li>DIY and Hobby</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n', '<table class=\"shop_attributes\">\r\n	<tbody>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Weight</th>\r\n			<td>0.20 lbs</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Dimensions</th>\r\n			<td>6.00 x 5.00 x 2.00 in</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Relay Type</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>Solid State AC, Solid State DC</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Number of Relays</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>4</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Max Relay Current Rating</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>3A</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Relay Driver</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>ULN2003</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n	</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n', 8, 'Yes', '2018-02-13', '<p>Numato 4 Channel Solid State Relay breakout module is a smart choice for controlling higher current loads from your microcontroller development board, PC parallel port or your favorite Arduino. This board has four on-board Solid State Relays which can switch up to 3A. All relay terminals are accessible through screw terminals which makes wiring up the board very easy. The relays are driven by popular darlington array ULN2003. This product is available for purchase with AC or DC Solid State Relays.<br />\r\n<strong>Features</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>4 on board Solid State Relays .</li>\r\n	<li>3A Maximum Switching Current.</li>\r\n	<li>ULN2003 Relay Driver.</li>\r\n	<li>LED indication for Power and individual relay status.</li>\r\n	<li>Connects directly to TTL devices (Microcontrollers, Arduino etc..).</li>\r\n	<li>Fuses are provided for over current protection for each relay.</li>\r\n	<li>Very compact and easy to wire up</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<div>\r\n<p><img alt=\"Flag Icon USA\" class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-5328\" src=\"https://numato.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/10/us.png\" style=\"height:11px; width:16px\" />&nbsp;CO, USA Warehouse :&nbsp;In Stock, Shipping today!<br />\r\n<img alt=\"Flag Icon India\" class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-5329\" src=\"https://numato.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/10/in.png\" style=\"height:11px; width:16px\" />&nbsp;BLR, India Warehouse:&nbsp;In Stock, Shipping today!</p>\r\n</div>\r\n', 'SKU: SSRC40001', 81.99, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0),
(92, '32 Channel Relay Controller Board- 24V', 78, 'Active', '<p>Numato 8 Relay breakout module is a smart choice for controlling higher current loads from your microcontroller development board, PC parallel port or your favourite Arduino. This board has eight on-board relays which can switch up to 10A. All relay terminals (C, NC, NO) are accessible through screw terminals which makes wiring up the board very easy. The relays are driven by popular darlington array ULN2803. Relay coil is rated for 12VDC.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Features</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>Very compact and easy to wire up</li>\r\n	<li>1.6mm FR4 PCB with Green solder mask and white silk screen</li>\r\n	<li>Connects directly to TTL devices (Microcontrollers, Arduino etc..)</li>\r\n	<li>Eight Relays with&nbsp;three pin screw terminals for easy connectivity</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Applications</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>Home Automation</li>\r\n	<li>Industrial Automation</li>\r\n	<li>Lighting Control</li>\r\n	<li>Garden Equipment Control</li>\r\n	<li>Test Fixtures</li>\r\n	<li>DIY and Hobby</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n', '<table class=\"shop_attributes\">\r\n	<tbody>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Weight</th>\r\n			<td>0.30 lbs</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Dimensions</th>\r\n			<td>5.00 x 3.00 x 2.00 in</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Number Of Relays</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>8</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Relay Type</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p><a href=\"https://numato.com/relay-type/mechanical\" rel=\"tag\">Mechanical</a></p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Max Relay Current Rating</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>10A</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Communication</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>TTL Compatible Input</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n	</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n', 9, 'Yes', '2018-02-13', '<p>Numato 8 Relay breakout module is a smart choice for controlling higher current loads from your microcontroller development board, PC parallel port or your favourite Arduino.<br />\r\n<strong>Features</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>8 on board SPDT Relays .</li>\r\n	<li>7A Maximum Switching Current.</li>\r\n	<li>ULN2803 Relay Driver.</li>\r\n	<li>Very compact and easy to wire up</li>\r\n	<li>Connects directly to TTL devices (Microcontrollers, Arduino etc..).</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Applications</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>Home Automation</li>\r\n	<li>Industrial Automation</li>\r\n	<li>Lighting Control</li>\r\n	<li>Garden Equipment Control</li>\r\n	<li>Test Fixtures</li>\r\n	<li>DIY and Hobby</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n', 'SKU: RL40004-24', 82.95, 0, 0, 1, 14, 25, -11),
(93, '8 Channel Solid State Relay Controller Board', 78, 'Active', '<p>Numato 8 Channel Solid State Relay breakout module is a smart choice for controlling higher current loads from your microcontroller development board, PC parallel port or your favorite Arduino. This board has eight on-board Solid State Relays which can switch up to 3A. All relay terminals are accessible through screw terminals which makes wiring up the board very easy. The relays are driven by popular darlington array ULN2003. This product is available for purchase with AC or DC Solid State Relays.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Features</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>Very compact and easy to wire up</li>\r\n	<li>1.6mm FR4 PCB with black solder mask and white silk screen</li>\r\n	<li>Connects directly to TTL devices (Microcontrollers, Arduino etc..)</li>\r\n	<li>Four Solid State Relays with&nbsp;one two pin screw terminals for easy connectivity</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Applications</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>Home Automation</li>\r\n	<li>Industrial Automation</li>\r\n	<li>Lighting Control</li>\r\n	<li>Garden Equipment Control</li>\r\n	<li>Test Fixtures</li>\r\n	<li>DIY and Hobby</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n', '<table class=\"shop_attributes\">\r\n	<tbody>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Weight</th>\r\n			<td>0.35 lbs</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Dimensions</th>\r\n			<td>10.00 x 5.00 x 2.00 in</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Relay Type</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>Solid State AC, Solid State DC</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Number of Relays</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>8</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Max Relay Current Rating</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>3A</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Relay Driver</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>ULN2803</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n	</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n', 10, 'Yes', '2018-02-13', '<p>Numato 8 Channel Solid State Relay breakout module is a smart choice for controlling higher current loads from your microcontroller development board, PC parallel port or your favorite Arduino. This board has eight on-board Solid State Relays which can switch up to 3A.<br />\r\n<strong>Features</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>8 on board Solid State Relays .</li>\r\n	<li>3A Maximum Switching Current.</li>\r\n	<li>ULN2003 Relay Driver.</li>\r\n	<li>LED indication for Power and individual relay status.</li>\r\n	<li>Connects directly to TTL devices (Microcontrollers, Arduino etc..).</li>\r\n	<li>Fuses are provided for over current protection for each relay.</li>\r\n	<li>Very compact and easy to wire up</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Applications</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>Home Automation</li>\r\n	<li>Industrial Automation</li>\r\n	<li>Lighting Control</li>\r\n	<li>Garden Equipment Control</li>\r\n	<li>Test Fixtures</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n', 'SKU: SSRC80001', 112.99, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1, -1);
INSERT INTO `tbl_product` (`product_id`, `product_name`, `product_category_id`, `product_status`, `product_description`, `product_specification`, `priorty`, `display_flag`, `product_entry_date`, `product_details`, `product_code`, `product_amt`, `product_tax`, `product_discount`, `product_threshold`, `total_product`, `total_sold`, `total_remaining`) VALUES
(94, '100BASE-T Ethernet Expansion Module', 89, 'Active', '<p>The heart of the Ethernet Expansion module is LAN8710A, a low-power 10BASE-T/100BASE-TX physical layer (PHY) transceiver. LAN8710A supports communication with Ethernet MAC layer via &nbsp;standard MII (IEEE 802.3u) interface. LAN8710A full-duplex 10-BASE-T/100BASE-TX transceiver and supports 10Mbps (10BASE-T) and 100Mbps (100BASE-TX) operation.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>LAN8710A implements auto-negotiation to automatically determine the best possible speed and mode of operation. HP Auto-MDIX support allows the use of direct connect or cross-over LAN cables. Ethernet Expansion Module also has Microchip 24AA02E48 2Kbit EEPROM with built in unique MAC address. This MAC address can be read from the EEPROM and used for the Ethernet interface. This ethernet module can be used with Numato FPGA boards or other FPGA/Microcontroller development boards.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Features</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>Three 2&times;6 pin Expansion connectors</li>\r\n	<li>High-Performance 10/100 Ethernet Transceiver</li>\r\n	<li>Single-Chip Ethernet Physical Layer Transceiver (PHY)</li>\r\n	<li>2 Kbit Electrically Erasable PROM (24AA02E48) for MAC Address</li>\r\n	<li>Dimension: 61.5mm X 61.5mm</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Applications</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>Product Prototype Development</li>\r\n	<li>Network appliance development</li>\r\n	<li>Embedded Telecom Applications</li>\r\n	<li>Digital Media Adapters /Servers</li>\r\n	<li>Development and testing of custom Projects</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n', '<table class=\"shop_attributes\">\r\n	<tbody>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Weight</th>\r\n			<td>0.15 lbs</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Dimensions</th>\r\n			<td>5.00 x 3.00 x 2.00 in</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Number of Ethernet Ports</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>1</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Supported Speeds</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>100BASE-T, 10BASE-T</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Ethernet PHY</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>LAN8710A</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Interface</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>MII</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>MAC Address</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>Yes</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>MAC Storage</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>External I2C EEPROM (24AA02E48)</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>External EEPROM Size</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>2Kbits</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n	</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n', 1, 'Yes', '2018-02-13', '<p>The heart of the Ethernet Expansion module is LAN8710A, a low-power 10BASE-T/100BASE-TX physical layer (PHY) transceiver. LAN8710A supports communication with Ethernet MAC layer via &nbsp;standard MII (IEEE 802.3u) interface. LAN8710A full-duplex 10-BASE-T/100BASE-TX transceiver and supports 10Mbps (10BASE-T) and 100Mbps (100BASE-TX) operation.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Features</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>Three 2&times;6 pin Expansion connectors</li>\r\n	<li>High-Performance 10/100 Ethernet Transceiver</li>\r\n	<li>Single-Chip Ethernet Physical Layer Transceiver (PHY)</li>\r\n	<li>2 Kbit Electrically Erasable PROM (24AA02E48) for MAC Address</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Applications</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>Product Prototype Development</li>\r\n	<li>Network appliance development</li>\r\n	<li>Embedded Telecom Applications</li>\r\n	<li>Digital Media Adapters /Servers</li>\r\n	<li>Development and testing of custom Projects</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n', 'SKU: EXPETH001', 25.99, 0, 0, 3, 18, 16, 2),
(97, '1 Channel USB Powered Solid State Relay Module', 77, 'Active', '<p>Numato Lab`s Channel USB Solid State&nbsp;Relay Module is great for controlling your devices through USB without any USB protocol knowledge. This modules plugs in to your design seamlessly. Individual relay can be controlled by simple commands.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>This product has two on board Solid State&nbsp;&nbsp;Relays that can switch up to 3A load.The relays are controlled by USB capable Microchip PIC Microcontroller (PIC18F14K50) and comes with built in firmware that supports simple commands to control relays and read relay status. The board, when attached to a PC/Laptop shows up as a serial port and all you need to control the board is a serial terminal application like HyperTerminal or Putty. This board can easily be controlled by writing simple serial port application in VC++, VB, VBA (Word, Excell etc), Perl, Python etc. The relays are powered from USB bus so it is important to connect this board directly to a PC or to a powered hub.<br />\r\n<strong>Features</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>1 on board Solid State Relay.</li>\r\n	<li>3A Maximum Switching Current.</li>\r\n	<li>4 TTL (3.3V)Compatible GPIOs.</li>\r\n	<li>4 Analog Input Channels (Multiplexed with GPIOs).</li>\r\n	<li>10 bits Analog Input Resolution.</li>\r\n	<li>USB interface with CDC support. As easy as using a serial port, no USB knowledge required.</li>\r\n	<li>Solid State Relay contacts available on easy to access screw terminals.</li>\r\n	<li>Can be controlled by using standard serial console applications or custom applications.</li>\r\n	<li>Can be powered from USB or external power supply.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Applications</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>Home Automation</li>\r\n	<li>Industrial Automation</li>\r\n	<li>Lighting Control</li>\r\n	<li>Garden Equipment Control</li>\r\n	<li>Test Fixtures</li>\r\n	<li>DIY and Hobby</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Supporting operating Systems</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>Windows XP</li>\r\n	<li>Windows 7</li>\r\n	<li>Windows 8/8.1</li>\r\n	<li>Windows 10</li>\r\n	<li>Linux</li>\r\n	<li>Mac OS X</li>\r\n	<li>Android</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n', '<table class=\"shop_attributes\">\r\n	<tbody>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Weight</th>\r\n			<td>0.15 lbs</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Dimensions</th>\r\n			<td>5.00 x 3.00 x 2.00 in</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Relay Type</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>Solid State AC, Solid State DC</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Number of Relays</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>1</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Max Relay Current Rating</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>3A</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Number Of GPIOs (Max)</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>4</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Analog Inputs</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>4(Multiplexed with IOs)</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Analog Input Resolution</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>10 Bits</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Communication</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>USB</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n	</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n', 1, 'Yes', '2018-02-14', '<p>Numato Lab`s Channel USB Solid State&nbsp;Relay Module is great for controlling your devices through USB without any USB protocol knowledge. This modules plugs in to your design seamlessly. Individual relay can be controlled by simple commands.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Features</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>1 on board Solid State Relay.</li>\r\n	<li>3A Maximum Switching Current.</li>\r\n	<li>4 TTL (3.3V)Compatible GPIOs.</li>\r\n	<li>4 Analog Input Channels (Multiplexed with GPIOs).</li>\r\n	<li>10 bits Analog Input Resolution.</li>\r\n	<li>USB interface with CDC support. As easy as using a serial port, no USB knowledge required.</li>\r\n	<li>Solid State Relay contacts available on easy to access screw terminals.</li>\r\n	<li>Can be controlled by using standard serial console applications or custom applications.</li>\r\n	<li>Can be powered from USB or external power supply.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;<img alt=\"Flag Icon USA\" class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-5328\" src=\"https://numato.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/10/us.png\" style=\"height:11px; width:16px\" />&nbsp;CO, USA Warehouse :&nbsp;In Stock, Shipping today!<br />\r\n&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;<img alt=\"Flag Icon India\" class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-5329\" src=\"https://numato.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/10/in.png\" style=\"height:11px; width:16px\" />&nbsp;BLR, India Warehouse:&nbsp;In Stock, Shipping today!</p>\r\n', 'SKU: SSRP2001', 49.99, 0, 0, 2, 7, 5, 2),
(98, 'Galatea Dual Port 100 BASE-T Ethernet Expansion', 89, 'Active', '								<p>Important! This product is designed for and compatible with <a href=\"https://numato.com/product/galatea-pci-express-spartan-6-fpga-development-board\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">Galatea PCI Express Spartan 6 FPGA Development Board</a>. The Galatea 100BASE-T Ethernet Expansion Module features LAN8710A, a low-power 10BASE-T/100BASE-TX physical layer (PHY) transceiver. LAN8710A supports communication with Ethernet MAC layer via standard MII (IEEE 802.3u) interface. LAN8710A full-duplex 10-BASE-T/100BASE-TX transceiver and supports 10Mbps (10BASE-T) and 100Mbps (100BASE-TX) operation. LAN8710A implements auto-negotiation to automatically determine the best possible speed and mode of operation. HP Auto-MDIX support allows the use of direct connect or cross-over LAN cables. This Expansion Module also has Microchip 24AA02E48 2Kbit EEPROM with built in unique MAC address. This MAC address can be read from the EEPROM and used for the Ethernet interface.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Features</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>2 High-Performance 10/100 Ethernet Transceiver</li>\r\n	<li>Single-Chip Ethernet Physical Layer Transceiver (PHY)</li>\r\n	<li>2 Kbit Electrically Erasable PROM (24AA02E48) with MAC Address</li>\r\n	<li>Dimensions: 56.61mm x 83.82mm</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Applications</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>Product Prototype Development</li>\r\n	<li>Network appliance development</li>\r\n	<li>Embedded Telecom Applications</li>\r\n	<li>Digital Media Adapters /Servers</li>\r\n	<li>Development and testing of custom Projects</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n', '								 <table class=\"shop_attributes\">\r\n	<tbody>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Weight</th>\r\n			<td>0.20 lbs</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Dimensions</th>\r\n			<td>5.00 x 3.00 x 2.00 in</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Number of Ethernet Ports</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>2</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Supported Speeds</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>100BASE-T, 10BASE-T</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Ethernet PHY</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>LAN8710A x 2</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Interface</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>MII</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>MAC Address</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>Yes</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>MAC Storage</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>External I2C EEPROM (24AA02E48)</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>External EEPROM Size</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>2Kbits</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n	</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n', 2, 'Yes', '2018-02-14', '								<p>Important! This product is designed for and compatible with <a href=\"https://numato.com/product/galatea-pci-express-spartan-6-fpga-development-board\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">Galatea PCI Express Spartan 6 FPGA Development Board</a>.  The Galatea 100BASE-T Ethernet Expansion Module features LAN8710A, a low-power 10BASE-T/100BASE-TX physical layer (PHY) transceiver. LAN8710A supports communication with Ethernet MAC layer via standard MII (IEEE 802.3u) interface. LAN8710A full-duplex 10-BASE-T/100BASE-TX transceiver and supports 10Mbps (10BASE-T) and 100Mbps (100BASE-TX) operation.<br />\r\n<strong>Features</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>2 High-Performance 10/100 Ethernet Transceiver</li>\r\n	<li>Single-Chip Ethernet Physical Layer Transceiver (PHY)</li>\r\n	<li>2 Kbit Electrically Erasable PROM (24AA02E48) with MAC Address</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Applications</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>Product Prototype Development</li>\r\n	<li>Network appliance development</li>\r\n	<li>Embedded Telecom Applications</li>\r\n	<li>Digital Media Adapters /Servers</li>\r\n	<li>Development and testing of custom Projects</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n', 'SKU: GTETH1002001', 50.99, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0),
(99, 'Galatea RTL8211E Gigabit Ethernet Expansion Module', 89, 'Active', '								<p>Important! This product is designed for and compatible with <a href=\"https://numato.com/product/galatea-pci-express-spartan-6-fpga-development-board\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">Galatea PCI Express Spartan 6 FPGA Development Board</a>. The heart of the RTL8211E Gigabit Ethernet Expansion module is RTL8211E-VB, a highly integrated Ethernet transceiver that comply with 10BASE-T, 100BASE-TX and 1000Base-T IEEE 802.3 standards. RTL8211E-VB supports communication with Ethernet MAC layer via standard RGMII interface, thus providing an alternative to the IEEE802.3z GMII interface. The main objective in using RGMII interface over GMII interface is to reduce the number of IOs to half for interconnecting MAC and PHY. RTL8211E-VB implements auto-negotiation to automatically determine the best possible speed and mode of operation. HP Auto-MDIX support allows the use of direct connect or cross-over LAN cables. RTL8211E Gigabit Ethernet Expansion Module also has Microchip 24AA02E48 2Kbit EEPROM with built in unique MAC address. This MAC address can be read from the EEPROM and used for the Ethernet interface.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Features</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>High-Performance 10/100/1000 Ethernet Transceiver</li>\r\n	<li>Single-Chip Ethernet Physical Layer Transceiver (PHY)</li>\r\n	<li>2 Kbit Electrically Erasable PROM (24AA02E48) with MAC Address</li>\r\n	<li>Dimension: 57.075mm X 83.8mm</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Applications</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>Product Prototype Development</li>\r\n	<li>Network appliance development</li>\r\n	<li>Embedded Telecom Applications</li>\r\n	<li>Digital Media Adapters /Servers</li>\r\n	<li>Development and testing of custom Projects</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n', '								 <table class=\"shop_attributes\">\r\n	<tbody>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Weight</th>\r\n			<td>0.20 lbs</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Dimensions</th>\r\n			<td>5.00 x 3.00 x 2.00 in</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Number of Ethernet Ports</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>1</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Supported Speeds</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>1000BASE-T, 100BASE-T, 10BASE-T</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Ethernet PHY</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>RTL8211E</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Interface</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>GMII</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>MAC Address</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>Yes</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>MAC Storage</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>External I2C EEPROM (24AA02E48 )</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>External EEPROM Size</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>2Kbits</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n	</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n', 3, 'Yes', '2018-02-14', '<p>Important!&nbsp;This product is designed for and compatible with&nbsp;<a href=\"https://numato.com/product/galatea-pci-express-spartan-6-fpga-development-board\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">Galatea PCI Express Spartan 6 FPGA Development Board</a>. &nbsp;The heart of the RTL8211E Gigabit Ethernet Expansion module is RTL8211E-VB, a highly integrated Ethernet transceiver that comply with 10BASE-T, 100BASE-TX and 1000Base-T IEEE 802.3 standards.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Features</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>High-Performance 10/100/1000 Ethernet Transceiver</li>\r\n	<li>Single-Chip Ethernet Physical Layer Transceiver (PHY)</li>\r\n	<li>2 Kbit Electrically Erasable PROM (24AA02E48) with MAC Address</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Applications</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>Product Prototype Development</li>\r\n	<li>Audio Record/Playback Systems</li>\r\n	<li>Media players</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n', 'SKU: GTETH1G001', 62.99, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0),
(100, 'RTL8211E Gigabit Ethernet Expansion Module', 89, 'Active', '								<p>The heart of the RTL8211E Gigabit Ethernet Expansion module is RTL8211E-VB, a highly integrated Ethernet transceiver from Realtek that comply with 10BASE-T, 100BASE-TX and 1000Base-T IEEE 802.3 standards. RTL8211E-VB supports communication with Ethernet MAC layer via standard RGMII interface. The main objective in using RGMII interface over GMII interface is to reduce the number of IOs to half for interconnecting MAC and PHY. RTL8211E-VB implements auto-negotiation to automatically determine the best possible speed and mode of operation. HP Auto-MDIX support allows the use of direct connect or cross-over LAN cables. RTL8211E Gigabit Ethernet Expansion Module also has Microchip 24AA02E48 2Kbit EEPROM with built in unique MAC address. This MAC address can be read from the EEPROM and used for the Ethernet interface.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Features</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>Three 2×6 pin Expansion connectors</li>\r\n	<li>High-Performance 10/100/1000 T Ethernet Transceiver</li>\r\n	<li>Single-Chip Ethernet Physical Layer Transceiver (PHY)</li>\r\n	<li>2 Kbit Electrically Erasable PROM (24AA02E48) with MAC Address</li>\r\n	<li>Dimension: 61.5mm X 61.5mm</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Applications</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>Product Prototype Development</li>\r\n	<li>Network appliance development</li>\r\n	<li>Embedded Telecom Applications</li>\r\n	<li>Digital Media Adapters /Servers</li>\r\n	<li>Development and testing of custom Projects</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n', '								 <table class=\"shop_attributes\">\r\n	<tbody>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Weight</th>\r\n			<td>0.15 lbs</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Dimensions</th>\r\n			<td>5.00 x 3.00 x 2.00 in</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Number of Ethernet Ports</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>1</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Supported Speeds</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>1000BASE-T, 100BASE-T, 10BASE-T</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Ethernet PHY</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>RTL8211E</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Interface</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>GMII</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>MAC Address</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>Yes</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>MAC Storage</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>External I2C EEPROM (24AA02E48)</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>External EEPROM Size</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>2Kbits</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n	</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n', 4, 'Yes', '2018-02-14', '								<p>The heart of the RTL8211E Gigabit Ethernet Expansion module is RTL8211E-VB, a highly integrated Ethernet transceiver from Realtek that comply with 10BASE-T, 100BASE-TX and 1000Base-T IEEE 802.3 standards. RTL8211E-VB supports communication with Ethernet MAC layer via standard RGMII interface.<br />\r\n<strong>Features</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>Three 2×6 pin Expansion connectors</li>\r\n	<li>High-Performance 10/100/1000 T Ethernet Transceiver</li>\r\n	<li>Single-Chip Ethernet Physical Layer Transceiver (PHY)</li>\r\n	<li>2 Kbit Electrically Erasable PROM (24AA02E48) with MAC Address</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Applications</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>Product Prototype Development</li>\r\n	<li>Network appliance development</li>\r\n	<li>Embedded Telecom Applications</li>\r\n	<li>Digital Media Adapters /Servers</li>\r\n	<li>Development and testing of custom Projects</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n', 'SKU: ETHEXPGB001', 50.99, 0, 0, 1, 17, 12, 5),
(101, 'Galatea IO Expansion Module', 90, 'Active', '								<p>Important! This product is designed for and compatible with <a href=\"https://numato.com/product/galatea-pci-express-spartan-6-fpga-development-board\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">Galatea PCI Express Spartan 6 FPGA Development Board</a>. This board is an IO breakout solution for Galatea PCI Express Spartan 6 FPGA Development Board. This product allows Galatea’s IOs to be broken out in to smaller 2×6 headers that would facilitate easy attachment of other peripheral expansion modules. The board features seven 2×6 expansion connector. Please note that the external power connector on Galatea PCI Express FPGA Development Board will not be accessible when this module is placed the high speed IO connector P5.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Features</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>7 (2×6)Expansion connectors</li>\r\n	<li>On board 1.5V to 3.3V Converter</li>\r\n	<li>56 IOs</li>\r\n	<li>Can be attached to either side of Galatea FPGA board</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n', '								 <table class=\"shop_attributes\">\r\n	<tbody>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Weight</th>\r\n			<td>0.10 lbs</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Dimensions</th>\r\n			<td>5.00 x 3.00 x 2.00 in</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Number of Expansion Connectors</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>7</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Number of IOs (Max)</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>56</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Onboard 1.5V to 3.3V Converter</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>Yes (TXB0108)</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n	</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n', 1, 'Yes', '2018-02-14', '								<p>Important! This product is designed for and compatible with <a href=\"https://numato.com/product/galatea-pci-express-spartan-6-fpga-development-board\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">Galatea PCI Express Spartan 6 FPGA Development Board</a>. This board is an IO breakout solution for Galatea PCI Express Spartan 6 FPGA Development Board. This product allows Galatea’s IOs to be broken out in to smaller 2×6 headers that would facilitate easy attachment of other peripheral expansion modules. The board features seven 2×6 expansion connector. Please note that the external power connector on Galatea PCI Express FPGA Development Board will not be accessible when this module is placed the high speed IO connector P5.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Features</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>7 (2×6)Expansion connectors</li>\r\n	<li>On board 1.5V to 3.3V Converter</li>\r\n	<li>56 IOs</li>\r\n	<li>Can be attached to either side of Galatea FPGA board</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n', 'SKU: GAIO001', 37.99, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0),
(102, 'Galatea SMA IO Interconnect Module', 90, 'Active', '								<p>Important! This product is designed for and compatible with <a href=\"https://numato.com/product/galatea-pci-express-spartan-6-fpga-development-board\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">Galatea PCI Express Spartan 6 FPGA Development Board</a>. Galatea SMA IO Interconnect Module is a SMA breakout solution for Galatea Spartan 6 PCI Express FPGA Board. This product allows Galatea’s IOs and GTP to be broken out in to SMA connectors that would facilitate easy attachment of other high speed peripherals. The board features 18 SMA connectors, which include one set of GTP transceiver and 12 IOs. (CLK, RX & TX pairs for GTP is available only when the module is placed on header P4 in galatea Spartan 6 PCIe Board).</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Features</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>18 SMA connectors</li>\r\n	<li>6 SMA connectors for GTP transceivers</li>\r\n	<li>Can be attached to either side of Galatea FPGA board</li>\r\n	<li>Dimension: 83.820mm X 56.591mm</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n', '								 <table class=\"shop_attributes\">\r\n	<tbody>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Weight</th>\r\n			<td>0.3 lbs</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Dimensions</th>\r\n			<td>5 x 3 x 2 in</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Number of SMA connectors:</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>18</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Number of IOs</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>12</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Number of GTPs</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>1 (Available only when placed on P4)</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n	</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n', 2, 'Yes', '2018-02-14', '								<p>Important! This product is designed for and compatible with <a href=\"https://numato.com/product/galatea-pci-express-spartan-6-fpga-development-board\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">Galatea PCI Express Spartan 6 FPGA Development Board</a>. Galatea SMA IO Interconnect Module is a SMA breakout solution for Galatea Spartan 6 PCI Express FPGA Board. This product allows Galatea’s IOs and GTP to be broken out in to SMA connectors that would facilitate easy attachment of other high speed peripherals.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Features</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>18 SMA connectors</li>\r\n	<li>6 SMA connectors for GTP transceivers when placed on header P4 on Galatea</li>\r\n	<li>Can be attached to either side of Galatea FPGA board</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n', 'SKU: GAIO002', 74.99, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0),
(103, 'IO Breakout Module for Mimas', 90, 'Active', '								<p>This board is an IO breakout solution for Mimas Spartan 6 development board. This product allows Mimas IOs to be broken out in to smaller 2×6 headers that would facilitate easy attachment of other peripheral expansion modules. The board features four 2×6 expansion connector.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Features</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>Four 2×6 pin expansion connectors</li>\r\n	<li>Can be attached to either side of Mimas</li>\r\n	<li>Dimension: 34.3mm X 88.1mm</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n', '								 <table class=\"shop_attributes\">\r\n	<tbody>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Weight</th>\r\n			<td>0.10 lbs</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Dimensions</th>\r\n			<td>5.00 x 3.00 x 2.00 in</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n	</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n', 3, 'Yes', '2018-02-14', '								<p>This board is an IO breakout solution for Mimas Sparta6 development board. This product allows Mimas IOs to be broken out in to smaller 2×6 headers that would facilitate easy attachment of other peripheral expansion modules. The board features four 2×6 expansion connector.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Features</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>Four 2×6 pin expansion connectors</li>\r\n	<li>Can be attached to either side of Mimas</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n', 'SKU: EXPIOBRK001', 6.99, 0, 0, 0, 6, 6, 0),
(104, 'IO Breakout Module for Saturn', 90, 'Active', '<p>This board is an IO breakout solution for Saturn Spartan 6 development board. This product allows&nbsp;Saturn IOs to be broken out in to smaller 2&times;6 headers that would facilitate easy attachment of other&nbsp;peripheral expansion modules. The board&nbsp;features four 2&times;6 expansion connector. The traces are length matched. Please see the documentation for complete length matching details.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Features</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>Four 2&times;6 pin expansion connector</li>\r\n	<li>Can be attached to either side of Saturn</li>\r\n	<li>Dimension: 34.3mm X 88.1mm</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n', '<table class=\"shop_attributes\">\r\n	<tbody>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Weight</th>\r\n			<td>0.16 lbs</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Dimensions</th>\r\n			<td>5.00 x 3.00 x 2.00 in</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>IO Pairs Length Matched</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>Yes</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n	</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n', 4, 'Yes', '2018-02-14', '<p>This board is an IO breakout solution for Saturn Sparta6 development board. This product allows&nbsp;Saturn IOs to be broken out in to smaller 2&times;6 headers that would facilitate easy attachment of other&nbsp;peripheral expansion modules. The board&nbsp;features four 2&times;6 expansion connector. The traces are length matched. Please see the documentation for complete length matching details.<br />\r\n<strong>Features</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>4 (2&times;6)Expansion connectors</li>\r\n	<li>Can be attached to either side of Saturn</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n', 'SKU: EXPIOBRK0020', 12.99, 0, 0, 0, 10, 10, 0),
(107, 'Galatea IP4776CZ38 HDMI Expansion Module', 91, 'Active', '<p>Important!&nbsp;This product is designed for and compatible with&nbsp;<a href=\"https://numato.com/product/galatea-pci-express-spartan-6-fpga-development-board\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">Galatea PCI Express Spartan 6 FPGA Development Board</a>.&nbsp;Galatea IP4776CZ38 HDMI Module features two buffered DVI-D interface with HDMI buffer IP4776CZ38 for better signal strength and signal integrity. The on board DVI-D interface can be used to transmit high quality HD video. This module is designed to be used with Numato Lab&rsquo;s Galatea PCI Express Spartan 6 FPGA Development Board.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Features</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>DVI-D/HDMI Connector</li>\r\n	<li>IP4776CZ38 HDMI Buffer</li>\r\n	<li>Dimension: 57.075mm X 83.80mm</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Applications</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>Product prototyping</li>\r\n	<li>Gaming consoles</li>\r\n	<li>Audio/Video playback devices</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n', '<table class=\"shop_attributes\">\r\n	<tbody>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Weight</th>\r\n			<td>0.10 lbs</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Dimensions</th>\r\n			<td>5.00 x 3.00 x 2.00 in</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>HDMI Inputs</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>1</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>HDMI Outputs</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>1</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n	</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n', 2, 'Yes', '2018-02-14', '<p>Important!&nbsp;This product is designed for and compatible with&nbsp;<a href=\"https://numato.com/product/galatea-pci-express-spartan-6-fpga-development-board\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">Galatea PCI Express Spartan 6 FPGA Development Board</a>.&nbsp;Galatea IP4776CZ38 HDMI Module features two buffered DVI-D interface with HDMI buffer IP4776CZ38 for better signal strength and signal integrity.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Features</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>DVI-D/HDMI Connector</li>\r\n	<li>IP4776CZ38 HDMI Buffer</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Applications</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>Product prototyping</li>\r\n	<li>Gaming consoles</li>\r\n	<li>Audio/Video playback devices</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n', 'SKU: GAHDMI20001', 62.99, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0),
(109, 'VGA Display Expansion Module', 91, 'Active', '<p>Numato Lab&rsquo;s VGA display module provides an easy and cost effective way to add VGA display to your&nbsp;custom project using a 12pin connector. It is designed to be used with Numato Lab&rsquo;s FPGA boards&nbsp;featuring a 2&times;6 pin Expansion connector (Boards without 2&times;6 &nbsp;expansion Connector may need IO&nbsp;breakout modules or manual wiring).</p>\r\n', '<table class=\"shop_attributes\">\r\n	<tbody>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Weight</th>\r\n			<td>0.10 lbs</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Dimensions</th>\r\n			<td>5.00 x 3.00 x 2.00 in</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Video Out</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>VGA</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n	</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n', 4, 'Yes', '2018-02-14', '<p>Numato Lab&rsquo;s VGA display module provides an easy and cost effective way to add VGA display to your custom project using a 12pin connector. It is designed to be used with Numato Lab&rsquo;s FPGA boards featuring a 2&times;6 pin Expansion connector (Boards without 2&times;6 expansion Connector may need IO breakout modules or manual wiring).</p>\r\n', 'SKU: EXPVGA001', 19.99, 0, 0, 0, 1, 1, 0),
(111, '2 Channel Solid State Relay Controller Board', 77, 'Active', '<p>Numato 2 Channel Solid State Relay breakout module is a smart choice for controlling higher current loads from your microcontroller development board, PC parallel port or your favorite Arduino. This board has two on-board Solid State Relays which can switch up to 3A. All relay terminals are accessible through screw terminals which makes wiring up the board very easy. The relays are driven by popular darlington array ULN2003. This product is available for purchase with AC or DC Solid State Relays.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Features</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>Very compact and easy to wire up</li>\r\n	<li>1.6mm FR4 PCB with black solder mask and white silk screen</li>\r\n	<li>Connects directly to TTL devices (Microcontrollers, Arduino etc..)</li>\r\n	<li>Two Solid State Relays with&nbsp;one two pin screw terminals for easy connectivity</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Applications</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>Home Automation</li>\r\n	<li>Industrial Automation</li>\r\n	<li>Lighting Control</li>\r\n	<li>Garden Equipment Control</li>\r\n	<li>Test Fixtures</li>\r\n	<li>DIY and Hobby</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n', '<table class=\"shop_attributes\">\r\n	<tbody>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Weight</th>\r\n			<td>0.20 lbs</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Dimensions</th>\r\n			<td>5.00 x 3.00 x 2.00 in</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Relay Type</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>Solid State AC, Solid State DC</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Number of Relays</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>2</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Max Relay Current Rating</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>3A</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Relay driver</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>ULN2003</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n	</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n', 2, 'Yes', '2018-02-14', '<p>Numato 2 Channel Solid State Relay breakout module is a smart choice for controlling higher current loads from your microcontroller development board, PC parallel port or your favorite Arduino. This board has two on-board Solid State Relays which can switch up to 3A. All relay terminals are accessible through screw terminals which makes wiring up the board very easy. The relays are driven by popular darlington array ULN2003. This product is available for purchase with AC or DC Solid State Relays.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Features</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>2 on board Solid State Relays .</li>\r\n	<li>3A Maximum Switching Current.</li>\r\n	<li>ULN2003 Relay Driver.</li>\r\n	<li>Very compact and easy to wire up</li>\r\n	<li>LED indication for Power and individual relay status.</li>\r\n	<li>Connects directly to TTL devices (Microcontrollers, Arduino etc..).</li>\r\n	<li>Fuses are provided for over current protection for each relay.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n', 'SKU: SSRC20001', 56.99, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0),
(113, '2 Channel Solid State Relay Controller Board', 77, 'Active', '<p>Numato 2 Channel Solid State Relay breakout module is a smart choice for controlling higher current loads from your microcontroller development board, PC parallel port or your favorite Arduino. This board has two on-board Solid State Relays which can switch up to 3A. All relay terminals are accessible through screw terminals which makes wiring up the board very easy. The relays are driven by popular darlington array ULN2003. This product is available for purchase with AC or DC Solid State Relays.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Features</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>Very compact and easy to wire up</li>\r\n	<li>1.6mm FR4 PCB with black solder mask and white silk screen</li>\r\n	<li>Connects directly to TTL devices (Microcontrollers, Arduino etc..)</li>\r\n	<li>Two Solid State Relays with&nbsp;one two pin screw terminals for easy connectivity</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Applications</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>Home Automation</li>\r\n	<li>Industrial Automation</li>\r\n	<li>Lighting Control</li>\r\n	<li>Garden Equipment Control</li>\r\n	<li>Test Fixtures</li>\r\n	<li>DIY and Hobby</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n', '<table class=\"shop_attributes\">\r\n	<tbody>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Weight</th>\r\n			<td>0.20 lbs</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Dimensions</th>\r\n			<td>5.00 x 3.00 x 2.00 in</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Relay Type</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>Solid State AC, Solid State DC</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Number of Relays</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>2</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Max Relay Current Rating</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>3A</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Relay driver</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>ULN2003</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n	</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n', 4, 'Yes', '2018-02-14', '<p>Numato 2 Channel Solid State Relay breakout module is a smart choice for controlling higher current loads from your microcontroller development board, PC parallel port or your favorite Arduino. This board has two on-board Solid State Relays which can switch up to 3A. All relay terminals are accessible through screw terminals which makes wiring up the board very easy. The relays are driven by popular darlington array ULN2003. This product is available for purchase with AC or DC Solid State Relays.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Features</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>2 on board Solid State Relays .</li>\r\n	<li>3A Maximum Switching Current.</li>\r\n	<li>ULN2003 Relay Driver.</li>\r\n	<li>Very compact and easy to wire up</li>\r\n	<li>LED indication for Power and individual relay status.</li>\r\n	<li>Connects directly to TTL devices (Microcontrollers, Arduino etc..).</li>\r\n	<li>Fuses are provided for over current protection for each relay.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n', 'SKU: SSRC20001', 44.95, 0, 0, 0, 3, 3, 0),
(116, '8 Channel Ethernet Solid State Relay Module', 77, 'Active', '								<p>Numato Lab 8 Channel Ethernet Solid State Relay module allows controlling electrical devices remotely through Ethernet. This is very helpful in those situations where the device that needs to be controlled is located far from the PC and thus can not run USB cable. Numato Lab Ethernet Solid State Relay modules are designed to be very easy to setup and use.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>This product has 8 on board Solid State Relays and 10 GPIOs. Each relay/gpio can be individually controlled through the built in easy to use web interface or through any popular terminal emulator that supports TELNET protocol. Each 8 Channel Ethernet Solid State Relay module is shipped with unique MAC address. These devices also supports assigning and retrieving custom identification string that can be used for identifying individual devices when there are large number of devices connected on the same network. All relay terminals are available on screw terminals which makes connecting external devices very easy.<br />\r\n<strong>Features</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>8 on board Solid State Relays with individual LEDs for status.</li>\r\n	<li>3A Maximum Switching Current.</li>\r\n	<li>10 TTL (3.3V)Compatible GPIOs.</li>\r\n	<li>10 Analog Input Channels (Multiplexed with GPIOs).</li>\r\n	<li>10 bits Analog Input Resolution.</li>\r\n	<li>Password protected Web console and Telnet communication interface.</li>\r\n	<li>LED indication for Power and individual relay status.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Applications</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>Home Automation</li>\r\n	<li>Industrial Automation</li>\r\n	<li>Lighting Control</li>\r\n	<li>Garden Equipment Control</li>\r\n	<li>Test Fixtures</li>\r\n	<li>DIY and Hobby</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n', '								 <table class=\"shop_attributes\">\r\n	<tbody>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Weight</th>\r\n			<td>0.60 lbs</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Dimensions</th>\r\n			<td>10.00 x 5.00 x 2.00 in</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Relay Type</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>Solid State AC, Solid State DC</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Max Relay Current Rating</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>3A</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Number Of GPIOs (Max)</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>10</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Analog Inputs</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>10</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Analog Input Resolution</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>10 Bits</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Host Interface</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>Ethernet</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>User Interface</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p><a href=\"https://numato.com/user-interface/htmlweb\" rel=\"tag\">HTML/Web</a>, <a href=\"https://numato.com/user-interface/telnet\" rel=\"tag\">TELNET</a></p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Number of Relays</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>8</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n	</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n', 7, 'Yes', '2018-02-15', '								<div class=\"woocommerce-product-details__short-description\">\r\n<p>Numato Lab 8 Channel Ethernet Solid State Relay module allows controlling electrical devices remotely through Ethernet. This is very helpful in those situations where the device that needs to be controlled is located far from the PC and thus can not run USB cable. Numato Lab Ethernet Solid State Relay modules are designed to be very easy to setup and use.<br />\r\n<strong>Features</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>8 on board Solid State Relays with individual LEDs for status.</li>\r\n	<li>3A Maximum Switching Current.</li>\r\n	<li>10 TTL (3.3V)Compatible GPIOs.</li>\r\n	<li>10 Analog Input Channels (Multiplexed with GPIOs).</li>\r\n	<li>10 bits Analog Input Resolution.</li>\r\n	<li>Password protected Web console and Telnet communication interface.</li>\r\n	<li>LED indication for Power and individual relay status.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Applications</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>Home Automation</li>\r\n	<li>Industrial Automation</li>\r\n	<li>Lighting Control</li>\r\n	<li>Test Fixtures</li>\r\n	<li>DIY and Hobby</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</div>\r\n', 'SKU: 8ETHSSR001', 186.95, 0, 0, 0, 6, 6, 0),
(117, '8 Channel Solid State Relay Controller Board', 77, 'Active', '<p>Numato 8 Channel Solid State Relay breakout module is a smart choice for controlling higher current loads from your microcontroller development board, PC parallel port or your favorite Arduino. This board has eight on-board Solid State Relays which can switch up to 3A. All relay terminals are accessible through screw terminals which makes wiring up the board very easy. The relays are driven by popular darlington array ULN2003. This product is available for purchase with AC or DC Solid State Relays.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Features</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>Very compact and easy to wire up</li>\r\n	<li>1.6mm FR4 PCB with black solder mask and white silk screen</li>\r\n	<li>Connects directly to TTL devices (Microcontrollers, Arduino etc..)</li>\r\n	<li>Four Solid State Relays with&nbsp;one two pin screw terminals for easy connectivity</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Applications</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>Home Automation</li>\r\n	<li>Industrial Automation</li>\r\n	<li>Lighting Control</li>\r\n	<li>Garden Equipment Control</li>\r\n	<li>Test Fixtures</li>\r\n	<li>DIY and Hobby</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n', '<table class=\"shop_attributes\">\r\n	<tbody>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Weight</th>\r\n			<td>0.35 lbs</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Dimensions</th>\r\n			<td>10.00 x 5.00 x 2.00 in</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Relay Type</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>Solid State AC, Solid State DC</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Number of Relays</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>8</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Max Relay Current Rating</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>3A</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Relay Driver</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>ULN2803</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n	</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n', 8, 'Yes', '2018-02-15', '<p>Numato 8 Channel Solid State Relay breakout module is a smart choice for controlling higher current loads from your microcontroller development board, PC parallel port or your favorite Arduino. This board has eight on-board Solid State Relays which can switch up to 3A.<br />\r\n<strong>Features</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>8 on board Solid State Relays .</li>\r\n	<li>3A Maximum Switching Current.</li>\r\n	<li>ULN2003 Relay Driver.</li>\r\n	<li>LED indication for Power and individual relay status.</li>\r\n	<li>Connects directly to TTL devices (Microcontrollers, Arduino etc..).</li>\r\n	<li>Fuses are provided for over current protection for each relay.</li>\r\n	<li>Very compact and easy to wire up</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Applications</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>Home Automation</li>\r\n	<li>Industrial Automation</li>\r\n	<li>Lighting Control</li>\r\n	<li>Garden Equipment Control</li>\r\n	<li>Test Fixtures</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n', 'SKU: SSRC80001', 112.99, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0),
(118, '8 Channel USB Solid State Relay Module', 73, 'Active', '<p>Numato Lab`s 8 Channel USB Solid State&nbsp;Relay Module is great for controlling your devices through USB without any USB protocol knowledge. This modules plugs in to your design seamlessly. Individual relay can be controlled by simple commands. This product has eight on board Solid State&nbsp;&nbsp;Relays that can switch up to 3A load.The relays are controlled by USB capable Microchip PIC Microcontroller (PIC18F14K50) and comes with built in firmware that supports simple commands to control relays and read relay status. The board, when attached to a PC/Laptop shows up as a serial port and all you need to control the board is a serial terminal application like HyperTerminal or Putty. This board can easily be controlled by writing simple serial port application in VC++, VB, VBA (Word, Excel etc), Perl, Python etc.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Features</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>8 on board Solid State Relays.</li>\r\n	<li>3A Maximum Switching Current.</li>\r\n	<li>USB interface with CDC support. As easy as using a serial port, no USB knowledge required.</li>\r\n	<li>Relay contacts available on easy to access screw terminals.</li>\r\n	<li>Digital circuitry can be powered from USB or external power supply.</li>\r\n	<li>Can be controlled by using standard serial console applications or custom applications.</li>\r\n	<li>No vendor specific libraries or APIs required.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Applications</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>Home Automation</li>\r\n	<li>Industrial Automation</li>\r\n	<li>Lighting Control</li>\r\n	<li>Garden Equipment Control</li>\r\n	<li>Test Fixtures</li>\r\n	<li>DIY and Hobby</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Supporting operating Systems</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>Windows XP</li>\r\n	<li>Windows 7</li>\r\n	<li>Windows 8/8.1</li>\r\n	<li>Windows 10</li>\r\n	<li>Linux</li>\r\n	<li>Mac OS X</li>\r\n	<li>Android</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n', '<table class=\"shop_attributes\">\r\n	<tbody>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Weight</th>\r\n			<td>0.60 lbs</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Dimensions</th>\r\n			<td>10.00 x 5.00 x 2.00 in</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Relay Type</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>Solid State AC, Solid State DC</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Number of Relays</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>8</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Max Relay Current Rating</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>3A</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Communication</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>USB</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n	</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n', 9, 'Yes', '2018-02-15', '<p>Numato Lab`s 8 Channel USB Solid State&nbsp;Relay Module is great for controlling your devices through USB without any USB protocol knowledge. This modules plugs in to your design seamlessly. Individual relay can be controlled by simple commands.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Features</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>8 on board Solid State Relays.</li>\r\n	<li>3A Maximum Switching Current.</li>\r\n	<li>USB interface with CDC support. As easy as using a serial port, no USB knowledge required.</li>\r\n	<li>Relay contacts available on easy to access screw terminals.</li>\r\n	<li>Digital circuitry can be powered from USB or external power supply.</li>\r\n	<li>Can be controlled by using standard serial console applications or custom applications.</li>\r\n	<li>No vendor specific libraries or APIs required.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Applications</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>Home Automation</li>\r\n	<li>Industrial Automation</li>\r\n	<li>Lighting Control</li>\r\n	<li>Garden Equipment Control</li>\r\n	<li>Test Fixtures</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n', 'SKU: SSR80001', 149.95, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1, -1);
INSERT INTO `tbl_product` (`product_id`, `product_name`, `product_category_id`, `product_status`, `product_description`, `product_specification`, `priorty`, `display_flag`, `product_entry_date`, `product_details`, `product_code`, `product_amt`, `product_tax`, `product_discount`, `product_threshold`, `total_product`, `total_sold`, `total_remaining`) VALUES
(119, '8 Channel USB Relay Module -12V ', 73, 'Active', '<p>URMC8 8 Channel USB Relay Module is great for controlling your devices through USB without any USB protocol knowledge. This modules plugs in to your design seamless. Individual relay can be controlled by simple commands. Numato&rsquo;s URMC8 8 Channel USB Relay Module provides exceptional value for money.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>It has eight on board 12V SPDT relays that can switch up to 10A load.The relays are controlled by USB capable Microchip PIC Microcontroller (PIC18F14K50) and comes with built in firmware that supports simple commands to control relays and read relay status. The board, when attached to a PC/Laptop shows up as a serial port and all you need to control the board is a serial terminal application like HyperTerminal or Putty.<br />\r\n<strong>Features</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>8 on board 12V SPDT Relays.</li>\r\n	<li>7A Maximum Switching Current.</li>\r\n	<li>USB interface with CDC support. As easy as using a serial port, no USB knowledge required.</li>\r\n	<li>Relay contacts available on easy to access screw terminals.</li>\r\n	<li>Digital circuitry can be powered from USB or external power supply.</li>\r\n	<li>Can be controlled by using standard serial console applications or custom applications.</li>\r\n	<li>No vendor specific libraries or APIs required.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Applications</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>Home Automation</li>\r\n	<li>Industrial Automation</li>\r\n	<li>Lighting Control</li>\r\n	<li>Garden Equipment Control</li>\r\n	<li>Test Fixtures</li>\r\n	<li>DIY and Hobby</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Supporting Operating Systems</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>Windows XP and later</li>\r\n	<li>Windows 7 Embedded and later</li>\r\n	<li>Linux</li>\r\n	<li>Mac OS X</li>\r\n	<li>Android</li>\r\n	<li>or any other operating system that supports USB CDC devices.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Languages that can be used for programming</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>C/C++</li>\r\n	<li>Visual Basic (VB6, VB2008, VB2010 express and other editions)</li>\r\n	<li>Visual Basic for Applications (Microsoft Office VBA)</li>\r\n	<li>Perl</li>\r\n	<li>Python</li>\r\n	<li>JAVA</li>\r\n	<li>Android</li>\r\n	<li>Javascript(Node.js)</li>\r\n	<li>And many more&hellip;</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n', '<table class=\"shop_attributes\">\r\n	<tbody>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Weight</th>\r\n			<td>0.31 lbs /140 grams</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Dimensions</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>LxWxH=10&nbsp; cm x 8 cm x 0.2 cm</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Number Of Relays</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>8</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Relay Type</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p><a href=\"https://numato.com/relay-type/mechanical\" rel=\"tag\">Mechanical</a></p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Relay Coil Voltage / Max Relay Current Rating</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>12V/10A</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Communication</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>USB</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n	</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n', 1, 'Yes', '2018-04-24', '<p>URMC8 8 Channel USB Relay Module is great for controlling your devices through USB without any USB protocol knowledge. This modules plugs in to your design seamless. Individual relay can be controlled by simple commands.<br />\r\n<strong>Features</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>8 on board 12V SPDT Relays.</li>\r\n	<li>7A Maximum Switching Current.</li>\r\n	<li>USB interface with CDC support. As easy as using a serial port, no USB knowledge required.</li>\r\n	<li>Relay contacts available on easy to access screw terminals.</li>\r\n	<li>Digital circuitry can be powered from USB or external power supply.</li>\r\n	<li>Can be controlled by using standard serial console applications or custom applications.</li>\r\n	<li>No vendor specific libraries or APIs required.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Applications</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>Home Automation</li>\r\n	<li>Industrial Automation</li>\r\n	<li>Lighting Control</li>\r\n	<li>Garden Equipment Control</li>\r\n	<li>Test Fixtures</li>\r\n	<li>DIY and Hobby</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n', 'RL80001-12V', 69.95, 0, 0, 5, 124, 119, 5),
(120, '64 Channel USB Relay Module', 73, 'Active', '<p>Numato Lab&rsquo;s 64 Channel USB Relay Module is a versatile product for controlling electrical and electronic devices remotely from a PC over USB link. Ease of use and wider operating system compatibility are the primary goals behind this product&rsquo;s design.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><br />\r\n<strong>Applications</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>Home Automation</li>\r\n	<li>Industrial Automation</li>\r\n	<li>Lighting Control</li>\r\n	<li>Garden Equipment Control</li>\r\n	<li>Test Fixtures</li>\r\n	<li>DIY and Hobby</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n', '<table border=\"1\" cellspacing=\"0\" style=\"border-collapse:collapse; height:441px; width:100%\">\r\n	<tbody>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<td style=\"height:49px; width:50%\">Weight</td>\r\n			<td style=\"height:49px; width:50%\">4.50 lbs</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<td style=\"height:49px; width:50%\">Dimensions</td>\r\n			<td style=\"height:49px; width:50%\">22 x 12 x 2 in</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<td style=\"height:49px; width:50%\">Number Of Relays&nbsp;</td>\r\n			<td style=\"height:49px; width:50%\">64</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<td style=\"height:49px; width:50%\">Relay Type</td>\r\n			<td style=\"height:49px; width:50%\"><a href=\"https://numato.com/relay-type/mechanical\" rel=\"tag\">Mechanical</a></td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<td style=\"height:49px; width:50%\">Max Relay Current Rating&nbsp;</td>\r\n			<td style=\"height:49px; width:50%\">10A</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<td style=\"height:49px; width:50%\">Number Of GPIOs (Max)</td>\r\n			<td style=\"height:49px; width:50%\">8</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<td style=\"height:49px; width:50%\">Analog Inputs</td>\r\n			<td style=\"height:49px; width:50%\">6(Multiplexed with IOs)</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<td style=\"height:49px; width:50%\">Analog Input Resolution&nbsp;</td>\r\n			<td style=\"height:49px; width:50%\">10 Bits</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<td style=\"height:49px; width:50%\">Communication&nbsp;</td>\r\n			<td style=\"height:49px; width:50%\">USB</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n	</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n', 3, 'Yes', '2018-08-21', '<p>Numato Lab&rsquo;s 64 Channel USB Relay Module is a versatile product for controlling electrical and electronic devices remotely from a PC over USB link. Ease of use and wider operating system compatibility are the primary goals behind this product&rsquo;s design.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><br />\r\n<strong>Applications</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>Home Automation</li>\r\n	<li>Industrial Automation</li>\r\n	<li>Lighting Control</li>\r\n	<li>Garden Equipment Control</li>\r\n	<li>Test Fixtures</li>\r\n	<li>DIY and Hobby</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n', 'RL640001', 496.99, 0, 0, 0, 5, 8, -3),
(121, 'Micro SD Expansion Module', 90, 'Active', '<h2>Description</h2>\r\n\r\n<p>Micro SD Expansion Module provides an easy and convenient way to interface Micro SD card to&nbsp;Numato Lab&rsquo;s FPGA/Microcontroller boards. It can be connected to any FPGA/Microcontroller board&nbsp;featuring 2&times;6 pin Expansion connector. This module can be manually wired to FPGA/Microcontroller&nbsp;boards that does not have 2&times;6 expansion header.This product is compatible with most of&nbsp;Numato Lab&rsquo;s FPGA boards.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Features</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>Micro SD card slot</li>\r\n	<li>2&times;6 pin expansion connector</li>\r\n	<li>Dimension: 19mm X 38mm</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Applications</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>Product Prototype Development</li>\r\n	<li>Development and testing of custom Projects</li>\r\n	<li>Audio playback device development</li>\r\n	<li>Data logging</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n', '<table border=\"1\" cellspacing=\"0\" style=\"border-collapse:collapse; width:99.8641%\">\r\n	<tbody>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th style=\"width:45.5163%\">Weight</th>\r\n			<td style=\"width:54.3478%\">0.10 lbs</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th style=\"width:45.5163%\">Dimensions</th>\r\n			<td style=\"width:54.3478%\">5.00 x 3.00 x 2.00 in</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th style=\"width:45.5163%\">Number of Slots</th>\r\n			<td style=\"width:54.3478%\">\r\n			<p>1</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n	</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n', 4, 'Yes', '2018-08-22', '<p>Micro SD Expansion Module provides an easy and convenient way to interface Micro SD card to Numato Lab&rsquo;s FPGA/Microcontroller boards. It can be connected to any FPGA/Microcontroller board featuring 2&times;6 pin Expansion connector. This module can be manually wired to FPGA/Microcontroller boards that does not have 2&times;6 expansion header.This product is compatible with most of Numato Lab&rsquo;s FPGA boards.</p>\r\n', 'SKU: EXPSDC001', 12.99, 0, 0, 0, 1, 1, 0),
(122, 'Callisto Spartan 6 USB 3.1 FPGA Module', 80, 'Active', '								<h2><strong>Description</strong></h2>\r\n\r\n<p>Callisto S6 is an easy to use FPGA Development board featuring the Xilinx Spartan 6 FPGA with 2Gb DDR3 SDRAM. This board contains the Xilinx XC6SLX150– FGG676 FPGA. The high-speed USB 3.1 interface (USB-C connector) provides fast and easy configuration download to the onboard SPI flash. There is no need for a programmer or special downloader cable to download bitstream to the board. The Development board also provides easy access to JTAG signals on a standard Xilinx Platform Cable compatible header. Callisto S6 provides the user the flexibility of adding their own peripherals through IO Expansion Headers.<br />\r\n<strong>Features</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>FPGA: Spartan XC6SLX150 in FGG676 package</li>\r\n	<li>DDR3: 2Gb DDR3 (MT41J128M16HA-125:K or equivalent)</li>\r\n	<li>Flash memory: 128 Mb Quadbit SPI flash memory (N25Q128A13ESE40E)</li>\r\n	<li>2 x 100MHz CMOS oscillator</li>\r\n	<li>USB 3.1 Gen1 @5Gbps (USB Type-C connector)</li>\r\n	<li>JTAG header for programming and debugging</li>\r\n	<li>12V DC power supply</li>\r\n	<li>A Push Button for the reset pin</li>\r\n	<li>284 IOs for user-defined purposes</li>\r\n	<li>Onboard voltage regulators for single power rail operation</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Applications</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>Signal Processing</li>\r\n	<li>Product Prototype Development</li>\r\n	<li>Communication devices development</li>\r\n	<li>Educational tool for Schools and Universities</li>\r\n	<li>Development and testing of custom embedded processors</li>\r\n	<li>Accelerated Computing Integration</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n', '								 <table border=\"1\" cellspacing=\"0\" style=\"border-collapse:collapse; width:99.8609%\">\r\n	<tbody>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th style=\"width:57.7191%\">FPGA</th>\r\n			<td style=\"width:42.1419%\">\r\n			<p><a href=\"https://numato.com/fpga/xc6slx150-2fgg676c\" rel=\"tag\">XC6SLX150- 2FGG676C</a></p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th style=\"width:57.7191%\">Memory</th>\r\n			<td style=\"width:42.1419%\">\r\n			<p><a href=\"https://numato.com/memory/ddr3-2gb\" rel=\"tag\">DDR3 – 2Gb</a></p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th style=\"width:57.7191%\">Number Of GPIOs (Max)</th>\r\n			<td style=\"width:42.1419%\">\r\n			<p>284</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th style=\"width:57.7191%\">Configuration Options</th>\r\n			<td style=\"width:42.1419%\">\r\n			<p>JTAG</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th style=\"width:57.7191%\">Non-Volatile Configuration Storage</th>\r\n			<td style=\"width:42.1419%\">\r\n			<p>N25Q128A13ESE40E</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th style=\"width:57.7191%\">Number of Clock Sources</th>\r\n			<td style=\"width:42.1419%\">\r\n			<p>2</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th style=\"width:57.7191%\">Communication</th>\r\n			<td style=\"width:42.1419%\">\r\n			<p>USB 3.1</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th style=\"width:57.7191%\">Primary Clock Frequency</th>\r\n			<td style=\"width:42.1419%\">\r\n			<p><a href=\"https://numato.com/primary-clock-frequency/100mhz\" rel=\"tag\">100MHz</a></p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n	</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n', 3, 'Yes', '2018-08-28', '								<p>Callisto Spartan 6 is an easy to use FPGA Development board featuring the Xilinx Spartan 6 FPGA with 2Gb DDR3 SDRAM. This board contains the Xilinx XC6SLX150– FGG676 FPGA. The high-speed USB 3.1 interface (USB-C connector) provides fast and easy configuration download to the onboard SPI flash. There is no need for a programmer or special downloader cable to download bitstream to the board. The Development board also provides easy access to JTAG signals on a standard Xilinx Platform Cable compatible header. Callisto S6 provides the user the flexibility of adding their own peripherals through IO Expansion Headers.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Features</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>FPGA: Spartan XC6SLX150 in FGG676 package</li>\r\n	<li>DDR3: 2Gb DDR3 (MT41J128M16HA-125:K or equivalent)</li>\r\n	<li>Flash memory: 128 Mb Quadbit SPI flash memory (N25Q128A13ESE40E)</li>\r\n	<li>2 x 100MHz CMOS oscillator</li>\r\n	<li>USB 3.1 Gen1 @5Gbps (USB Type-C connector)</li>\r\n	<li>JTAG header for programming and debugging</li>\r\n	<li>12V DC power supply</li>\r\n	<li>A Push Button for the reset pin</li>\r\n	<li>284 IOs for user-defined purposes</li>\r\n	<li>Onboard voltage regulators for single power rail operation</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n', 'SKU: NLFX1003', 647.99, 0, 0, 0, 1, 1, 0),
(123, 'Mimas A7 – Artix 7 FPGA Development Board', 81, 'Active', '<h2><strong>Description</strong></h2>\r\n\r\n<p>Mimas A7 is a serious upgrade to our lower cost Mimas V2 FPGA Development board. Based on Artix 7&trade; 50T FPGA, Mimas A7 plenty powerful as it is versatile offering improved system performance for cost sensitive markets. This FPGA Development Board follows the philosophy of offering a large variety of peripherals on a compact form factor to allow minimal external components to run and evaluate as many designs as possible. Mimas A7 is a great platform for implementing Soft processors such as Microblaze to make it a complete embedded platform. The built in Gigabit Ethernet offers low latency high bandwidth data transfer to host. The USB 2.0 host interface based on popular FT2232H offers high bandwidth data transfer and board programming without the need for any external programming adapters. Onboard HDMI IN/OUT interfaces along with large DDR3 SDRAM makes Mimas A7 a great platform for video capture, processing and rendering. The staple peripherals such as switches and seven segment displays offer great value for learning, prototyping and debugging. This board could be used as an FPGA module to integrate to other larger designs as well.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Features</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>Device: Xilinx Artix 7 FPGA (XC7A50T-1FGG484C)</li>\r\n	<li>DDR3: 2Gb DDR3 (MT41J128M16HA-125 or equivalent)</li>\r\n	<li>FTDI FT2232H based host interface</li>\r\n	<li>Built-in programming interface. No expensive JTAG adapters needed for programming the board</li>\r\n	<li>Gigabit Ethernet</li>\r\n	<li>HDMI IN/OUT interfaces</li>\r\n	<li>High-Speed Serial Interface (GTP) available on mini DisplayPort connectors</li>\r\n	<li>Onboard 128Mb flash memory for FPGA configuration storage and custom user data storage</li>\r\n	<li>100MHz LVDS oscillator</li>\r\n	<li>Micro SD card slot for memory expansion</li>\r\n	<li>Seven Segment Display and switches for easy learning, prototyping and debugging</li>\r\n	<li>FPGA configuration via JTAG and USB</li>\r\n	<li>80 IOs (40 professionally length matched Differential Pairs) for user-defined purposes</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Applications</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>Product Prototype Development</li>\r\n	<li>Accelerated computing integration</li>\r\n	<li>Development and testing of custom embedded processors</li>\r\n	<li>Signal Processing</li>\r\n	<li>Communication devices development</li>\r\n	<li>Educational tool for Schools and Universities</li>\r\n	<li>Video processing</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n', '<table border=\"1\" cellspacing=\"0\" style=\"border-collapse:collapse; width:99.8609%\">\r\n	<tbody>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th style=\"width:36.8567%\">FPGA</th>\r\n			<td style=\"width:63.0042%\">\r\n			<p><a href=\"https://numato.com/fpga/xc7a50t-1fgg484c\" rel=\"tag\">XC7A50T-1FGG484C</a></p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th style=\"width:36.8567%\">Configuration Options</th>\r\n			<td style=\"width:63.0042%\">\r\n			<p>JTAG, USB</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th style=\"width:36.8567%\">Ethernet</th>\r\n			<td style=\"width:63.0042%\">\r\n			<p>Gigabit</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th style=\"width:36.8567%\">HDMI Inputs</th>\r\n			<td style=\"width:63.0042%\">\r\n			<p>1</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th style=\"width:36.8567%\">HDMI Outputs</th>\r\n			<td style=\"width:63.0042%\">\r\n			<p>1</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th style=\"width:36.8567%\">Host Interface</th>\r\n			<td style=\"width:63.0042%\">\r\n			<p>USB 2.0</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th style=\"width:36.8567%\">Memory</th>\r\n			<td style=\"width:63.0042%\">\r\n			<p><a href=\"https://numato.com/memory/ddr3-2gbits\" rel=\"tag\">DDR3 &ndash; 2GBits</a></p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th style=\"width:36.8567%\">Number Of GPIOs (Max)</th>\r\n			<td style=\"width:63.0042%\">\r\n			<p>80</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th style=\"width:36.8567%\">Number Of Diff Pairs</th>\r\n			<td style=\"width:63.0042%\">\r\n			<p>40</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th style=\"width:36.8567%\">Primary Clock Frequency</th>\r\n			<td style=\"width:63.0042%\">\r\n			<p><a href=\"https://numato.com/primary-clock-frequency/100mhz\" rel=\"tag\">100MHz</a></p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th style=\"width:36.8567%\">High Speed Serial</th>\r\n			<td style=\"width:63.0042%\">\r\n			<p>GTP x4 (on two mini DisplayPort connectors)</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n	</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n', 1, 'Yes', '2018-08-28', '<p>Mimas A7 is a serious upgrade to our lower cost Mimas V2 FPGA Development board. Based on Artix 7&trade; 50T FPGA, Mimas A7 plenty powerful as it is versatile. This FPGA Development Board follows the philosophy of offering a large variety of peripherals on a compact form factor to allow minimal external components to run and evaluate as many designs as possible. Mimas A7 is a great platform for implementing Soft processors such as Microblaze to make it a complete embedded platform. The built in Gigabit Ethernet offers low latency high bandwidth data transfer to host. The USB 2.0 host interface based on popular FT2232H offers high bandwidth data transfer and board programming without the need for any external programming adapters. Onboard HDMI IN/OUT interfaces along with large DDR3 SDRAM makes Mimas A7 a great platform for video capture, processing and rendering. The staple peripherals such as switches and seven segment displays offer great value for learning, prototyping and debugging.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Features</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>Device: Xilinx Artix 7 FPGA (XC7A50T-1FGG484C)</li>\r\n	<li>DDR3: 2Gb DDR3 (MT41J128M16HA-125 or equivalent)</li>\r\n	<li>FTDI FT2232H based host interface</li>\r\n	<li>Built in programming interface. No expensive JTAG adapters needed for programming the board</li>\r\n	<li>Gigabit Ethernet</li>\r\n	<li>HDMI IN/OUT interfaces</li>\r\n	<li>HighSpeed Serial Interface (GTP) available on mini DisplayPort connectors</li>\r\n	<li>Onboard 128Mb flash memory for FPGA configuration storage and custom user data storage</li>\r\n	<li>100MHz LVDS oscillator</li>\r\n	<li>Micro SD card slot for memory expansion</li>\r\n	<li>Seven Segment Display and switches for easy learning, prototyping and debugging</li>\r\n	<li>FPGA configuration via JTAG and USB</li>\r\n	<li>80 IOs (40 professionally length matched Differential Pairs) for user defined purposes</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n', 'SKU: NLFX1001', 224.95, 0, 0, 1, 111, 110, 1),
(126, '32 Channel Relay Controller Board-12V', 78, 'Active', '<h3><strong>Description</strong></h3>\r\n\r\n<p>Numato Lab`s 32 Channel Relay Controller Board is a smart choice for controlling higher current loads from your micro controller development board or a PC parallel port. This board has thirty two onboard relays which can switch up to 10A. All relay terminals (C, NC, NO) are accessible through screw terminals which makes wiring up the board very easy. The relays are driven by popular darlington array ULN2803. Relay coil is rated for 12VDC.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Features</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>32 on board SPDT Relays .</li>\r\n	<li>7A Maximum Switching Current.</li>\r\n	<li>ULN2803 Relay Driver.</li>\r\n	<li>Very compact and easy to wire up</li>\r\n	<li>Connects directly to TTL devices (Microcontrollers, Arduino etc..).</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Applications</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>Home Automation</li>\r\n	<li>Industrial Automation</li>\r\n	<li>Lighting Control</li>\r\n	<li>Garden Equipment Control</li>\r\n	<li>Test Fixtures</li>\r\n	<li>DIY and Hobby</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n', '<table border=\"1\" cellspacing=\"0\" style=\"border-collapse:collapse; width:99.8609%\">\r\n	<tbody>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th style=\"width:53.5466%\">Weight</th>\r\n			<td style=\"width:46.3143%\">1.50 lbs</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th style=\"width:53.5466%\">Dimensions</th>\r\n			<td style=\"width:46.3143%\">12.00 x 9.00 x 2.00 in</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th style=\"width:53.5466%\">Number Of Relays</th>\r\n			<td style=\"width:46.3143%\">\r\n			<p>32</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th style=\"width:53.5466%\">Relay Type</th>\r\n			<td style=\"width:46.3143%\">\r\n			<p><a href=\"https://numato.com/relay-type/mechanical\" rel=\"tag\">Mechanical</a></p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th style=\"width:53.5466%\">Max Relay Current Rating</th>\r\n			<td style=\"width:46.3143%\">\r\n			<p>10A</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th style=\"width:53.5466%\">Communication</th>\r\n			<td style=\"width:46.3143%\">\r\n			<p>TTL Compatible Input</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n	</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n', 11, 'Yes', '2018-08-30', '<p>Numato Lab&rsquo;s 32 Channel Relay Controller Board is a smart choice for controlling higher current loads from your micro controller development board or a PC parallel port.<br />\r\n<strong>Features</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>32 on board SPDT Relays .</li>\r\n	<li>7A Maximum Switching Current.</li>\r\n	<li>ULN2803 Relay Driver.</li>\r\n	<li>Very compact and easy to wire up</li>\r\n	<li>Connects directly to TTL devices (Microcontrollers, Arduino etc..).</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Applications</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>Home Automation</li>\r\n	<li>Industrial Automation</li>\r\n	<li>Lighting Control</li>\r\n	<li>Garden Equipment Control</li>\r\n	<li>Test Fixtures</li>\r\n	<li>DIY and Hobby</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n', 'SKU: RL320003', 52.95, 0, 0, 1, 11, 9, 2),
(127, 'Prodigy UR Series – 8 Channel USB Modbus Relay ', 93, 'Active', '<h2><strong>Description</strong></h2>\r\n\r\n<p>Prodigy UR08/UR16 is an Input/Output module that supports Modbus protocol with a serial interface over USB. This product has 8/16 Relays (Dry Contacts) and 8 Additional IOs that supports Digital Input, Digital Output and Analog Input functions. The USB host interface makes connecting this device to any Windows, Linux, Mac machines or embedded computers such as RPi&nbsp; an easy task. Meanwhile, support for industry standard Modbus protocol makes it easy to use this device with almost any automation software that supports Modbus/RTU. UR08/UR16 when connected to a host computer, is enumerated as a regular serial port. This alleviates the difficulty of working with USB protocol and offers a transparent interface to access the device. UR08 acts as a Modbus slave device at slave address 1. UR08/UR16 is enclosed in a flame resistant enclosure with support for DIN rail mounting. Flexible DIN Rail mounting system allows easy installation and removal without screws or other mechanisms. UR08/UR16 supports several features such as Relay Timer, Safety Timer (Watchdog), Programmable Power On State etc..</p>\r\n', '<table border=\"1\" cellspacing=\"0\" style=\"border-collapse:collapse; width:99.8609%\">\r\n	<tbody>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th style=\"width:51.8776%\">Weight</th>\r\n			<td style=\"width:47.9833%\">N/A</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th style=\"width:51.8776%\">Analog Input Resolution</th>\r\n			<td style=\"width:47.9833%\">\r\n			<p>12 Bits</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th style=\"width:51.8776%\">Analog Inputs</th>\r\n			<td style=\"width:47.9833%\">\r\n			<p>8</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th style=\"width:51.8776%\">Host Interface</th>\r\n			<td style=\"width:47.9833%\">\r\n			<p>USB 2.0 CDC</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th style=\"width:51.8776%\">IO Voltage Max</th>\r\n			<td style=\"width:47.9833%\">\r\n			<p>3.3V</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th style=\"width:51.8776%\">Max Relay Current Rating</th>\r\n			<td style=\"width:47.9833%\">\r\n			<p>5A</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th style=\"width:51.8776%\">Number Of GPIOs (Max)</th>\r\n			<td style=\"width:47.9833%\">\r\n			<p>8</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th style=\"width:51.8776%\">Number Of Relays</th>\r\n			<td style=\"width:47.9833%\">\r\n			<p><a href=\"https://numato.com/number-of-relays/16\" rel=\"tag\">16</a>,&nbsp;<a href=\"https://numato.com/number-of-relays/8\" rel=\"tag\">8</a></p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th style=\"width:51.8776%\">Relay Type</th>\r\n			<td style=\"width:47.9833%\">\r\n			<p><a href=\"https://numato.com/relay-type/mechanical\" rel=\"tag\">Mechanical</a></p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th style=\"width:51.8776%\">Package Contents</th>\r\n			<td style=\"width:47.9833%\">\r\n			<p>Prodigy UR08/UR16 x1<br />\r\n			USB A to B Cable x1<br />\r\n			12V Power Supply x1</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n	</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n', 7, 'Yes', '2018-08-31', '<p>Prodigy UR08/UR16 is a USB Relay output module that supports Modbus protocol. The USB Serial (CDC) host interface makes connecting this device to any Windows, Linux, Mac machines or embedded computers such as RPi&nbsp; an easy task. Support of industry standard Modbus protocol makes it easy to use this device with almost any automation software that supports Modbus/RTU.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Features</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>8/16 Relays rated up to 250V/5A each</li>\r\n	<li>8 IOs that supports Digital Input, Digital Output and Analog Input features</li>\r\n	<li>USB CDC (Serial) interface that works with Windows, Linux, Mac and more. No USB knowledge required!</li>\r\n	<li>Compatible with most automation software in market that supports Modbus RTU</li>\r\n	<li>Features such as Relay Timer, Watchdog timer for fail safe operation, Configurable Power On states etc..</li>\r\n	<li>Write your own script or software with help of large number of sample code provided in various languages</li>\r\n	<li>Detachable screw terminals for easy wiring and replacement</li>\r\n	<li>Flame-resistant enclosure with DIN Rail and Wall Mounting support</li>\r\n	<li>+12V Power Supply (included)</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n', 'SKU: NLRM8001', 249.95, 0, 0, 0, 7, 7, 0),
(128, 'Prodigy ZRX Series -64 Channel  ', 93, 'Active', '<h2><strong>Description</strong></h2>\r\n\r\n<p>Prodigy ZRX16/ZRX32/ZRX64 is an Input/Output module that supports Modbus RTU over USB and RS485 and Modbus TCP over Ethernet. This product has 16/32/64 Relays (Dry Contacts) and 8 Additional IOs that supports Digital Input, Digital Output and 6 Analog Input functions. The RS485/USB/Ethernet host interface makes connecting this device to any Windows, Linux, Mac machines or embedded computers such as RPi an easy task. Meanwhile, support for industry standard Modbus protocol makes it easy to use this device with almost any automation software that supports Modbus &ndash; RTU/TCP. ZRX16/ZRX32/ZRX64 when RTU model connected to a host computer, is enumerated as a regular serial port. This alleviates the difficulty of working with USB protocol and offers a transparent interface to access the device. ZRX16/ZRX32/ZRX64 acts as a Modbus slave device at slave address 1. Flexible DIN Rail mounting system allows easy installation and removal with screws. ZRX16/ZRX32/ZRX64 supports several features such as Relay Timer, Safety Timer (Watchdog), Programmable Power On State etc..</p>\r\n', '<table border=\"1\" cellspacing=\"0\" style=\"border-collapse:collapse; width:99.8609%\">\r\n	<tbody>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th style=\"width:20.1669%\">Number Of Relays</th>\r\n			<td style=\"width:79.694%\">\r\n			<p><a href=\"https://numato.com/number-of-relays/16\" rel=\"tag\">16</a>,&nbsp;<a href=\"https://numato.com/number-of-relays/32\" rel=\"tag\">32</a>,&nbsp;<a href=\"https://numato.com/number-of-relays/64\" rel=\"tag\">64</a></p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th style=\"width:20.1669%\">Relay Type</th>\r\n			<td style=\"width:79.694%\">\r\n			<p><a href=\"https://numato.com/relay-type/mechanical\" rel=\"tag\">Mechanical</a></p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th style=\"width:20.1669%\">Max Relay Current Rating</th>\r\n			<td style=\"width:79.694%\">\r\n			<p>5A</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th style=\"width:20.1669%\">Number Of GPIOs (Max)</th>\r\n			<td style=\"width:79.694%\">\r\n			<p>8</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th style=\"width:20.1669%\">IO Voltage Max</th>\r\n			<td style=\"width:79.694%\">\r\n			<p>3.3V</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th style=\"width:20.1669%\">Analog Inputs</th>\r\n			<td style=\"width:79.694%\">\r\n			<p>6</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th style=\"width:20.1669%\">Analog Input Resolution</th>\r\n			<td style=\"width:79.694%\">\r\n			<p>12 Bits</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th style=\"width:20.1669%\">Host Interface</th>\r\n			<td style=\"width:79.694%\">\r\n			<p>Ethernet, USB 2.0 CDC</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th style=\"width:20.1669%\">Warranty</th>\r\n			<td style=\"width:79.694%\">\r\n			<p><a href=\"https://numato.com/warranty/standard\" rel=\"tag\">Standard</a></p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th style=\"width:20.1669%\">Package Contents</th>\r\n			<td style=\"width:79.694%\">\r\n			<p>Prodigy ZRX16/ZRX32/ZRX64 &ndash; RTU/TCP x1, USB A to B Cable x1, LAN Cable x1(TCP), 12V Power Supply x1</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n	</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n', 7, 'Yes', '2018-08-31', '<h1>&nbsp;</h1>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"woocommerce-product-details__short-description\">\r\n<p>Prodigy ZRX16/ZRX32/ZRX64 is an Input/Output module that supports Modbus RTU over USB and RS485 and Modbus TCP over Ethernet. The USB/Ethernet host interface makes connecting this device to any Windows, Linux, Mac machines or embedded computers such as RPi an easy task. Support of industry standard Modbus protocol makes it easy to use this device with almost any automation software that supports Modbus &ndash; RTU/TCP.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Features</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>16/32/64 SPST Relays rated up to 250V/5A each</li>\r\n	<li>8 IOs that supports Digital Input, Digital Output, and 6 Analog Input features</li>\r\n	<li>USB CDC (Serial) interface that works with Windows, Linux, Mac and more. No USB knowledge required!</li>\r\n	<li>Compatible with most automation software in the market that supports Modbus RTU/TCP</li>\r\n	<li>Features such as Relay Timer, the Watchdog timer for fail-safe operation, Configurable Power On states etc..</li>\r\n	<li>Write your own script or software with help of a large number of sample code provided in various languages</li>\r\n	<li>Detachable screw terminals for easy wiring and replacement</li>\r\n	<li>+12V Power Supply (included)</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</div>\r\n', 'SKU: NLRM6401', 599.95, 0, 0, 0, 3, 3, 0),
(130, 'Narvi Spartan 7 FPGA Module ', 119, 'Active', '<h2>Description</h2>\r\n\r\n<p>Narvi is an easy to use FPGA Development board featuring Spartan 7 FPGA (XC7S50 &ndash; CSG324A package) with FTDI&rsquo;s FT2232H Dual-Channel USB device. It is specially designed for development and integration of FPGA based accelerated features to other designs. Narvi is pin compatible with Saturn Spartan 6 FPGA Module, Skoll Kintex 7 FPGA Module, Neso Artix 7 FPGA Module, Styx Zynq 7020 FPGA Module and Telesto MAX10 FPGA Module and thus offers a seamless upgrade path. The high-speed USB 2.0 interface provides fast and easy configuration download to the onboard SPI flash. No programmer or special downloader cable is needed to download the bit stream to the board. The second FTDI channel can be used to develop custom high data-rate USB based applications. Narvi provides user flexibility in adding their own peripherals through IO Expansion Headers.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Features</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>Pin compatible with :</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<ul>\r\n		<li>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<a href=\"https://numato.com/product/saturn-spartan-6-fpga-development-board-with-ddr-sdram\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">Saturn Spartan 6 FPGA Module</a></li>\r\n		<li>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<a href=\"https://numato.com/product/skoll-kintex-7-fpga-development-board\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">Skoll Kintex 7 FPGA Module</a></li>\r\n		<li>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<a href=\"https://numato.com/product/neso-artix-7-fpga-development-board\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">Neso Artix 7 FPGA Module</a></li>\r\n		<li>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<a href=\"https://numato.com/product/styx-zynq-7020-fpga-module\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">Styx Zynq 7020 FPGA Module</a></li>\r\n		<li>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<a href=\"https://numato.com/product/telesto-max10-fpga-module\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">Telesto MAX10 FPGA Module</a>&nbsp;and offers a seamless upgrade path.\r\n		<ul>\r\n			<li>FPGA: XC7S50 in CSGA324 package, Speed Grade: -1</li>\r\n			<li>DDR3: 2Gb DDR3 (MT41J128M16HA-125:K or equivalent).</li>\r\n			<li>Flash memory: 128 Mb Quadbit SPI flash memory (N25Q128A13ESE40E).</li>\r\n			<li>100MHz CMOS oscillator.</li>\r\n			<li>High-Speed USB 2.0 interface for On-board flash programming. FT2232H Channel B is dedicated for SPI Flash /JTAG Programming. Channel A can be used for custom applications.</li>\r\n			<li>Onboard voltage regulators for single power rail operation.</li>\r\n			<li>FPGA configuration via JTAG and USB.</li>\r\n			<li>Maximum IOs for user-defined purposes.</li>\r\n			<li>&ndash;FPGA &ndash; 130 IOs</li>\r\n			<li>&ndash;FT2232H &ndash; 8 IOs</li>\r\n		</ul>\r\n		</li>\r\n	</ul>\r\n	</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Applications</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<ul>\r\n		<li>Product Prototype Development</li>\r\n		<li>Accelerated computing integration</li>\r\n		<li>Development and testing of custom embedded processors</li>\r\n		<li>Signal Processing</li>\r\n		<li>Communication devices development</li>\r\n		<li>Educational tool for Schools and Universities</li>\r\n	</ul>\r\n	</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n', '<table class=\"shop_attributes\">\r\n	<tbody>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Speed Grade</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>-1</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>FPGA</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p><a href=\"https://numato.com/fpga/xc7s50-csga324\" rel=\"tag\">XC7S50 &ndash; CSGA324</a></p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Memory</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p><a href=\"https://numato.com/memory/ddr3-2gbits\" rel=\"tag\">DDR3 &ndash; 2GBits</a></p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Primary Clock Frequency</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p><a href=\"https://numato.com/primary-clock-frequency/100mhz\" rel=\"tag\">100MHz</a></p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Configuration Options</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>JTAG, USB</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Number Of GPIOs (Max)</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>130</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Host Interface</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>USB 2.0</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n	</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n', 1, 'Yes', '2019-04-14', '<p>Narvi is an easy to use FPGA Development board featuring Spartan 7 FPGA (XC7S50 &ndash; CSG324A package) with FTDI&rsquo;s FT2232H Dual-Channel USB device. It is specially designed for development and integration of FPGA based accelerated features to other designs. The high-speed USB 2.0 interface provides fast and easy configuration download to the onboard SPI flash. No programmer or special downloader cable is needed to download the bit stream to the board. The second FTDI channel can be used to develop custom high data-rate USB based applications. Narvi provides user flexibility in adding their own peripherals through IO Expansion Headers.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Features</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>Pin compatible with :</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<a href=\"https://numato.com/product/saturn-spartan-6-fpga-development-board-with-ddr-sdram\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">Saturn Spartan 6 FPGA Module</a></li>\r\n	<li>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<a href=\"https://numato.com/product/skoll-kintex-7-fpga-development-board\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">Skoll Kintex 7 FPGA Module</a></li>\r\n	<li>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<a href=\"https://numato.com/product/neso-artix-7-fpga-development-board\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">Neso Artix 7 FPGA Module</a></li>\r\n	<li>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<a href=\"https://numato.com/product/styx-zynq-7020-fpga-module\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">Styx Zynq 7020 FPGA Module</a></li>\r\n	<li>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<a href=\"https://numato.com/product/telesto-max10-fpga-module\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">Telesto MAX10 FPGA Module</a>&nbsp;and offers a seamless upgrade path.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>FPGA: XC7S50 in CSGA324 package, Speed Grade: -1</li>\r\n	<li>DDR3: 2Gb DDR3 (MT41J128M16HA-125:K or equivalent).</li>\r\n	<li>Flash memory: 128 Mb Quadbit SPI flash memory (N25Q128A13ESE40E).</li>\r\n	<li>100MHz CMOS oscillator.</li>\r\n	<li>High-Speed USB 2.0 interface for On-board flash programming. FT2232H Channel B is dedicated for SPI Flash /JTAG Programming. Channel A can be used for custom applications.</li>\r\n	<li>Onboard voltage regulators for single power rail operation.</li>\r\n	<li>FPGA configuration via JTAG and USB.</li>\r\n	<li>Maximum IOs for user-defined purposes.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&ndash; FPGA &ndash; 130 IOs</li>\r\n	<li>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&ndash; FT2232H &ndash; 8 IOs</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n', 'SKU: NLFX1007', 164.95, 0, 0, 0, 33, 33, 0),
(131, 'Aller Artix-7 FPGA Board with M.2 Interface', 81, 'Active', '<h2>Description</h2>\r\n\r\n<p>Aller is specifically designed for development and integration of FPGA based accelerated features into other larger designs, it can be used with laptops, desktops, and servers featuring standard 2280 M.2 form factor M-key slot.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Aller is an easy to use M.2 form-factor FPGA Development Board featuring Xilinx Artix-7 FPGA with x4 PCIe Gen2 lanes on M.2 M-Key interface, Trusted Platform Module (TPM AT97SC3205), 2Gb DDR3 SDRAM and 1Gb QSPI Flash Memory.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Nowadays, most of the new laptops come with M.2 M-key slots for NVMe storage modules and Aller can be seamlessly used with those slots. Open source PCI Express IP cores such as litepcie make the development of PCIe designs very cost-effective. The M.2 M-Key provides up to 4x PCIe lanes, each running at 5 GT/s (PCIe Gen 2) on Aller.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Features</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>Xilinx Artix 7 FPGA (XC7A200T-2FBG484I)</li>\r\n	<li>2Gb DDR3 ( MT41J128M16JT-125:K TR )</li>\r\n	<li>4 lane PCIe Gen2 (5 GT/s)</li>\r\n	<li>Trusted Platform Module (AT97SC3205)</li>\r\n	<li>M.2 Connector Interface, M-Key</li>\r\n	<li>Onboard 1Gb QSPI flash memory for FPGA configuration</li>\r\n	<li>1 RGB LED for custom use</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Applications</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>Product Prototype Development</li>\r\n	<li>Accelerated computing</li>\r\n	<li>Signal Processing</li>\r\n	<li>Memory Intensive FPGA development</li>\r\n	<li>High Hash Rate calculations for Blockchain technologies</li>\r\n	<li>Offloading computationally intensive algorithms to FPGA</li>\r\n	<li>Machine Learning and Artificial Intelligence</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n', '<table class=\"shop_attributes\">\r\n	<tbody>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>FPGA</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p><a href=\"https://numato.com/fpga/xc7a100t-1fgg484c\" rel=\"tag\">XC7A100T-1FGG484C</a></p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Configuration Options</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>JTAG</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Memory&nbsp;</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>DDR3-2DBits</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Non-Volatile Configuration Storage</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>1Gb flash memory</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Total Number of GTP</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>4 (1x PCIe x1)</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Junction Temperature Range</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>0-90 degrees Celsius</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Power Supply</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>3.3V from M.2 connector (M-Key)</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Primary Clock Frequency</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>100MHz</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Package Contents</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>A standard heat sink, Aller Artix-7 M.2 FPGA Module &ndash; 1 Qty</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n	</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n', 3, 'Yes', '2019-04-14', '<p>Aller is specifically designed for development and integration of FPGA based accelerated features into other larger designs, it can be used with laptops, desktops, and servers featuring standard 2280 M.2 form factor M-key slot.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Nowadays, most of the new laptops come with M.2 M-key slots for NVMe storage modules and Aller can be seamlessly used with those slots. Open source PCI Express IP cores such as litepcie make the development of PCIe designs very cost-effective.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Features</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>Xilinx Artix 7 FPGA (XC7A200T-2FBG484I)</li>\r\n	<li>2Gb DDR3 ( MT41J128M16JT-125:K TR )</li>\r\n	<li>4 lane PCIe Gen2 (5 GT/s)</li>\r\n	<li>Trusted Platform Module (AT97SC3205)</li>\r\n	<li>M.2 Connector Interface, M-Key</li>\r\n	<li>Onboard 1Gb QSPI flash memory for FPGA configuration</li>\r\n	<li>1 RGB LED for custom use</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n', 'SKU: NLFX1006', 474.95, 0, 0, 0, 12, 10, 2),
(132, 'Tagus–Artix 7 PCIe Board -XC7A200T in -2 FBG484I', 81, 'Active', '<h2>Description</h2>\r\n\r\n<p>Tagus is an easy to use FPGA Development Board featuring Xilinx Artix-7 FPGA with x1 PCIe interface, Trusted Platform Module (ATXXXXXX) , Dual SFP+ cages, and 2Gb DDR3 SDRAM. This board features Xilinx XC7A100T&ndash; FGG484 FPGA. The board features Low Pin Count (LPC) high-speed FMC connector conforming to ANSI/VITA 57.1 Standard for the purpose of adding additional features to the board by using custom or commercial off-the-shelf daughter boards.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Features</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>FPGA: Artix-7 XC7A200T in -1 FBG484 package</li>\r\n	<li>1 lane PCIe Gen2.0(5.0GT/s)</li>\r\n	<li>DDR3: 2Gb DDR3 (MT41J128M16HA-125:K or equivalent)</li>\r\n	<li>128 Mb QSPI flash memory (N25Q128A13ESE40E) for Configuration and optional data storage</li>\r\n	<li>USB to UART serial converter</li>\r\n	<li>1 x 100MHz CMOS oscillator</li>\r\n	<li>Maximum 68 IOs for user-defined purposes on ANSI/VITA 57.1 Standard compliant FMC LPC connector</li>\r\n	<li>1x GTP lanes upto 6.6Gbps on ANSI/VITA 57.1 Standard compliant FMC LPC connector</li>\r\n	<li>1 RGB LED for custom use</li>\r\n	<li>1x Trusted Platform Module (ATXXXXXX )</li>\r\n	<li>Dual SFP+ Cages</li>\r\n	<li>MicroSD adapter for bulk data storage</li>\r\n	<li>Onboard voltage regulators for single power rail operation</li>\r\n	<li>Can be powered from PCIe slot or from an external power supply</li>\r\n	<li>JTAG header for programming and debugging</li>\r\n	<li>All differential pairs are length matched on the board</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Applications</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>Parallel Processing and Accelerators</li>\r\n	<li>Product Prototype Development</li>\r\n	<li>Development and Testing of custom embedded processors</li>\r\n	<li>Signal Processing</li>\r\n	<li>Communication Devices Development</li>\r\n	<li>Data Acquisition</li>\r\n	<li>Educational tool for Schools and Universities</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n', '<table class=\"shop_attributes\">\r\n	<tbody>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>FPGA</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p><a href=\"https://numato.com/fpga/xc7a100t-1fgg484\" rel=\"tag\">XC7A200T-1FBG484</a></p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Configuration Options</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>JTAG, USB</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Memory</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>DDR3-2GBits</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Number Of GPIOs (Max)</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>68</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Non-Volatile Configuration Storage</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>N25Q128A13ESE40E</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Total Number of GTP</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>4 (1x PCIe x1, 1x FMC LPC, 2x SFP+)</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Differential Pairs Length Matched</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>Yes</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Communication</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>x1 PCIe, USB-RS232</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Primary Clock Frequency</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>100MHz</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n	</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n', 7, 'Yes', '2019-04-14', '<p>Tagus is an easy to use FPGA Development Board featuring Xilinx Artix-7 FPGA with x1 PCIe interface, Trusted Platform Module (ATXXXXXX) , Dual SFP+ cages, and 2Gb DDR3 SDRAM. This board features Xilinx XC7A200T&ndash; FBG484 FPGA. The board features Low Pin Count (LPC) high-speed FMC connector conforming to ANSI/VITA 57.1 Standard for the purpose of adding additional features to the board by using custom or commercial off-the-shelf daughter boards.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Features</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>FPGA: Artix-7 XC7A200T in -1 FBG484 package</li>\r\n	<li>1 lane PCIe Gen2.0(5.0GT/s)</li>\r\n	<li>DDR3: 2Gb DDR3 (MT41J128M16HA-125:K or equivalent)</li>\r\n	<li>128 Mb QSPI flash memory (N25Q128A13ESE40E) for Configuration and optional data storage</li>\r\n	<li>USB to UART serial converter</li>\r\n	<li>1 x 100MHz CMOS oscillator</li>\r\n	<li>Maximum 68 IOs for user-defined purposes on ANSI/VITA 57.1 Standard compliant FMC LPC connector</li>\r\n	<li>1x GTP lanes upto 6.6Gbps on ANSI/VITA 57.1 Standard compliant FMC LPC connector</li>\r\n	<li>1 RGB LED for custom use</li>\r\n	<li>1x Trusted Platform Module (ATXXXXXX )</li>\r\n	<li>Dual SFP+ Cages</li>\r\n	<li>MicroSD adapter for bulk data storage</li>\r\n	<li>Onboard voltage regulators for single power rail operation</li>\r\n	<li>Can be powered from PCIe slot or from an external power supply</li>\r\n	<li>JTAG header for programming and debugging</li>\r\n	<li>All differential pairs are length matched on the board</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n', 'SKU: NLFX1005', 574.95, 0, 0, 0, 51, 62, -11);
INSERT INTO `tbl_product` (`product_id`, `product_name`, `product_category_id`, `product_status`, `product_description`, `product_specification`, `priorty`, `display_flag`, `product_entry_date`, `product_details`, `product_code`, `product_amt`, `product_tax`, `product_discount`, `product_threshold`, `total_product`, `total_sold`, `total_remaining`) VALUES
(133, 'Callisto Kintex 7 USB 3.1 FPGA Module  XC7K160T-FB', 82, 'Active', '<h2>Description</h2>\r\n\r\n<p>Callisto K7 is an easy to use FPGA Module featuring the Xilinx Kintex 7 FPGA with 4Gb DDR3 SDRAM. This board contains the Xilinx XC7K410T&ndash; FBG676 FPGA. The high-speed USB 3.1 interface (USB-C connector) provides fast and easy configuration download to the onboard SPI flash. There is no need for a programmer or special downloader cable to download bitstream to the board. The FPGA Module also provides easy access to JTAG signals on a standard Xilinx Platform Cable compatible header. Callisto K7 provides the user the flexibility of adding their own peripherals through IO Expansion Headers.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Features</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>FPGA: Kintex XC7K410T in FBG676 package</li>\r\n	<li>DDR3: 4Gb DDR3 (MT41J256M16HA-125:K or equivalent)</li>\r\n	<li>Flash memory: 1 Gb Quadbit SPI flash memory (MT25QL01GBBB)</li>\r\n	<li>1 x 100MHz CMOS oscillator</li>\r\n	<li>USB 3.1 Gen1 @5Gbps (USB Type-C connector)</li>\r\n	<li>Onboard voltage regulators for single power rail operation</li>\r\n	<li>12V DC power supply</li>\r\n	<li>A Push Button for the reset pin</li>\r\n	<li>JTAG header for programming and debugging.</li>\r\n	<li>274 IOs for user-defined purposes</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Applications</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>Product Prototype Development</li>\r\n	<li>Communication Devices Development</li>\r\n	<li>Accelerated Computing Integration</li>\r\n	<li>Development and Testing of Custom embedded processors</li>\r\n	<li>Signal Processing</li>\r\n	<li>Educational tool for Schools and Universities</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n', '<table class=\"shop_attributes\">\r\n	<tbody>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>FPGA</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p><a href=\"https://numato.com/fpga/xc7k160t-fbg676\" rel=\"tag\">XC7K160T&ndash; FBG676</a>,&nbsp;</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Memory</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>DDR3-4Gb</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Number Of GPIOs (Max)</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>274</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Configuration Options</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>JTAG, USB</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Non-Volatile Configuration Storage</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>MT25QL01GBBB</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Number of Clock Sources</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>1</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Communication</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>USB 3.1</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Primary Clock Frequency</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>100MHz</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n	</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n', 3, 'Yes', '2019-04-14', '<div class=\"woocommerce-product-details__short-description\">\r\n<p>Callisto K7 is an easy to use FPGA Module featuring the Xilinx Kintex 7 FPGA with 4Gb DDR3 SDRAM. This board contains the Xilinx <a href=\"https://numato.com/product/callisto-kintex-7-usb-3-1-fpga-module/?attribute_pa_fpga=xc7k160t-fbg676\">XC7K160T&ndash; FBG676</a>. Other FPGA configurations are available at request.The high-speed USB 3.1 interface (USB-C connector) provides fast and easy configuration download to the onboard SPI flash. There is no need for a programmer or special downloader cable to download bitstream to the board. The FPGA Module also provides easy access to JTAG signals on a standard Xilinx Platform Cable compatible header. Callisto K7 provides the user the flexibility of adding their own peripherals through IO Expansion Headers.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Features</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>FPGA: Kintex XC7K410T in FBG676 package</li>\r\n	<li>DDR3: 4Gb DDR3 (MT41J256M16HA-125:K or equivalent)</li>\r\n	<li>Flash memory: 1 Gb Quadbit SPI flash memory (MT25QL01GBBB)</li>\r\n	<li>1 x 100MHz CMOS oscillator</li>\r\n	<li>USB 3.1 Gen1 @5Gbps (USB Type-C connector)</li>\r\n	<li>Onboard voltage regulators for single power rail operation</li>\r\n	<li>12V DC power supply</li>\r\n	<li>A Push Button for the reset pin</li>\r\n	<li>JTAG header for programming and debugging.</li>\r\n	<li>274 IOs for user-defined purposes</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</div>\r\n', 'SKU: NLFX1002', 874.95, 0, 0, 0, 19, 19, 0),
(134, 'Proteus Kintex 7 USB 3.1 Development Board-XC7K160', 82, 'Active', '								<h2>Description</h2>\r\n\r\n<p>Proteus is an easy to use FPGA Development board featuring the Xilinx Kintex-7 FPGA with 4GB DDR3L SDRAM. This board contains the Xilinx XC7K160T– FBG676 FPGA. The high-speed USB 3.1 interface (USB-C connector) provides fast and easy configuration download to the onboard SPI flash. There is no need for a programmer or special downloader cable to download bitstream to the board. The board features a High Pin Count (HPC), high-speed FMC connector for aiding the addition of additional features to the board by utilizing custom or commercial off-the-shelf daughter boards. Proteus provides user the flexibility of adding their own peripherals through IO Expansion Headers.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Features</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>FPGA Xilinx Kintex-7 XC7K160T– FBG676 package; Speed Grade: 2.</li>\r\n	<li>4GB DDR3L SODIMM SDRAM M471B5173CB0-YK0 or compatible</li>\r\n	<li>128 MB QSPI flash memory (N25Q128A13ESE40E) for Configuration and optional data storage</li>\r\n	<li>1 x 100MHz CMOS oscillator, 1x 150MHz LVDS oscillator for users</li>\r\n	<li>2 x 150MHz LVDS oscillator for GTP</li>\r\n	<li>USB 3.1 Gen 1 @ 5Gbps (USB Type-C connector)</li>\r\n	<li>Onboard voltage regulators for single power rail operation</li>\r\n	<li>12V DC power supply</li>\r\n	<li>Maximum 130 IOs for user-defined purposes on FMC connector</li>\r\n	<li>8 x GTX lanes upto 6.6Gbps on ANSI/VITA 57.1 Standard compliant FMC HPC connector</li>\r\n	<li>Micro SD Card</li>\r\n	<li>A Push Button for the reset pin</li>\r\n	<li>JTAG header for programming and debugging.</li>\r\n	<li>1 RGB LED for custom use.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Applications</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>Product Prototype Development</li>\r\n	<li>Communication Devices Development</li>\r\n	<li>Accelerated Computing Integration</li>\r\n	<li>Development and Testing of Custom embedded processors</li>\r\n	<li>Signal Processing</li>\r\n	<li>Educational tool for Schools and Universities</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n', '								 <table class=\"shop_attributes\">\r\n	<tbody>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>FPGA</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p><a href=\"https://numato.com/fpga/xc7k160t-fbg676\" rel=\"tag\">XC7K160T– FBG676</a>, <a href=\"https://numato.com/fpga/xc7k325t-fbg676-2\" rel=\"tag\">XC7K325T – FBG676</a>, <a href=\"https://numato.com/fpga/xc7k410t-fbg676\" rel=\"tag\">XC7K410T – FBG676</a></p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Memory</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>DDR3-4GBytes</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Number Of GPIOs (Max)</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>130</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Configuration Options</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>JTAG, USB</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Non-Volatile Configuration Storage</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>N25Q128A13ESE40E</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Number of Clock Sources</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>3</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Total Number of GTX</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>8</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Differential Pairs Length Matched</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>Yes</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Communication</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>USB 3.1</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Primary Clock Frequency</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>100MHz</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n	</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n', 4, 'Yes', '2019-04-14', '								<p>Proteus is an easy to use FPGA Development board featuring the Xilinx Kintex-7 FPGA with 4GB DDR3L SDRAM. This board contains the Xilinx XC7K160T– FBG676 FPGA.Other FPGA configurations are available at request.The high-speed USB 3.1 interface (USB-C connector) provides fast and easy configuration download to the onboard SPI flash. There is no need for a programmer or special downloader cable to download bitstream to the board. The board features a High Pin Count (HPC), high-speed FMC connector for aiding the addition of additional features to the board by utilizing custom or commercial off-the-shelf daughter boards. Proteus provides user the flexibility of adding their own peripherals through IO Expansion Headers.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Features</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>FPGA Xilinx Kintex-7 XC7K160T– FBG676 package; Speed Grade: 2.</li>\r\n	<li>4GB DDR3L SODIMM SDRAM M471B5173CB0-YK0 or compatible</li>\r\n	<li>128 MB QSPI flash memory (N25Q128A13ESE40E) for Configuration and optional data storage</li>\r\n	<li>1 x 100MHz CMOS oscillator, 1x 150MHz LVDS oscillator for users</li>\r\n	<li>2 x 150MHz LVDS oscillator for GTP</li>\r\n	<li>USB 3.1 Gen 1 @ 5Gbps (USB Type-C connector)</li>\r\n	<li>Onboard voltage regulators for single power rail operation</li>\r\n	<li>12V DC power supply</li>\r\n	<li>Maximum 130 IOs for user-defined purposes on FMC connector</li>\r\n	<li>8 x GTX lanes upto 6.6Gbps on ANSI/VITA 57.1 Standard compliant FMC HPC connector</li>\r\n	<li>Micro SD Card</li>\r\n	<li>A Push Button for the reset pin</li>\r\n	<li>JTAG header for programming and debugging.</li>\r\n	<li>1 RGB LED for custom use.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n', 'SKU: NLFX1004', 1294.99, 0, 0, 0, 2, 2, 0),
(135, 'Prodigy ZGX Series – 16/32/64 Channel USB/RTU/TCP ', 120, 'Active', '<h2>Description</h2>\r\n\r\n<p>Prodigy ZGX16/ZGX32/ZGX64 is an Digital Input/Output module that supports Modbus RTU over USB and RS485 and Modbus TCP over Ethernet. This product has 16/32/64 GPIO(3.3V)&nbsp; multiplexed with 8/14/32(Max) Analog Inputs that supports. The RS485/USB/Ethernet host interface makes connecting this device to any Windows, Linux, Mac machines or embedded computers such as RPi an easy task. Meanwhile, support for industry standard Modbus protocol makes it easy to use this device with almost any automation software that supports Modbus &ndash; RTU/TCP. ZGX16/ZGX32/ZGX64 when RTU model connected to a host computer, is enumerated as a regular serial port. This alleviates the difficulty of working with USB protocol and offers a transparent interface to access the device. ZGX16/ZGX32/ZGX64 acts as a Modbus slave device at slave address 1. Flexible DIN Rail mounting system allows easy installation and removal with screws. ZGX16/ZGRX32/ZGX64 supports several features such as GPIO Timer, Safety Timer (Watchdog), Programmable Power On State etc..</p>\r\n', '<table class=\"shop_attributes\">\r\n	<tbody>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Number Of GPIOs (Max)</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>16, 32, 64</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>IO Voltage Max</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>3.3V</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Analog Inputs(Max)</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>8, 24, 32</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Analog Input Resolution</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>12 Bits</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Host Interface</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>Ethernet, USB 2.0 CDC</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Warranty</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>Standard&nbsp;</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Package Contents</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>Prodigy ZGX16/ZGX32/ZGX64 &ndash; RTU/TCP x1, USB A to B Cable x1, LAN Cable x1(TCP), 12V Power Supply x1</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n	</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n', 1, 'Yes', '2019-04-14', '<p>Prodigy ZGX16/ZGX32/ZGX64 is an Input/Output module that supports Modbus RTU over USB and RS485 and Modbus TCP over Ethernet. The USB/Ethernet host interface makes connecting this device to any Windows, Linux, Mac machines or embedded computers such as RPi an easy task. Support of industry standard Modbus protocol makes it easy to use this device with almost any automation software that supports Modbus &ndash; RTU/TCP.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Features</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>16/32/64 3.3V GPIOs</li>\r\n	<li>8/14/32 Analog Inputs(Multiplexed with GPIO)</li>\r\n	<li>USB CDC (Serial) interface that works with Windows, Linux, Mac and more. No USB knowledge required!</li>\r\n	<li>Compatible with most automation software in the market that supports Modbus RTU/TCP</li>\r\n	<li>Features such as GPIO Timer, the Watchdog timer for fail-safe operation, Configurable Power On states etc..</li>\r\n	<li>Write your own script or software with help of a large number of sample code provided in various languages</li>\r\n	<li>Detachable screw terminals for easy wiring and replacement</li>\r\n	<li>+12V Power Supply (included)</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n', 'SKU:GPMOD00', 224.99, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0),
(136, '4 Port Gigabit Ethernet FMC Module', 89, 'Active', '<h2>&nbsp;</h2>\r\n\r\n<p>The FMCETHX001 Ethernet Expansion Module features RTL8211E-VB-CG which is a highly integrated Ethernet transceiver that complies with 10Base-T, 100Base-TX, and 1000Base-T IEEE 802.3 standards. It provides all the necessary physical layer functions to transmit and receive Ethernet packets over CAT 5 UTP cable or CAT 3 UTP (10Mbps only) cable.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>The RTL8211E-VB-CG uses state-of-the-art DSP technology and an Analog Front End (AFE) to enable high-speed data transmission and reception over UTP cable. Functions such as Crossover Detection &amp; Auto-Correction, polarity correction, adaptive equalization, cross-talk cancellation, echo cancellation, timing recovery, and error correction are implemented in the RTL8211E-VB-CG to provide robust transmission and reception capabilities at 10Mbps, 100Mbps, or 1000Mbps.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Data transfer between MAC and PHY is via the Reduced Gigabit Media Independent Interface (RGMII) for 1000Base-T, 10Base-T, and 100Base-TX.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Features</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>4 High-Performance 10/100/1000Mbps Ethernet Transceiver</li>\r\n	<li>Dimension: 76.50mm x 69.00mm</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Applications</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>Network Interface Adapter.</li>\r\n	<li>MAU (Media Access Unit).</li>\r\n	<li>CNR (Communication and Network Riser).</li>\r\n	<li>ACR (Advanced Communication Riser).</li>\r\n	<li>Ethernet hub.</li>\r\n	<li>Ethernet switch.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n', '<table class=\"shop_attributes\">\r\n	<tbody>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Weight</th>\r\n			<td>0.6 lbs</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Number of Ethernet Ports</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>4</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Ethernet PHY</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>RTL8211E</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Interface</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>RGMII</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>RGMII Voltage</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>3.3V</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Supported Speeds</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>1000BASE-T, 100BASE-T, 10BASE-T</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Dimensions</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>76.50mm x 69.00mm</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n	</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n', 8, 'Yes', '2019-06-13', '<p>The FMCETHX001 Ethernet Expansion Module features RTL8211E-VB-CG which is a highly integrated Ethernet transceiver that complies with 10Base-T, 100Base-TX, and 1000Base-T IEEE 802.3 standards. It provides all the necessary physical layer functions to transmit and receive Ethernet packets over CAT 5 UTP cable or CAT 3 UTP (10Mbps only) cable.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>The RTL8211E-VB-CG uses state-of-the-art DSP technology and an Analog Front End (AFE) to enable high-speed data transmission and reception over UTP cable. Functions such as Crossover Detection &amp; Auto-Correction, polarity correction, adaptive equalization, cross-talk cancellation, echo cancellation, timing recovery, and error correction are implemented in the RTL8211E-VB-CG to provide robust transmission and reception capabilities at 10Mbps, 100Mbps, or 1000Mbps.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Data transfer between MAC and PHY is via the Reduced Gigabit Media Independent Interface (RGMII) for 1000Base-T, 10Base-T, and 100Base-TX.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Features</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>4 High-Performance 10/100/1000Mbps Ethernet Transceiver</li>\r\n	<li>Dimension: 76.50mm x 69.00mm</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Applications</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>Network Interface Adapter.</li>\r\n	<li>MAU (Media Access Unit).</li>\r\n	<li>CNR (Communication and Network Riser).</li>\r\n	<li>ACR (Advanced Communication Riser).</li>\r\n	<li>Ethernet hub.</li>\r\n	<li>Ethernet switch.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n', 'SKU: NLFMCET001', 372.99, 0, 0, 0, 8, 8, 0),
(137, '128 Channel USB GPIO Module With Analog Inputs', 69, 'Active', '<h2>Description</h2>\r\n\r\n<p>Numato Lab&rsquo;s 128 Channel USB GPIO Module helps to connect real-world devices to your computer easily through USB. No USB specific knowledge is required to set up and use this module. Numato Lab&rsquo;s GPIO devices provide an interface that looks like a Serial Port on your Operating System and thus effectively hiding the complexity of USB. All that you need to operate GPIOs is a standard Serial Terminal Emulator such as HyperTerminal/Teraterm or your favorite programming language such a C/C++, Python, Perl, etc&hellip; Besides providing standard General Purpose IOs, this product has multiple Analog Inputs as well. These Analog inputs can be used to read Analog quantities such as temperature, pressure, etc.. with the help of appropriate sensors.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Features</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>128 TTL(3.3V) compatible GPIOs available</li>\r\n	<li>32 Analog input channels (Pins shared with GPIOs)</li>\r\n	<li>12 Bit Analog input resolution</li>\r\n	<li>All GPIOs can be individually configured as input or output.</li>\r\n	<li>20 mA Source/Sink capacity.</li>\r\n	<li>It can be controlled by using standard serial console applications or custom applications.</li>\r\n	<li>Onboard controller can be reprogrammed for custom applications</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Applications</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>Building automated test fixtures</li>\r\n	<li>Add more IOs and Analog channels to industrial/modular computers</li>\r\n	<li>Add more IOs and Analog channels to Raspberry Pi, Intel Edison, BeagleBone and similar CPU boards</li>\r\n	<li>Add IOs to Android-based systems (Smartphones, Tabs and custom devices)</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Supporting operating systems</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>Windows XP</li>\r\n	<li>Windows 7</li>\r\n	<li>Windows 8/8.1</li>\r\n	<li>Windows 10</li>\r\n	<li>Linux</li>\r\n	<li>Mac OS X</li>\r\n	<li>Android</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><a href=\"https://numato.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/05/128-Channel-USB-GPIO-Module-Wire-Diagram.png\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\"><img alt=\"128 Channel USB GPIO Module - Wire Diagram\" class=\"aligncenter size-large wp-image-10171\" src=\"https://numato.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/05/128-Channel-USB-GPIO-Module-Wire-Diagram-800x1024.png\" style=\"height:819px; width:640px\" /></a></p>\r\n', '<table class=\"shop_attributes\">\r\n	<tbody>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Dimensions</th>\r\n			<td>10.00 x 5.00 x 2.00 in</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Number Of GPIOs (Max)</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>128</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Analog Inputs(Max)</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>32</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Analog Input Resolution</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>12 Bits</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>IO Voltage Max</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>3.3V</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Product Dimensions</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>6.88 x 2.55 x 0.65 in</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Communication</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>USB</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n	</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n', 5, 'Yes', '2019-09-02', '<p>Numato Lab&rsquo;s 128 Channel USB GPIO Module helps to connect real-world devices to your computer easily through USB. No USB specific knowledge is required to set up and use this module.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Features</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>128 TTL (3.3V)compatible GPIOs available.</li>\r\n	<li>32 Analog input channels (Multiplexed with GPIOs)</li>\r\n	<li>12 Bit Analog input resolution</li>\r\n	<li>All GPIOs can be individually configured as input or output.</li>\r\n	<li>It can be controlled by using standard serial console applications or custom applications.</li>\r\n	<li>Onboard controller can be reprogrammed for custom applications</li>\r\n	<li>USB interface with CDC support. As easy as using a serial port, no USB knowledge required</li>\r\n	<li>All IOs available on easy to access screw terminals</li>\r\n	<li>Can be powered from USB or external power supply</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n', 'SKU: GP1280001', 310.99, 0, 0, 0, 5, 4, 1),
(138, '8 Channel USB Relay Module -24V ', 73, 'Active', '<p>URMC8 8 Channel USB Relay Module is great for controlling your devices through USB without any USB protocol knowledge. This modules plugs in to your design seamless. Individual relay can be controlled by simple commands. Numato&rsquo;s URMC8 8 Channel USB Relay Module provides exceptional value for money.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>It has eight on board 24V SPDT relays that can switch up to 10A load.The relays are controlled by USB capable Microchip PIC Microcontroller (PIC18F14K50) and comes with built in firmware that supports simple commands to control relays and read relay status. The board, when attached to a PC/Laptop shows up as a serial port and all you need to control the board is a serial terminal application like HyperTerminal or Putty.<br />\r\n<strong>Features</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>8 on board 24V SPDT Relays.</li>\r\n	<li>7A Maximum Switching Current.</li>\r\n	<li>USB interface with CDC support. As easy as using a serial port, no USB knowledge required.</li>\r\n	<li>Relay contacts available on easy to access screw terminals.</li>\r\n	<li>Digital circuitry can be powered from USB or external power supply.</li>\r\n	<li>Can be controlled by using standard serial console applications or custom applications.</li>\r\n	<li>No vendor specific libraries or APIs required.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Applications</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>Home Automation</li>\r\n	<li>Industrial Automation</li>\r\n	<li>Lighting Control</li>\r\n	<li>Garden Equipment Control</li>\r\n	<li>Test Fixtures</li>\r\n	<li>DIY and Hobby</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Supporting Operating Systems</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>Windows XP and later</li>\r\n	<li>Windows 7 Embedded and later</li>\r\n	<li>Linux</li>\r\n	<li>Mac OS X</li>\r\n	<li>Android</li>\r\n	<li>or any other operating system that supports USB CDC devices.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Languages that can be used for programming</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>C/C++</li>\r\n	<li>Visual Basic (VB6, VB2008, VB2010 express and other editions)</li>\r\n	<li>Visual Basic for Applications (Microsoft Office VBA)</li>\r\n	<li>Perl</li>\r\n	<li>Python</li>\r\n	<li>JAVA</li>\r\n	<li>Android</li>\r\n	<li>Javascript(Node.js)</li>\r\n	<li>And many more&hellip;</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n', '<table class=\"shop_attributes\">\r\n	<tbody>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Weight</th>\r\n			<td>0.31 lbs /140 grams</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Dimensions</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>LxWxH=10&nbsp; cm x 8 cm x 0.2 cm</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Number Of Relays</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>8</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Relay Type</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p><a href=\"https://numato.com/relay-type/mechanical\" rel=\"tag\">Mechanical</a></p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Relay Coil Voltage/Max Relay Current Rating</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>24V/10A</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Communication</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>USB</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n	</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n', 1, 'Yes', '2020-05-10', '<p>URMC8 8 Channel USB Relay Module is great for controlling your devices through USB without any USB protocol knowledge. This modules plugs in to your design seamless. Individual relay can be controlled by simple commands.<br />\r\n<strong>Features</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>8 on board 24V SPDT Relays.</li>\r\n	<li>7A Maximum Switching Current.</li>\r\n	<li>USB interface with CDC support. As easy as using a serial port, no USB knowledge required.</li>\r\n	<li>Relay contacts available on easy to access screw terminals.</li>\r\n	<li>Digital circuitry can be powered from USB or external power supply.</li>\r\n	<li>Can be controlled by using standard serial console applications or custom applications.</li>\r\n	<li>No vendor specific libraries or APIs required.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Applications</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>Home Automation</li>\r\n	<li>Industrial Automation</li>\r\n	<li>Lighting Control</li>\r\n	<li>Garden Equipment Control</li>\r\n	<li>Test Fixtures</li>\r\n	<li>DIY and Hobby</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n', 'RL80001-24V ', 79.95, 0, 0, 5, 47, 36, 11),
(139, '16 Channel USB Relay Module-24V ', 73, 'Active', '<p>URMC16 16 Channel USB Relay Module is great for controlling your devices through USB without any USB protocol knowledge. This modules plugs in to your design seamless. Individual relay can be controlled by simple commands. Numato&rsquo;s URMC16 16 Channel USB Relay Module provides exceptional value for money.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>It has sixteen on board 24V DC relays that can switch up to 10A load.The relays are controlled by USB capable Microchip PIC Microcontroller (PIC18F65J50) and comes with built in firmware that supports simple commands to control relays and read relay status. The board, when attached to a PC/Laptop shows up as a serial port and all you need to control the board is a serial terminal application like HyperTerminal or Putty. This board can easily be controlled by writing simple serial port application in VC++, VB, VBA (Word, Excell etc), Perl, Python etc.<br />\r\n<strong>Features</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>16 on board 24V SPDT Relays.</li>\r\n	<li>7A Maximum Switching Current.</li>\r\n	<li>10 TTL (3.3V)Compatible GPIOs.</li>\r\n	<li>5 Analog Input Channel(Multiplexed with GPIOs).</li>\r\n	<li>10 Bit Analog Input Resolution.</li>\r\n	<li>USB interface with CDC support. As easy as using a serial port, no USB knowledge required.</li>\r\n	<li>2,8mA Maximum IO Source/Sink Current(Depending on the IOs).</li>\r\n	<li>Digital circuitry can be powered from USB or external power supply.</li>\r\n	<li>Can be controlled by using standard serial console applications or custom applications.</li>\r\n	<li>No vendor specific libraries or APIs required.</li>\r\n	<li>Microchip PIC Microcontroller (PIC18F65J50).</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Applications</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>Home Automation</li>\r\n	<li>Industrial Automation</li>\r\n	<li>Lighting Control</li>\r\n	<li>Garden Equipment Control</li>\r\n	<li>Test Fixtures</li>\r\n	<li>DIY and Hobby</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Supporting Operating Systems</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>Windows XP and later</li>\r\n	<li>Windows 7 Embedded and later</li>\r\n	<li>Linux</li>\r\n	<li>Mac OS X</li>\r\n	<li>Android</li>\r\n	<li>or any other operating system that supports USB CDC devices.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Languages that can be used for programming</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>C/C++</li>\r\n	<li>Visual Basic (VB6, VB2008, VB2010 express and other editions)</li>\r\n	<li>Visual Basic for Applications (Microsoft Office VBA)</li>\r\n	<li>Perl</li>\r\n	<li>Python</li>\r\n	<li>JAVA</li>\r\n	<li>Android</li>\r\n	<li>Javascript(Node.js)</li>\r\n	<li>And many more&hellip;</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n', '<table class=\"shop_attributes\">\r\n	<tbody>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Weight</th>\r\n			<td>0.70 lbs</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Dimensions</th>\r\n			<td>10.00 x 5.00 x 2.00 in</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Number Of Relays</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>16</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Relay Type</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p><a href=\"https://numato.com/relay-type/mechanical\" rel=\"tag\">Mechanical</a></p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Relay Coil Voltage/Max Relay Current Rating</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>24V/10A</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Communication</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>USB</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Number Of GPIOs (Max)</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>10</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Analog Inputs</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>5(Multiplexed with IOs)</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Analog Input Resolution</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>10 Bits</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n	</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n', 3, 'Yes', '2020-05-11', '<p>URMC16 16 Channel USB Relay Module is great for controlling your devices through USB without any USB protocol knowledge. This modules plugs in to your design seamless. Individual relay can be controlled by simple commands. Numato&rsquo;s URMC16 16 Channel USB Relay Module provides exceptional value for money.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Features</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>16 on board 24V SPDT Relays.</li>\r\n	<li>7A Maximum Switching Current.</li>\r\n	<li>10 TTL (3.3V)Compatible GPIOs.</li>\r\n	<li>5 Analog Input Channel(Multiplexed with GPIOs).</li>\r\n	<li>10 Bit Analog Input Resolution.</li>\r\n	<li>USB interface with CDC support. As easy as using a serial port, no USB knowledge required.</li>\r\n	<li>2,8mA Maximum IO Source/Sink Current(Depending on the IOs).</li>\r\n	<li>Digital circuitry can be powered from USB or external power supply.</li>\r\n	<li>Can be controlled by using standard serial console applications or custom applications.</li>\r\n	<li>No vendor specific libraries or APIs required.</li>\r\n	<li>Microchip PIC Microcontroller (PIC18F65J50).</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n', 'SKU: RL160001-24V', 118.99, 0, 0, 5, 95, 94, 1),
(140, '32 Channel USB Relay Module -24V', 73, 'Active', '<p>URMC32 32 Channel USB Relay Module is great for controlling your devices through USB without any USB protocol knowledge. This modules plugs in to your design seamless. Individual relay can be controlled by simple commands.Numato`s URMC32 32 Channel USB Relay Module provides exceptional value for money.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>It has thirty two on board 24v DC relays that can switch up to 10A load.The relays are controlled by USB capable Microchip PIC Microcontroller (PIC18F65J50) and comes with built in firmware that supports simple commands to control relays and read relay status. The board, when attached to a PC/Laptop shows up as a serial port and all you need to control the board is a serial terminal application like HyperTerminal or Putty. This board can easily be controlled by writing simple serial port application in VC++, VB, VBA (Word, Excel etc), Perl, Python etc.<br />\r\n<strong>Features</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>32 on board 24V SPDT Relays.</li>\r\n	<li>7A Maximum Switching Current.</li>\r\n	<li>8 TTL (3.3V)Compatible GPIOs.</li>\r\n	<li>5 Analog Input Channel(Multiplexed with GPIOs).</li>\r\n	<li>10 Bit Analog Input Resolution.</li>\r\n	<li>USB interface with CDC support. As easy as using a serial port, no USB knowledge required.</li>\r\n	<li>Relay contacts available on easy to access screw terminals.</li>\r\n	<li>Digital circuitry can be powered from USB or external power supply.</li>\r\n	<li>Can be controlled by using standard serial console applications or custom applications.</li>\r\n	<li>No vendor specific libraries or APIs required.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Applications</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>Home Automation</li>\r\n	<li>Industrial Automation</li>\r\n	<li>Lighting Control</li>\r\n	<li>Garden Equipment Control</li>\r\n	<li>Test Fixtures</li>\r\n	<li>DIY and Hobby</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Supporting Operating Systems</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>Windows XP and later</li>\r\n	<li>Windows 7 Embedded and later</li>\r\n	<li>Linux</li>\r\n	<li>Mac OS X</li>\r\n	<li>Android</li>\r\n	<li>or any other operating system that supports USB CDC devices.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Languages that can be used for programming</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>C/C++</li>\r\n	<li>Visual Basic (VB6, VB2008, VB2010 express and other editions)</li>\r\n	<li>Visual Basic for Applications (Microsoft Office VBA)</li>\r\n	<li>Perl</li>\r\n	<li>Python</li>\r\n	<li>JAVA</li>\r\n	<li>Android</li>\r\n	<li>Javascript(Node.js)</li>\r\n	<li>And many more&hellip;</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n', '<table class=\"shop_attributes\">\r\n	<tbody>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Weight</th>\r\n			<td>1.50 lbs</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Dimensions</th>\r\n			<td>12.00 x 9.00 x 2.00 in</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Number Of Relays</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>32</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Relay Type</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p><a href=\"https://numato.com/relay-type/mechanical\" rel=\"tag\">Mechanical</a></p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Relay Coil Voltage / Max Relay Current Rating</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>24V / 10A&nbsp;&nbsp;</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Number Of GPIOs (Max)</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>8</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Analog Inputs</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>5(Multiplexed with IOs)</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Analog Input Resolution</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>10 Bits</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Communication</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>USB</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n	</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n', 1, 'Yes', '2020-05-11', '<p>URMC32 32 Channel USB Relay Module is great for controlling your devices through USB without any USB protocol knowledge. This modules plugs in to your design seamless. Individual relay can be controlled by simple commands.Numato`s URMC32 32 Channel USB Relay Module provides exceptional value for money.<br />\r\n<strong>Features</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>32 on board 24V SPDT Relays.</li>\r\n	<li>7A Maximum Switching Current.</li>\r\n	<li>8 TTL (3.3V)Compatible GPIOs.</li>\r\n	<li>5 Analog Input Channel(Multiplexed with GPIOs).</li>\r\n	<li>10 Bit Analog Input Resolution.</li>\r\n	<li>USB interface with CDC support. As easy as using a serial port, no USB knowledge required.</li>\r\n	<li>Relay contacts available on easy to access screw terminals.</li>\r\n	<li>Digital circuitry can be powered from USB or external power supply.</li>\r\n	<li>Can be controlled by using standard serial console applications or custom applications.</li>\r\n	<li>No vendor specific libraries or APIs required.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n', 'SKU: RL320001-24V', 209.95, 0, 0, 0, 103, 99, 4),
(141, '16 Channel Ethernet Relay Module-24V', 75, 'Active', '<p>Numato Lab 16 Channel Ethernet Relay module allows controlling electrical devices remotely through Ethernet. This is very helpful in those situations where the device that needs to be controlled is located far from the PC and thus can not run USB cable. Numato Lab Ethernet Relay modules are designed to be very easy to setup and use.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>This product has 16 on board relays and 8 GPIOs. Each relay/gpio can be individually controlled through the built in easy to use web interface or through any popular terminal emulator that supports TELNET protocol. All GPIOs can be used as analog inputs (10 bits resolution) as well. Each 16 Channel Ethernet Relay module is shipped with unique MAC address. These devices also supports assigning and retrieving custom identification string that can be used for identifying individual devices when there are large number of devices connected on the same network. All relay terminals are available on screw terminals which makes connecting external devices very easy.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Features</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>Microcontroller: Microchip PIC18F97J60(1-Mbit Flash Microcontroller with 10Mbps Ethernet communication peripheral)</li>\r\n	<li>Memory: Microchip 25LC1024 serial EEPROM provides 1024 Kbits of storage for both web pages and nonvolatile configuration options</li>\r\n	<li>MAC Address: Separate Serial EEPROM(24AA02E48) with Globally Unique value used as MAC Address</li>\r\n	<li>Reset Jumper: To reset the firmware of board to factory defaults</li>\r\n	<li>Password protected Web console and Telnet communication interface</li>\r\n	<li>LED indication for Power and individual relay status</li>\r\n	<li>Relay: 16 SPDT Relays with individual LEDs for status</li>\r\n	<li>GPIO: 8 GPIOs, each can be configured as analog inputs</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Applications</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>Home Automation</li>\r\n	<li>Lighting Control</li>\r\n	<li>Garden Equipment Control</li>\r\n	<li>Industrial Automation</li>\r\n	<li>Test Fixtures</li>\r\n	<li>DIY and Hobby</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n', '<table class=\"shop_attributes\">\r\n	<tbody>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Weight</th>\r\n			<td>0.80 lbs</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Dimensions</th>\r\n			<td>10.00 x 5.00 x 2.00 in</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Number of Relays</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>16</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Relay Type</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p><a href=\"https://numato.com/relay-type/mechanical\" rel=\"tag\">Mechanical</a></p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Relay Coil Voltage / Max Relay Current Rating</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>24V / 10A</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Number Of GPIOs (Max)</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>8</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Analog Inputs</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>8 (Multiplexed with IOs)</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Analog Input Resolution</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>10 Bits</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Communication</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>10BASE-T Ethernet</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>User Interface</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p><a href=\"https://numato.com/user-interface/htmlweb\" rel=\"tag\">HTML/Web</a>,&nbsp;<a href=\"https://numato.com/user-interface/telnet\" rel=\"tag\">TELNET</a></p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n	</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n', 2, 'Yes', '2020-05-11', '<p>Numato Lab 16 Channel Ethernet Relay module allows controlling electrical devices remotely through Ethernet. This is very helpful in those situations where the device that needs to be controlled is located far from the PC and thus can not run USB cable. Numato Lab Ethernet Relay modules are designed to be very easy to setup and use.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Features</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>16 SPDT Relays with individual LEDs for status.</li>\r\n	<li>7A Maximum Switching Current.</li>\r\n	<li>8 TTL (3.3V)Compatible GPIOs.</li>\r\n	<li>8 Analog Input Channel(Multiplexed with GPIOs).</li>\r\n	<li>10 Bit Analog Input Resolution.</li>\r\n	<li>Unique MAC Address.</li>\r\n	<li>10BASE-T Ethernet Communication.</li>\r\n	<li>Password protected Web console and Telnet communication interface.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n', 'SKU: 16ETHRL001-24V', 142.79, 0, 0, 0, 19, 14, 5),
(142, '8 Channel Ethernet Relay Module-24V', 75, 'Active', '<p>Numato Lab 8 Channel Ethernet Relay module allows controlling electrical devices remotely through Ethernet using easy to use Web interface or TELNET interface and can be programmed using almost any language. &nbsp;With&nbsp;8 Relays that supports up to 10A, 10 Digital IOs and 10 multiplexed Analog inputs, this product avoids the need of buying additional Digital IO and Analog input modules. This product works with any operating system that has a browser or has a TELNET tool. This includes Windows, Linux, Mac OSX, Android etc..</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Each relay/gpio can be individually controlled through the built in easy to use web interface or through any popular terminal emulator that supports TELNET protocol. The 8 Channel Ethernet Relay module is shipped with unique MAC address. These devices also supports assigning and retrieving custom identification string that can be used for identifying individual devices when there are large number of devices connected on the same network. All relay terminals are available on screw terminals which makes connecting external devices very easy.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Features</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>Eight relays that can handle up to 10A</li>\r\n	<li>10 Digital IOs and 10 Analog inputs (multiplexed with Digital IOs)</li>\r\n	<li>10bit ADC resolution for Analog Inputs</li>\r\n	<li>Plugs directly to the router or PC</li>\r\n	<li>Supports DHCP and static IP</li>\r\n	<li>Easy to use Web interface with point and click Relay/GPIO control (please see pictures below)</li>\r\n	<li>Human readable commands over TELNET. Works with any off the shelf TENET client(please see pictures below)</li>\r\n	<li>Programmable with almost any language</li>\r\n	<li>Built in unique MAC address and configurable identification string</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Applications</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>Automated test fixtures</li>\r\n	<li>Home and industrial automation</li>\r\n	<li>Remote device monitoring and control</li>\r\n	<li>Remote data logging</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><img alt=\"ethernetrelay8status\" class=\"__mce_add_custom__\" src=\"https://numato.com/wp-content/uploads/2017/07/ethernetrelay8status.png\" style=\"height:346px; width:450px\" title=\"ethernetrelay8status\" /></p>\r\n\r\n<p>Easy to use web interface with point and click to control relays and GPIOs. A common&nbsp;<a href=\"https://cdn3.bigcommerce.com/s-hziwvf/product_images/uploaded_images/ethernetrelay8statuspage.png?t=1455655123\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">status page</a>displays status of all relays and GPIOs in one location. This makes monitoring the device status without moving to different pages. Dedicated interfaces for Relays and GPIOs for configuration and control. Each relay can be controlled independantly by simply clicking the toggle button. Individual GPIOs can be configured as Digital Input, Digitl Output or Analog input. When a GPIO is configured as Digital Input or Analog Input, that GPIO is monitored periodically and current status is updated immediately.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><img alt=\"ethernetrelay8-mactelnetsmall\" class=\"__mce_add_custom__\" src=\"https://numato.com/wp-content/uploads/2017/07/ethernetrelay8-mactelnetsmall.png\" style=\"height:346px; width:450px\" title=\"ethernetrelay8-mactelnetsmall\" />For those who wants finer control, this product offers a TELNET interface. The TELNET interface helps controlling individual relays and GPIOs using any off the shelf TELNET client programs such as TeraTerm, Putty, HyperTerminal or even with built in TELNET clients shipped with various operating systems such as Windows, Linux and Mac OSX. The interface uses simple human readable commands that can be executed from a command prompt just like entering commands at Windows or Linux command prompt. Response from the device if any, will be displayed in human readable text.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><img alt=\"ethernetrelay8python\" class=\"__mce_add_custom__\" src=\"https://numato.com/wp-content/uploads/2017/07/ethernetrelay8python.png\" style=\"height:195px; width:450px\" title=\"ethernetrelay8python\" />Looking for automation or want to control relays and GPIOs from your custom application? We&rsquo;ve got that covered too. TELNET is a widely supported open protocol and it is easy to write a custom script or applicaton by using TELNET library provided by most programming platforms or even by using raw TCP/IP sockets. For example, connecting to 8 Channel Ethernet Relay Module and &nbsp;reading version information using Python 3.x can be accomplished in less than a dozen lines of code.</p>\r\n', '<table class=\"shop_attributes\">\r\n	<tbody>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Weight</th>\r\n			<td>0.55 lbs</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Dimensions</th>\r\n			<td>10.00 x 5.00 x 2.00 in</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Number Of Relays</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>8</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Relay Type</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p><a href=\"https://numato.com/relay-type/mechanical\" rel=\"tag\">Mechanical</a></p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Relay Coil Voltage / Max Relay Current Rating</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>24V / 10A</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Number Of GPIOs (Max)</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>10</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Analog Inputs</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>10 (Multiplexed with IOs)</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Analog Input Resolution</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>10 Bits</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Communication</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>10BASE-T Ethernet</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>User Interface</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p><a href=\"https://numato.com/user-interface/htmlweb\" rel=\"tag\">HTML/Web</a>,&nbsp;<a href=\"https://numato.com/user-interface/telnet\" rel=\"tag\">TELNET</a></p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n	</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n', 1, 'Yes', '2020-05-11', '<p>Numato Lab 8 Channel Ethernet Relay module allows controlling electrical devices remotely through Ethernet using easy to use Web interface or TELNET interface and can be programmed using almost any language. &nbsp;With&nbsp;8 Relays that supports up to 10A, 10 Digital IOs and 10 multiplexed Analog inputs, this product avoids the need of buying additional Digital IO and Analog input modules. This product works with any operating system that has a browser or has a TELNET tool. This includes Windows, Linux, Mac OSX, Android etc..</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Features</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>8 SPDT Relays with individual LEDs for status.</li>\r\n	<li>7A Maximum Switching Current.</li>\r\n	<li>10 TTL (3.3V)Compatible GPIOs.</li>\r\n	<li>10 Analog Input Channel(Multiplexed with GPIOs).</li>\r\n	<li>10 Bit Analog Input Resolution.</li>\r\n	<li>Unique MAC Address.</li>\r\n	<li>10BASE-T Ethernet Communication.</li>\r\n	<li>Password protected Web console and Telnet communication interface.</li>\r\n	<li>Supports DHCP and static IP</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n', 'SKU: 8ETHRL001-24V', 123.99, 0, 0, 1, 8, 7, 1);
INSERT INTO `tbl_product` (`product_id`, `product_name`, `product_category_id`, `product_status`, `product_description`, `product_specification`, `priorty`, `display_flag`, `product_entry_date`, `product_details`, `product_code`, `product_amt`, `product_tax`, `product_discount`, `product_threshold`, `total_product`, `total_sold`, `total_remaining`) VALUES
(143, '32 Channel Ethernet Relay Module-24V', 75, 'Active', '<p>Numato Lab 32 Channel Ethernet Relay module allows controlling electrical devices remotely through Ethernet. This is very helpful in those situations where the device that needs to be controlled is located far from the PC and thus can not run USB cable. Numato Lab Ethernet Relay modules are designed to be very easy to setup and use.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>This product has 32 on board relays and 8 GPIOs. Each relay/gpio can be individually controlled through the built in easy to use web interface or through any popular terminal emulator that supports TELNET protocol. All GPIOs can be used as analog inputs (10 bits resolution) as well. Each 32 Channel Ethernet Relay module is shipped with unique MAC address. These devices also supports assigning and retrieving custom identification string that can be used for identifying individual devices when there are large number of devices connected on the same network. All relay terminals are available on screw terminals which makes connecting external devices very easy.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Features</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>Microcontroller: Microchip PIC18F97J60(1-Mbit Flash Microcontroller with 10Mbps Ethernet communication peripheral)</li>\r\n	<li>Memory: Microchip 25LC1024 serial EEPROM provides 1024 Kbits of storage for both web pages and nonvolatile configuration options</li>\r\n	<li>MAC Address: Separate Serial EEPROM(24AA02E48) with Globally Unique value used as MAC Address</li>\r\n	<li>Reset Jumper: To reset the firmware of board to factory defaults</li>\r\n	<li>Password protected Web console and Telnet communication interface</li>\r\n	<li>LED indication for Power and individual relay status</li>\r\n	<li>Relay: 32 SPDT Relays with individual LEDs for status</li>\r\n	<li>GPIO: 8 GPIOs, each can be configured as analog inputs</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Applications</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>Home Automation</li>\r\n	<li>Lighting Control</li>\r\n	<li>Garden Equipment Control</li>\r\n	<li>Industrial Automation</li>\r\n	<li>Test Fixtures</li>\r\n	<li>DIY and Hobby</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n', '<table class=\"shop_attributes\">\r\n	<tbody>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Weight</th>\r\n			<td>1.50 lbs</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Dimensions</th>\r\n			<td>12.00 x 9.00 x 2.00 in</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Number Of Relays</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>32</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Relay Type</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p><a href=\"https://numato.com/relay-type/mechanical\" rel=\"tag\">Mechanical</a></p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Relay Coil Voltage / Max Relay Current Rating</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>24V / 10A</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Number Of GPIOs (Max)</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>8</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Analog Inputs</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>8 (Multiplexed with IOs)</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Analog Input Resolution</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>10 Bits</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Communication</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>10BASE-T Ethernet</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>User Interface</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p><a href=\"https://numato.com/user-interface/htmlweb\" rel=\"tag\">HTML/Web</a>,&nbsp;<a href=\"https://numato.com/user-interface/telnet\" rel=\"tag\">TELNET</a></p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n	</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n', 1, 'Yes', '2020-05-11', '<p>Numato Lab 32 Channel Ethernet Relay module allows controlling electrical devices remotely through Ethernet. This is very helpful in those situations where the device that needs to be controlled is located far from the PC and thus can not run USB cable. Numato Lab Ethernet Relay modules are designed to be very easy to setup and use.<br />\r\n<strong>Features</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>32 SPDT Relays with individual LEDs for status.</li>\r\n	<li>7A Maximum Switching Current.</li>\r\n	<li>8 TTL (3.3V)Compatible GPIOs.</li>\r\n	<li>8 Analog Input Channel(Multiplexed with GPIOs).</li>\r\n	<li>10 Bit Analog Input Resolution.</li>\r\n	<li>Unique MAC Address.</li>\r\n	<li>10BASE-T Ethernet Communication.</li>\r\n	<li>Password protected Web console and Telnet communication interface.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n', 'SKU: 32ETHRL001-24V', 234.95, 0, 0, 0, 21, 20, 1),
(144, '8 Channel USB GPIO Module - GP80001EP', 69, 'Active', '<p>Numato Lab&rsquo;s 8 Channel USB GPIO Module helps connecting real world devices to your computer easily through USB. No USB specific knowledge is required to set up and use this module. Numato Lab&rsquo;s GPIO devices provide an interface that looks like a Serial Port on your Operating System and thus effectively hiding the complexity of USB. All that you need to operate GPIOs is a standard Serial Terminal Emulator such as HyperTerminal/Teraterm or your favorite programming language such a C/C++, Python, Perl etc&hellip; Besides providing standard General Purpose IOs, this product has multiple Analog Inputs as well. These Analog inputs can be used to read Analog quantities such as temperature, pressure etc.. with the help of appropriate sensors.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Features</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>8 TTL compatible GPIOs available</li>\r\n	<li>6 Analog input channels (Multiplexed with GPIOs)</li>\r\n	<li>10 Bit Analog input resolution</li>\r\n	<li>All GPIOs can be individually configured as input or output.</li>\r\n	<li>Can be controlled by using standard serial console applications or custom applications.</li>\r\n	<li>On board controller can be reprogrammed for custom applications</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Applications</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>Building automated test fixtures</li>\r\n	<li>Add more IOs and Analog channels to industrial/modular computers</li>\r\n	<li>Add more IOs and Analog channels to Raspberry Pi, Intel Edison, BeagleBone and similar CPU boards</li>\r\n	<li>Add IOs to Android based systems (Smartphones, Tabs and custom devices)</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Supported operating systems</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>Windows XP</li>\r\n	<li>Windows 7</li>\r\n	<li>Windows 8/8.1</li>\r\n	<li>Windows 10</li>\r\n	<li>Linux</li>\r\n	<li>Mac OS X</li>\r\n	<li>Android</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Why Numato Lab&rsquo;s 8 Channel USB GPIO module With Analog Inputs?</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p>Building computer or Smartphone controlled devices wasn&rsquo;t always the easiest thing to do. Specialized knowledge in hardware and software were often needed to get even simplest of the things done. But what could you do if you can control devices from your Windows/Linux/Mac/Android device in less than five minutes? The possibilities are unlimited. Build a computer controlled security system, an automated test fixture, a computer controlled garage door and much more with Numato Lab&rsquo;s USB GPIO devices!</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Numato Lab&rsquo;s USB GPIO devices are designed to help customers to get started very easily and keep everything as simple as possible even when building complex systems. This goal is achieved by a few carefully designed features below.</p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li><a href=\"https://numato.com/product/8-channel-usb-gpio-module-with-analog-inputs#simpleusbinterface\">Simple USB-Serial interface</a></li>\r\n	<li><a href=\"https://numato.com/product/8-channel-usb-gpio-module-with-analog-inputs#EasyCommands\">Simple and easy to use commands&nbsp;</a></li>\r\n	<li><a href=\"https://numato.com/product/8-channel-usb-gpio-module-with-analog-inputs#NoThirdPartyAPI\">No product specific libraries or APIs</a></li>\r\n	<li><a href=\"https://numato.com/product/8-channel-usb-gpio-module-with-analog-inputs#largeNumberOfLanguages\">Large verity of supported programming languages</a></li>\r\n	<li><a href=\"https://numato.com/product/8-channel-usb-gpio-module-with-analog-inputs#LargeSampleCode\">Huge collection of sample code to help you get started</a></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><strong><a name=\"simpleusbinterface\"></a><img alt=\"usbgpio8 windows device manager\" class=\"alignleft size-medium wp-image-2681\" src=\"https://numato.com/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/usbgpio8-windows-device-manager-300x154.png\" style=\"height:154px; width:300px\" title=\"usbgpio8 windows device manager\" />Simple USB-Serial interface</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p>Numato Lab&rsquo;s USB GPIO devices present themselves to the Operating System as a serial port. This means all the complexity related to USB are abstracted out and you will be using the device as if it is a simple serial port. This serial port interface can be accessed using a standard Serial Terminal Emulator software such as HyperTerminal, Teraterm, PUTTY or through your own custom script or application that can be written using one of more than a dozen different programming languages. On Windows the device will be visible in the Device manager as a normal serial port. On Linux and Mac, the device will be listed under /dev directory, usually with a name in the format ttyACMx. On Android, the device can be enumerated and controlled using packages provided by Android such as UsbManager, UsbDevice, UsbConfiguration, UsbDevice, UsbInterface etc&hellip;</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong><a name=\"EasyCommands\"></a><img alt=\"usbgpio8 putty terminal\" class=\"alignright size-medium wp-image-2680\" src=\"https://numato.com/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/usbgpio8-putty-terminal-300x152.png\" style=\"height:152px; width:300px\" title=\"usbgpio8 putty terminal\" />Easy to use commands</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p>Numato Lab&rsquo;s USB GPIO devices support simple and human readable commands to control the device (For example, command &ldquo;gpio on 1&rdquo; will turn ON GPIO1). These commands can be manually typed in through a standard Serial&nbsp;Terminal Emulator such as HyperTerminal or Teraterm and can also be sent from a custom application or script. Custom applications or scripts can be used to automate the interaction with the device and implement logic such as conditional device control based on input values or timer etc&hellip;</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong><a name=\"NoThirdPartyAPI\"></a>No product specific libraries or APIs</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p>Unlike many other USB GPIO devices, Numato Lab&rsquo;s GPIO devices does not depend on any third party library of API. The device can be accessed by using the serial port access APIs natively provided by the Operating System where available. That being said, libraries do exist on many platforms that may make accessing devices easier. But their use is fully optional.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong><a name=\"largeNumberOfLanguages\"></a>Large number of supported programming languages</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p>If the particular language of your choice supports serial ports, it should be possible to use that language to write custom script or application on an Operating System that support USB Serial Ports. Currently Numato Lab&rsquo;s GPIO devices are tested on different Windows version, Linux, Mac and Android. A script or application can be written using but not limited to C, C++, Visual Basic, Java, C#, AutoHotkey, VBA (MS Excel, MS Word etc&hellip;), Node.js, Autoit, Labview, Perl, Java (Android) etc..</p>\r\n\r\n<div><strong><a name=\"LargeSampleCode\"></a><img alt=\"visualbasic\" class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-2682\" src=\"https://numato.com/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/visualbasic.png\" style=\"height:80px; width:80px\" title=\"visualbasic\" /><img alt=\"python\" class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-2679\" src=\"https://numato.com/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/python.png\" style=\"height:80px; width:81px\" title=\"python\" /><img alt=\"perlxcf\" class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-2678\" src=\"https://numato.com/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/perlxcf.png\" style=\"height:80px; width:178px\" title=\"perlxcf\" /><img alt=\"node.js\" class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-2677\" src=\"https://numato.com/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/node.js.png\" style=\"height:80px; width:296px\" title=\"node.js\" /><img alt=\"microsoft-word\" class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-2676\" src=\"https://numato.com/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/microsoft-word.png\" style=\"height:80px; width:81px\" title=\"microsoft-word\" /><img alt=\"microsoft-excel\" class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-2675\" src=\"https://numato.com/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/microsoft-excel.png\" style=\"height:80px; width:81px\" title=\"microsoft-excel\" /><img alt=\"java\" class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-2674\" src=\"https://numato.com/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/java.png\" style=\"height:80px; width:97px\" title=\"java\" /><img alt=\"csharp\" class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-2673\" src=\"https://numato.com/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/csharp.png\" style=\"height:80px; width:137px\" title=\"csharp\" /><img alt=\"c-c\" class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-2672\" src=\"https://numato.com/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/c-c-.png\" style=\"height:80px; width:262px\" title=\"c-c\" /><img alt=\"android\" class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-2671\" src=\"https://numato.com/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/android.png\" style=\"height:80px; width:80px\" title=\"android\" /></strong></div>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Large collection of sample code</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p>Numato Lab provides dozens of sample code/projects that can be used to kick start your development (Please see Sample Code tab).</p>\r\n', '<table class=\"shop_attributes\">\r\n	<tbody>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Weight</th>\r\n			<td>0.10 lbs</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Dimensions</th>\r\n			<td>5.00 x 3.00 x 2.00 in</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Number Of GPIOs (Max)</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>8</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Analog Inputs</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>6</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Host Interface</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>USB 2.0 CDC</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Analog Input Resolution</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>10 Bits</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Multiplexed Analog Inputs</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>Yes, with Digital IOs</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Package Contents</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>8 Channel USB GPIO Module With Analog Inputs &ndash; 1Unit</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Warranty</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p><a href=\"https://numato.com/warranty/standard\" rel=\"tag\">Standard</a></p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>RoHS</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>Yes</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>SKU</th>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>GP80001</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n	</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n', 4, 'Yes', '2020-05-30', '<p>Numato Lab&rsquo;s 8 Channel USB GPIO Module helps connecting real world devices to your computer easily through USB. No USB specific knowledge is required to set up and use this module. Numato Lab&rsquo;s GPIO devices provide an interface that looks like a Serial Port on your Operating System and thus effectively hiding the complexity of USB. All that you need to operate GPIOs is a standard Serial Terminal Emulator such as HyperTerminal/Teraterm or your favorite programming language such a C/C++, Python, Perl etc&hellip; Besides providing standard General Purpose IOs, this product has multiple Analog Inputs as well. These Analog inputs can be used to read Analog quantities such as temperature, pressure etc.. with the help of appropriate sensors.Product SKU &ndash;&nbsp;GP80001</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Features</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>8 TTL compatible GPIOs available</li>\r\n	<li>6 Analog input channels (Multiplexed with GPIOs)</li>\r\n	<li>10 Bit Analog input resolution</li>\r\n	<li>All GPIOs can be individually configured as input or output.</li>\r\n	<li>Can be controlled by using standard serial console applications or custom applications.</li>\r\n	<li>On board controller can be reprogrammed for custom applications</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Applications</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>Building automated test fixtures</li>\r\n	<li>Add more IOs and Analog channels to industrial/modular computers</li>\r\n	<li>Add more IOs and Analog channels to Raspberry Pi, Intel Edison, BeagleBone and similar CPU boards</li>\r\n	<li>Add IOs to Android based systems (Smartphones, Tabs and custom devices)</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n', 'SKU: GP80001-Encloser', 37.99, 0, 0, 5, 149, 145, 4),
(148, 'TapNLink NFC', 169, 'Active', '<p><strong>TapNLink NFC (Type5) module for local connection of mobiles to microcontroller-based electronic systems.</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p>TapNLink NFC modules provide a contactless interface&nbsp;for linking mobile devices to equipment and appliances. Using TapNLink&nbsp;<a href=\"https://www.iotize.com/nfc-3-stroke-configuration.html\">3-stroke configuration</a>, users&nbsp;interact with appliances from an app on their mobile in three intuitive steps:&nbsp;1) tap to launch the app and retrieve current parameters, 2) modify parameters in the app, and 3) tap again to update the&nbsp;parameters.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>TapNLink connects directly to a systems&#39; microcontroller or circuitry. Thanks to TapNLink&#39;s power optimization and Energy Harvesting mode, it can be powed either entirely by a mobile device during NFC communication, or by the target system&#39;s power supply.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>All TapNLink products are easily configured to control access to data in&nbsp;the target system by different types of users. TapNLink facilitates rapid creation of user interfaces that run on Android, iOS and&nbsp;Windows-based mobile devices.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Wireless Channels</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>Near Field Communication (NFC) Type5 tag (ISO/IEC 15693) supporting\r\n	<ul>\r\n		<li>Bi-directional proximity communication with mobiles</li>\r\n		<li>Power by Energy Harvesting from the mobile</li>\r\n	</ul>\r\n	</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Supported Target Connections</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>Serial interface with Software Secure Serial Port (S3P) protocol</li>\r\n	<li>Serial interface with ARM SWD debug protocol</li>\r\n	<li>UART with Modbus protocol</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Mobile Platform Support&nbsp;</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>HTML5 web apps&nbsp;(Android, iOS)</li>\r\n	<li>API for Cordova (Android, iOS, Windows 10)</li>\r\n	<li>Java (Android, iOS native)</li>\r\n	<li>Auto-app generator for Android and iOS mobiles</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Security</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>Configurable access profiles&nbsp;</li>\r\n	<li>Configurable, encrypted passwords</li>\r\n	<li>AES-128/256 module-level data encryption</li>\r\n	<li>Configurable secure pairing with NFC</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Mechanical Charateristics</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>Dimensions: L 38mm x W 28mm x&nbsp; H 3mm</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Packaging Options</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>Bare board (default)</li>\r\n	<li>Optional ABS plastic casing (IP44)</li>\r\n	<li>Optional silcone resin (IP65)</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Compliance</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>CE (Europe), FCC (USA), IC (Canada).</li>\r\n	<li>REACH</li>\r\n	<li>RoHS</li>\r\n	<li>WEEE</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Ordering Information</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>SKU: TnL-FIT203</li>\r\n	<li>MOQ: 1&nbsp;modules</li>\r\n	<li>Prices include:\r\n	<ul>\r\n		<li>TapNLink modules pre-qualified, pre-programmed and ready to configure</li>\r\n		<li>IoTize Studio configuration and testing software</li>\r\n		<li>Software for HMI&nbsp;on mobile devices (iOS, Android, Windows 10)</li>\r\n		<li>IoTize Cloud MQTT infrastructure (open source)</li>\r\n	</ul>\r\n	</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Associated Evaluation Kit :&nbsp;</strong></p>\r\n', '<p><strong>Mechanical Charateristics</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>Dimensions: L 38mm x W 28mm x&nbsp; H 3mm</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Packaging Options</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>Bare board (default)</li>\r\n	<li>Optional ABS plastic casing (IP44)</li>\r\n	<li>Optional silcone resin (IP65)</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Electrical Characteristics</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>Input voltage: 2.3V to 3.6V</li>\r\n	<li>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Typical&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Energy Harvesting*<br />\r\n	Standby:&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; 1 &micro;A&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; 0<br />\r\n	Tx/Rx:&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;1 mA&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;0<br />\r\n	<br />\r\n	* Up to 3 mA can be relayed to the target application during energy harvesting from an NFC mobile device.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Temperature Range</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>-20&deg;C, +55&deg;C</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n', 1, 'Yes', '2021-01-04', '<p><strong>TapNLink NFC (Type5) module for local connection of mobiles to microcontroller-based electronic systems.</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p>TapNLink NFC modules provide a contactless interface&nbsp;for linking mobile devices to equipment and appliances. Using TapNLink&nbsp;<a href=\"https://www.iotize.com/nfc-3-stroke-configuration.html\">3-stroke configuration</a>, users&nbsp;interact with appliances from an app on their mobile in three intuitive steps:&nbsp;1) tap to launch the app and retrieve current parameters, 2) modify parameters in the app, and 3) tap again to update the&nbsp;parameters.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>TapNLink connects directly to a systems&#39; microcontroller or circuitry. Thanks to TapNLink&#39;s power optimization and Energy Harvesting mode, it can be powed either entirely by a mobile device during NFC communication, or by the target system&#39;s power supply.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>All TapNLink products are easily configured to control access to data in&nbsp;the target system by different types of users. TapNLink facilitates rapid creation of user interfaces that run on Android, iOS and&nbsp;Windows-based mobile devices.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Wireless Channels</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>Near Field Communication (NFC) Type5 tag (ISO/IEC 15693) supporting\r\n	<ul>\r\n		<li>Bi-directional proximity communication with mobiles</li>\r\n		<li>Power by Energy Harvesting from the mobile</li>\r\n	</ul>\r\n	</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Supported Target Connections</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>Serial interface with Software Secure Serial Port (S3P) protocol</li>\r\n	<li>Serial interface with ARM SWD debug protocol</li>\r\n	<li>UART with Modbus protocol</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Mobile Platform Support&nbsp;</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>HTML5 web apps&nbsp;(Android, iOS)</li>\r\n	<li>API for Cordova (Android, iOS, Windows 10)</li>\r\n	<li>Java (Android, iOS native)</li>\r\n	<li>Auto-app generator for Android and iOS mobiles</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Security</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>Configurable access profiles&nbsp;</li>\r\n	<li>Configurable, encrypted passwords</li>\r\n	<li>AES-128/256 module-level data encryption</li>\r\n	<li>Configurable secure pairing with NFC</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Compliance</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>CE (Europe), FCC (USA), IC (Canada).</li>\r\n	<li>REACH</li>\r\n	<li>RoHS</li>\r\n	<li>WEEE</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Ordering Information</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>SKU: TnL-FIT203</li>\r\n	<li>MOQ: 1&nbsp;modules</li>\r\n	<li>Prices include:\r\n	<ul>\r\n		<li>TapNLink modules pre-qualified, pre-programmed and ready to configure</li>\r\n		<li>IoTize Studio configuration and testing software</li>\r\n		<li>Software for HMI&nbsp;on mobile devices (iOS, Android, Windows 10)</li>\r\n		<li>IoTize Cloud MQTT infrastructure (open source)</li>\r\n	</ul>\r\n	</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Associated Evaluation Kit :&nbsp;</strong></p>\r\n', 'SKU: TnL-FIT203', 24.95, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 0),
(149, 'TapNLink NFC , BLE', 169, 'Active', '<p><strong>TapNLink BLE, NFC (Type5) module for local connection of mobiles to microcontroller-based electronic systems.</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p>TapNLink modules provide wireless interfaces for linking electronic systems to mobile devices and to the Cloud. TapNLink connects directly to the target system&#39;s microcontroller. It integrates into and is powered by the target system.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>All TapNLink products are easily configured to control access by different types of users to data in&nbsp;the target system. TapNLink facilitates rapid creation of Human Machine Interfaces (HMI) that run on Android, iOS and&nbsp;Windows&nbsp;mobiles. HMI apps are easily customized for different users&nbsp;and can be deployed and updated to keep pace with evolving system requirements&nbsp;and user needs.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Wireless Channels</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>Near Field Communication (NFC) Type5 tag (ISO/IEC 15693)</li>\r\n	<li>Bluetooth Low Energy (BLE) 4.1</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Supported Target Connections</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>Serial interface with Software Secure Serial Port (S3P) protocol</li>\r\n	<li>Serial interface with ARM SWD debug protocol</li>\r\n	<li>UART with Modbus protocol</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Mobile Platform Support&nbsp;</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>HTML5 web apps&nbsp;(Android, iOS)</li>\r\n	<li>API for Cordova (Android, iOS, Windows 10)&nbsp;</li>\r\n	<li>Java (Android, iOS native)</li>\r\n	<li>Auto-app generator for Android and iOS mobiles</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Security</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>Configurable access profiles&nbsp;</li>\r\n	<li>Configurable, encrypted passwords</li>\r\n	<li>AES-128/256 module-level data encryption</li>\r\n	<li>Configurable secure pairing with NFC</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Compliance</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>CE (Europe), FCC (USA), IC (Canada).</li>\r\n	<li>REACH</li>\r\n	<li>RoHS</li>\r\n	<li>WEEE</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Ordering Information</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>SKU: TnL-FIR103</li>\r\n	<li>MOQ: 1</li>\r\n	<li>Prices include:\r\n	<ul>\r\n		<li>TapNLink modules pre-qualified, pre-programmed and ready to configure</li>\r\n		<li>IoTize Studio configuration and testing software</li>\r\n		<li>Software for HMI&nbsp;on mobile devices (iOS, Android, Windows 10)</li>\r\n		<li>IoTize Cloud MQTT infrastructure (open source)</li>\r\n	</ul>\r\n	</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Associated Evaluation Kit :&nbsp;</strong></p>\r\n', '<p><strong>Mechanical Charateristics</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>Dimensions: L 38mm x W 28mm x&nbsp; H 3mm</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Packaging Options</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>Bare board (default)</li>\r\n	<li>Optional ABS plastic casing (IP44)</li>\r\n	<li>Optional silcone resin (IP65)</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Electrical Characteristics</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>Input voltage: 2.3V to 3.6V</li>\r\n	<li>Power consumption: from 10mA to 80mAH (depending on communication channel)</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Temperature Range</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>-20&deg;C, +55&deg;C</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n', 2, 'Yes', '2021-01-04', '<p><strong>TapNLink BLE, NFC (Type5) module for local connection of mobiles to microcontroller-based electronic systems.</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p>TapNLink modules provide wireless interfaces for linking electronic systems to mobile devices and to the Cloud. TapNLink connects directly to the target system&#39;s microcontroller. It integrates into and is powered by the target system.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>All TapNLink products are easily configured to control access by different types of users to data in&nbsp;the target system. TapNLink facilitates rapid creation of Human Machine Interfaces (HMI) that run on Android, iOS and&nbsp;Windows&nbsp;mobiles. HMI apps are easily customized for different users&nbsp;and can be deployed and updated to keep pace with evolving system requirements&nbsp;and user needs.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Wireless Channels</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>Near Field Communication (NFC) Type5 tag (ISO/IEC 15693)</li>\r\n	<li>Bluetooth Low Energy (BLE) 4.1</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Supported Target Connections</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>Serial interface with Software Secure Serial Port (S3P) protocol</li>\r\n	<li>Serial interface with ARM SWD debug protocol</li>\r\n	<li>UART with Modbus protocol</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Mobile Platform Support&nbsp;</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>HTML5 web apps&nbsp;(Android, iOS)</li>\r\n	<li>API for Cordova (Android, iOS, Windows 10)&nbsp;</li>\r\n	<li>Java (Android, iOS native)</li>\r\n	<li>Auto-app generator for Android and iOS mobiles</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Security</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>Configurable access profiles&nbsp;</li>\r\n	<li>Configurable, encrypted passwords</li>\r\n	<li>AES-128/256 module-level data encryption</li>\r\n	<li>Configurable secure pairing with NFC</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Compliance</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>CE (Europe), FCC (USA), IC (Canada).</li>\r\n	<li>REACH</li>\r\n	<li>RoHS</li>\r\n	<li>WEEE</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Ordering Information</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>SKU: TnL-FIR103</li>\r\n	<li>MOQ: 1</li>\r\n	<li>Prices include:\r\n	<ul>\r\n		<li>TapNLink modules pre-qualified, pre-programmed and ready to configure</li>\r\n		<li>IoTize Studio configuration and testing software</li>\r\n		<li>Software for HMI&nbsp;on mobile devices (iOS, Android, Windows 10)</li>\r\n		<li>IoTize Cloud MQTT infrastructure (open source)</li>\r\n	</ul>\r\n	</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Associated Evaluation Kit :&nbsp;</strong></p>\r\n', 'SKU: TnL-FIR103', 34.95, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 0),
(150, 'TapNLink NFC , BLE ,  WIFI', 169, 'Active', '<p><strong>TapNLink module Wi-Fi, BLE, NFC (Type5) for local connection of microcontroller-based electronic systems to mobiles or to the Cloud</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p>TapNLink modules provide wireless interfaces for linking electronic systems to mobile devices and to the Cloud. TapNLink connects directly to the target system&#39;s microcontroller. It integrates into and is powered by the target system.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>All TapNLink products are easily configured to control access by different types of users to data in&nbsp;the target system. TapNLink facilitates rapid creation of Human Machine Interfaces (HMI) that run on Android, iOS and&nbsp;Windows&nbsp;mobiles. HMI apps are easily customized for different users&nbsp;and can be deployed and updated to keep pace with evolving system requirements&nbsp;and user needs.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>TapNLink Wi-Fi modules can also be configured to connect the target system permanently to a wireless network and the Cloud. This enables permanent logging of target system data and alarms.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Wireless Channels</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>Wi-Fi&nbsp;802.11b/g/n</li>\r\n	<li>Bluetooth Low Energy (BLE 4.2)</li>\r\n	<li>Near Field Communication (NFC) Type5 tag (ISO/IEC 15693)</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Supported Target Connections</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p>Connects on 2 GPIO of the target microcontroller and supports:</p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>Serial interface with Software Secure Serial Port (S3P) protocol</li>\r\n	<li>Serial interface with ARM SWD debug protocol</li>\r\n	<li>UART with Modbus protocol</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Mobile Platform Support&nbsp;</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>HTML5 web apps (Android, iOS)</li>\r\n	<li>API for Cordova (Android, iOS, Windows 10)</li>\r\n	<li>Java (Android, iOS native)</li>\r\n	<li>Auto-app generator for Android and iOS mobiles</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Security</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>Configurable access profiles&nbsp;</li>\r\n	<li>Configurable, encrypted passwords</li>\r\n	<li>AES-128/256 module-level data encryption</li>\r\n	<li>Configurable secure pairing with NFC</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Compliance</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>CE (Europe), FCC (USA), IC (Canada).</li>\r\n	<li>REACH</li>\r\n	<li>RoHS</li>\r\n	<li>WEEE</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Ordering Information</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>Base Part Number:&nbsp; TnL-FIW103</li>\r\n	<li>Unitary Price:&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;27.30 EUR / module</li>\r\n	<li>MOQ:&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;20 modules</li>\r\n	<li>Prices include:\r\n	<ul>\r\n		<li>TapNLink modules pre-qualified, pre-programmed and ready to configure</li>\r\n		<li>IoTize Studio configuration and testing software</li>\r\n		<li>Software for HMI&nbsp;on mobile devices (iOS, Android, Windows 10)</li>\r\n		<li>IoTize Cloud MQTT infrastructure (open source)</li>\r\n	</ul>\r\n	</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Associated Evaluation Kit :&nbsp;</strong></p>\r\n', '<p><strong>Mechanical Charateristics</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>Dimensions: L 38mm x W 28mm x&nbsp; H 3mm</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Packaging Options</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>Bare board (default)</li>\r\n	<li>Optional ABS plastic casing (IP44).</li>\r\n	<li>Optional silcone resin (IP65) treatment.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Electrical Characteristics</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>Input voltage: 2.3V to 3.6V</li>\r\n	<li>Low power consumption:\r\n	<ul>\r\n		<li>Standby: 100 &micro;A</li>\r\n		<li>NFC Tx/Rx: &nbsp; &nbsp; 7 mA</li>\r\n		<li>Wi-Fi Rx: 110 mA</li>\r\n		<li>Wi-Fi Tx : 280 mA (802.11b)</li>\r\n	</ul>\r\n	</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Temperature Range</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>-20&deg;C, +55&deg;C</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n', 2, 'Yes', '2021-01-04', '<p><strong>TapNLink module Wi-Fi, BLE, NFC (Type5) for local connection of microcontroller-based electronic systems to mobiles or to the Cloud</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p>TapNLink modules provide wireless interfaces for linking electronic systems to mobile devices and to the Cloud. TapNLink connects directly to the target system&#39;s microcontroller. It integrates into and is powered by the target system.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>All TapNLink products are easily configured to control access by different types of users to data in&nbsp;the target system. TapNLink facilitates rapid creation of Human Machine Interfaces (HMI) that run on Android, iOS and&nbsp;Windows&nbsp;mobiles. HMI apps are easily customized for different users&nbsp;and can be deployed and updated to keep pace with evolving system requirements&nbsp;and user needs.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>TapNLink Wi-Fi modules can also be configured to connect the target system permanently to a wireless network and the Cloud. This enables permanent logging of target system data and alarms.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Wireless Channels</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>Wi-Fi&nbsp;802.11b/g/n</li>\r\n	<li>Bluetooth Low Energy (BLE 4.2)</li>\r\n	<li>Near Field Communication (NFC) Type5 tag (ISO/IEC 15693)</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Supported Target Connections</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p>Connects on 2 GPIO of the target microcontroller and supports:</p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>Serial interface with Software Secure Serial Port (S3P) protocol</li>\r\n	<li>Serial interface with ARM SWD debug protocol</li>\r\n	<li>UART with Modbus protocol</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Mobile Platform Support&nbsp;</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>HTML5 web apps (Android, iOS)</li>\r\n	<li>API for Cordova (Android, iOS, Windows 10)</li>\r\n	<li>Java (Android, iOS native)</li>\r\n	<li>Auto-app generator for Android and iOS mobiles</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Security</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>Configurable access profiles&nbsp;</li>\r\n	<li>Configurable, encrypted passwords</li>\r\n	<li>AES-128/256 module-level data encryption</li>\r\n	<li>Configurable secure pairing with NFC</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Compliance</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>CE (Europe), FCC (USA), IC (Canada).</li>\r\n	<li>REACH</li>\r\n	<li>RoHS</li>\r\n	<li>WEEE</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Ordering Information</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>Base Part Number:&nbsp; TnL-FIW103</li>\r\n	<li>Unitary Price:&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;27.30 EUR / module</li>\r\n	<li>MOQ:&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;20 modules</li>\r\n	<li>Prices include:\r\n	<ul>\r\n		<li>TapNLink modules pre-qualified, pre-programmed and ready to configure</li>\r\n		<li>IoTize Studio configuration and testing software</li>\r\n		<li>Software for HMI&nbsp;on mobile devices (iOS, Android, Windows 10)</li>\r\n		<li>IoTize Cloud MQTT infrastructure (open source)</li>\r\n	</ul>\r\n	</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Associated Evaluation Kit :&nbsp;</strong></p>\r\n', 'SKU: TnL-FIW103', 24.95, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 0),
(152, 'TapNLink Primer NFC-BLE', 169, 'Active', '<p><strong>TapNLink Primer evaluation kit for implementing TnL-FIR103 modules with BLE and NFC for interfaces connecting MCU-based electronic systems to mobile devices and the Cloud.</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p>With TapNLink Primer, it takes just minutes for system designers to create their first IoT proofs-of-concept. This Primer&nbsp;connects microcontroller-based&nbsp;systems to mobile devices via&nbsp;<a href=\"https://www.iotize.com/bluetooth-ble.html\">Bluetooth Low Energy</a>&nbsp;(BLE) or&nbsp;<a href=\"https://www.iotize.com/nfc.html\">Near Field Communication</a>&nbsp;<strong>*</strong>&nbsp;(NFC) interface. Using a mobile device as a gateway, the Primer&nbsp;also transfers data from the target MCU application to a provisioned and pre-configured IoT service platform on the Cloud.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>The Primer connects to a target MCU using only 2&nbsp;GPIO and either:</p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li><strong>Serial protocol</strong>&nbsp;(S3P - Sofware Secure Serial Protocol)&nbsp;<strong>**</strong></li>\r\n	<li><strong>SWD</strong>&nbsp;(debug)&nbsp;<strong>protoco</strong>l for ARM Cortex M-based microcontrollers</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p>The Primer implements by configuration only. There is no coding or hardware to design.&nbsp;Just specify the variables in the target MCU application to access, set access rights and display parameters. The Primer&#39;s&nbsp;configuration software,&nbsp;<em><strong>IoTize Studio</strong></em>,&nbsp;automatically generates the HMI for your mobiles&nbsp;(Android or iOS) and prepares the Cloud environment to log data for the&nbsp;selected variables.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>In just minutes, you can connect a mobile to your microcontroller application, read and write data from a custom mobile HMI app and view logged data on the Cloud.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Notes:<br />\r\n<strong>*&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;</strong>&nbsp;TapNLink Primer&nbsp;implements the STMicroelectronics&#39; ST25DV dynamic NFC tag.&nbsp;<a href=\"https://www.iotize.com/iotize-st-partner.html\">More information about ST25DV...</a><br />\r\n<strong>**&nbsp; &nbsp;</strong>&nbsp;S3P enables connection to any microcontroller, regardless of its architecture.</p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Security Features</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>Configurable access profiles&nbsp;</li>\r\n	<li>Configurable, encrypted passwords</li>\r\n	<li>Configurable&nbsp;<a href=\"https://www.iotize.com/video-iotize-nfc-demo.html\">BLE pairing by NFC</a></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Mobile Platform Support</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>HTML5 web apps</li>\r\n	<li>Cordova-based&nbsp;hybrid apps (native, Java)</li>\r\n	<li>Automatic app generation&nbsp;(Android, iOS)</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Primer Contents</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>1x&nbsp; &nbsp; TapNLink wireless module (Wi-Fi, BLE, NFC interfaces)</li>\r\n	<li>1x&nbsp; &nbsp; ABS plastic cover</li>\r\n	<li>1x&nbsp; &nbsp; Six-probe connection cable</li>\r\n	<li>1x&nbsp; &nbsp; STM32 sample application board and software</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>FREE Supporting Software</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>IoTize Studio configuration software for Windows PCs</li>\r\n	<li>Tap Manager app for mobile devices (Android, iOS)</li>\r\n	<li>Server-based automatic app generation tools (Android)</li>\r\n	<li>Cloud Primer platform (provisioned, pre-configured)</li>\r\n	<li>Arduino&nbsp;Tap library for Arduino integration (<a href=\"https://github.com/iotize-sas/Arduino-Tap/blob/master/extras/howto.md\">on GitHub</a>)</li>\r\n	<li>MQTT relay (open source)</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p>The TapNLink Primer also includes sample microcontroller application firmware for all STM32 microcontrollers and an accompanying Sensor Demo app for Android and iOS mobiles to help you get started.</p>\r\n', '<p><strong>Physical Characteristics</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>PCB dimensions: 38 mm x 28 mm x 3 mm</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n', 4, 'Yes', '2021-01-06', '<p><strong>TapNLink Primer evaluation kit for implementing TnL-FIR103 modules with BLE and NFC for interfaces connecting MCU-based electronic systems to mobile devices and the Cloud.</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p>With TapNLink Primer, it takes just minutes for system designers to create their first IoT proofs-of-concept. This Primer&nbsp;connects microcontroller-based&nbsp;systems to mobile devices via&nbsp;<a href=\"https://www.iotize.com/bluetooth-ble.html\">Bluetooth Low Energy</a>&nbsp;(BLE) or&nbsp;<a href=\"https://www.iotize.com/nfc.html\">Near Field Communication</a>&nbsp;<strong>*</strong>&nbsp;(NFC) interface. Using a mobile device as a gateway, the Primer&nbsp;also transfers data from the target MCU application to a provisioned and pre-configured IoT service platform on the Cloud.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>The Primer connects to a target MCU using only 2&nbsp;GPIO and either:</p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li><strong>Serial protocol</strong>&nbsp;(S3P - Sofware Secure Serial Protocol)&nbsp;<strong>**</strong></li>\r\n	<li><strong>SWD</strong>&nbsp;(debug)&nbsp;<strong>protoco</strong>l for ARM Cortex M-based microcontrollers</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p>The Primer implements by configuration only. There is no coding or hardware to design.&nbsp;Just specify the variables in the target MCU application to access, set access rights and display parameters. The Primer&#39;s&nbsp;configuration software,&nbsp;<em><strong>IoTize Studio</strong></em>,&nbsp;automatically generates the HMI for your mobiles&nbsp;(Android or iOS) and prepares the Cloud environment to log data for the&nbsp;selected variables.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>In just minutes, you can connect a mobile to your microcontroller application, read and write data from a custom mobile HMI app and view logged data on the Cloud.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Notes:<br />\r\n<strong>*&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;</strong>&nbsp;TapNLink Primer&nbsp;implements the STMicroelectronics&#39; ST25DV dynamic NFC tag.&nbsp;<a href=\"https://www.iotize.com/iotize-st-partner.html\">More information about ST25DV...</a><br />\r\n<strong>**&nbsp; &nbsp;</strong>&nbsp;S3P enables connection to any microcontroller, regardless of its architecture.</p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Security Features</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>Configurable access profiles&nbsp;</li>\r\n	<li>Configurable, encrypted passwords</li>\r\n	<li>Configurable&nbsp;<a href=\"https://www.iotize.com/video-iotize-nfc-demo.html\">BLE pairing by NFC</a></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Mobile Platform Support</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>HTML5 web apps</li>\r\n	<li>Cordova-based&nbsp;hybrid apps (native, Java)</li>\r\n	<li>Automatic app generation&nbsp;(Android, iOS)</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Primer Contents</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>1x&nbsp; &nbsp; TapNLink wireless module (Wi-Fi, BLE, NFC interfaces)</li>\r\n	<li>1x&nbsp; &nbsp; ABS plastic cover</li>\r\n	<li>1x&nbsp; &nbsp; Six-probe connection cable</li>\r\n	<li>1x&nbsp; &nbsp; STM32 sample application board and software</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>FREE Supporting Software</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>IoTize Studio configuration software for Windows PCs</li>\r\n	<li>Tap Manager app for mobile devices (Android, iOS)</li>\r\n	<li>Server-based automatic app generation tools (Android)</li>\r\n	<li>Cloud Primer platform (provisioned, pre-configured)</li>\r\n	<li>Arduino&nbsp;Tap library for Arduino integration (<a href=\"https://github.com/iotize-sas/Arduino-Tap/blob/master/extras/howto.md\">on GitHub</a>)</li>\r\n	<li>MQTT relay (open source)</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p>The TapNLink Primer also includes sample microcontroller application firmware for all STM32 microcontrollers and an accompanying Sensor Demo app for Android and iOS mobiles to help you get started.</p>\r\n', 'SKU: IOTZ-TAPNLINK-PRIMER-NB', 34.95, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 0);
INSERT INTO `tbl_product` (`product_id`, `product_name`, `product_category_id`, `product_status`, `product_description`, `product_specification`, `priorty`, `display_flag`, `product_entry_date`, `product_details`, `product_code`, `product_amt`, `product_tax`, `product_discount`, `product_threshold`, `total_product`, `total_sold`, `total_remaining`) VALUES
(153, 'TapNLink Primer NFC-BLE-WiFi', 169, 'Active', '<p><strong>TapNLink Primer evaluation kit for implementing TnL-FIW103 modules with Wi-Fi, BLE and NFC for interfaces connecting MCU-based electronic systems to mobile devices.</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p>With TapNLink Primer, it takes just minutes for system designers to create their first IoT proofs-of-concept. The Primer connects microcontroller-based&nbsp;systems to mobile devices via&nbsp;<a href=\"https://www.iotize.com/wi-fi.html\">Wi-Fi</a>,&nbsp;<a href=\"https://www.iotize.com/bluetooth-ble.html\">Bluetooth Low Energy</a>&nbsp;(BLE) or&nbsp;<a href=\"https://www.iotize.com/nfc.html\">Near Field Communication</a>&nbsp;<strong>*</strong>&nbsp;(NFC) interface. Users can rapidly and easily create Human-Machine Interfaces (HMI) that run as mobile apps for any microcontroller-based system.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>The Primer connects to a target MCU using only 2&nbsp;GPIO and either:</p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li><strong>Serial protocol</strong>&nbsp;(S3P - Sofware Secure Serial Protocol)&nbsp;<strong>**</strong></li>\r\n	<li><strong>SWD</strong>&nbsp;(debug)&nbsp;<strong>protoco</strong>l for ARM Cortex M-based microcontrollers</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p>The Primer implements by configuration only. There is no coding or hardware to design.&nbsp;Just specify the variables in the target system, set access rights and display parameters. The Primer&#39;s configuration software,&nbsp;<em><strong>IoTize Studio</strong></em>,&nbsp;automatically generates the HMI for your mobiles (Android, iOS).</p>\r\n\r\n<p>In just minutes, you will be able to connect a mobile to your microcontroller application, and view, or change&nbsp;data from your&nbsp;mobile app.&nbsp;<strong>***</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p>Notes:<br />\r\n<strong>*&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;</strong>&nbsp;TapNLink Primer implements the STMicroelectronics&#39; ST25DV dynamic NFC tag.&nbsp;<a href=\"https://www.iotize.com/iotize-st-partner.html\">More information about ST25DV...</a><br />\r\n<em><strong>**&nbsp; &nbsp;</strong>&nbsp;S3P enables connection to any microcontroller, regardless of its architecture.<br />\r\n<strong>***</strong>&nbsp; &nbsp;Primer firmware can also be reprogrammed to allow permanent connection&nbsp;to a network and data logging to the Cloud.</em></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Security Features</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>Configurable access profiles&nbsp;</li>\r\n	<li>Configurable, encrypted passwords</li>\r\n	<li>Configurable&nbsp;<a href=\"https://www.iotize.com/video-iotize-nfc-demo.html\">BLE pairing using NFC</a></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Mobile Platform Support</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>HTML5 web apps</li>\r\n	<li>Cordova-based&nbsp;hybrid apps (native, Java)</li>\r\n	<li>Automatic app generation&nbsp;(Android, iOS)</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Primer Contents</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>1x&nbsp; &nbsp; TapNLink wireless module (Wi-Fi, BLE, NFC interfaces)</li>\r\n	<li>1x&nbsp; &nbsp; ABS plastic cover</li>\r\n	<li>1x&nbsp; &nbsp; Six-probe connection cable</li>\r\n	<li>1x&nbsp; &nbsp; STM32 sample application board and software</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>FREE Supporting Software</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>IoTize Studio configuration software for Windows PCs</li>\r\n	<li>Tap Manager app for mobile devices (Android, iOS)</li>\r\n	<li>Arduino Tap library for Arduino integration (<a href=\"https://github.com/iotize-sas/Arduino-Tap/blob/master/extras/howto.md\">on GitHub</a>)</li>\r\n	<li>MQTT relay (open source)</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p>The TapNLink Primer also includes sample microcontroller application firmware for all STM32 microcontrollers and an accompanying Sensor Demo app for Android and iOS mobiles to help you get started.</p>\r\n', '<p><strong>Physical Characteristics</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>PCB dimensions: 38 mm x 28 mm x 3 mm</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n', 5, 'Yes', '2021-01-06', '<p><strong>TapNLink Primer evaluation kit for implementing TnL-FIW103 modules with Wi-Fi, BLE and NFC for interfaces connecting MCU-based electronic systems to mobile devices.</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p>With TapNLink Primer, it takes just minutes for system designers to create their first IoT proofs-of-concept. The Primer connects microcontroller-based&nbsp;systems to mobile devices via&nbsp;<a href=\"https://www.iotize.com/wi-fi.html\">Wi-Fi</a>,&nbsp;<a href=\"https://www.iotize.com/bluetooth-ble.html\">Bluetooth Low Energy</a>&nbsp;(BLE) or&nbsp;<a href=\"https://www.iotize.com/nfc.html\">Near Field Communication</a>&nbsp;<strong>*</strong>&nbsp;(NFC) interface. Users can rapidly and easily create Human-Machine Interfaces (HMI) that run as mobile apps for any microcontroller-based system.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>The Primer connects to a target MCU using only 2&nbsp;GPIO and either:</p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li><strong>Serial protocol</strong>&nbsp;(S3P - Sofware Secure Serial Protocol)&nbsp;<strong>**</strong></li>\r\n	<li><strong>SWD</strong>&nbsp;(debug)&nbsp;<strong>protoco</strong>l for ARM Cortex M-based microcontrollers</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p>The Primer implements by configuration only. There is no coding or hardware to design.&nbsp;Just specify the variables in the target system, set access rights and display parameters. The Primer&#39;s configuration software,&nbsp;<em><strong>IoTize Studio</strong></em>,&nbsp;automatically generates the HMI for your mobiles (Android, iOS).</p>\r\n\r\n<p>In just minutes, you will be able to connect a mobile to your microcontroller application, and view, or change&nbsp;data from your&nbsp;mobile app.&nbsp;<strong>***</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p>Notes:<br />\r\n<strong>*&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;</strong>&nbsp;TapNLink Primer implements the STMicroelectronics&#39; ST25DV dynamic NFC tag.&nbsp;<a href=\"https://www.iotize.com/iotize-st-partner.html\">More information about ST25DV...</a><br />\r\n<em><strong>**&nbsp; &nbsp;</strong>&nbsp;S3P enables connection to any microcontroller, regardless of its architecture.<br />\r\n<strong>***</strong>&nbsp; &nbsp;Primer firmware can also be reprogrammed to allow permanent connection&nbsp;to a network and data logging to the Cloud.</em></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Security Features</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>Configurable access profiles&nbsp;</li>\r\n	<li>Configurable, encrypted passwords</li>\r\n	<li>Configurable&nbsp;<a href=\"https://www.iotize.com/video-iotize-nfc-demo.html\">BLE pairing using NFC</a></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Mobile Platform Support</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>HTML5 web apps</li>\r\n	<li>Cordova-based&nbsp;hybrid apps (native, Java)</li>\r\n	<li>Automatic app generation&nbsp;(Android, iOS)</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Primer Contents</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>1x&nbsp; &nbsp; TapNLink wireless module (Wi-Fi, BLE, NFC interfaces)</li>\r\n	<li>1x&nbsp; &nbsp; ABS plastic cover</li>\r\n	<li>1x&nbsp; &nbsp; Six-probe connection cable</li>\r\n	<li>1x&nbsp; &nbsp; STM32 sample application board and software</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>FREE Supporting Software</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>IoTize Studio configuration software for Windows PCs</li>\r\n	<li>Tap Manager app for mobile devices (Android, iOS)</li>\r\n	<li>Arduino Tap library for Arduino integration (<a href=\"https://github.com/iotize-sas/Arduino-Tap/blob/master/extras/howto.md\">on GitHub</a>)</li>\r\n	<li>MQTT relay (open source)</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p>The TapNLink Primer also includes sample microcontroller application firmware for all STM32 microcontrollers and an accompanying Sensor Demo app for Android and iOS mobiles to help you get started.</p>\r\n', 'SKU: IOTZ-TAPNLINK-PRIMER-NBW', 39.95, 0, 0, 1, 1, 0, 1),
(154, 'TapNPass Fixed NFC-BLE adapter for Modbus®, Serial', 169, 'Active', '<p><strong>TapNPass Fixed BLE and NFC (Type5) wireless adapter for local connection of mobile devices to electronic systems via RS-232, RS-485 or USB fieldbus. Supports Modbus.</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>TapNPass Fixed</strong>&nbsp;adapters provide a permanent wireless interface for connecting mobile devices to a target system&nbsp;with an accessible serial fieldbus or Modbus port. They integrate into and are powered by&nbsp;the target system.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>All TapNPass products are easily configured to control access by different types of users who conduct&nbsp;or supervise&nbsp;servicing of the target system. They facilitate&nbsp;rapid creation of user interfaces that run on Android, iOS and Windows-based mobile devices.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Wireless Channels</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>Near Field Communication (NFC) Type5 tag (ISO/IEC 15693)</li>\r\n	<li>Bluetooth Low Energy (BLE) 4.1</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Supported Serial Connections</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>RS-232, RS-485 et USB (protocoles CDC, FTDI and Silabs CP210x).</li>\r\n	<li>Transparent or Modbus service modes.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Mobile Platform Support&nbsp;</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>HTML5 generic applications</li>\r\n	<li>API for Cordova (Android, iOS, Windows 10) or Android native (Java)</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Security</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>Configurable access profiles&nbsp;</li>\r\n	<li>Configurable, encrypted passwords</li>\r\n	<li>AES-128/256 module-level data encryption</li>\r\n	<li>Configurable secure pairing with NFC</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Compliance</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>CE (Europe), FCC (USA), IC (Canada).</li>\r\n	<li>REACH</li>\r\n	<li>RoHS</li>\r\n	<li>WEEE</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Ordering Information</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p>SKU:&nbsp;TnP-FSR103<br />\r\nMOQ: 1<br />\r\nPrice&nbsp;includes:</p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li><strong>TapNPass-F NFC/BLE to Serial fieldbus adapter</strong>&nbsp;pre-programmed and ready to configure</li>\r\n	<li><strong>RS-232 serial cord</strong>&nbsp;(RJ45 to DB9)</li>\r\n	<li><strong>RS-485 serial cord</strong>&nbsp;(RJ45 to DB9)</li>\r\n	<li><strong>Modbus adapter</strong>&nbsp;(RJ45 to RJ45)</li>\r\n	<li><strong>IoTize Tap Toolbox Serial/Modbus utilities app for Android and iOS</strong>&nbsp;mobile devices</li>\r\n	<li><strong>IoTize Studio configuration and testing software</strong></li>\r\n	<li><strong>Cordova support</strong>&nbsp;for mobile HMI development and customization</li>\r\n	<li><strong>IoTize Cloud MQTT infrastructure</strong>&nbsp;(open source)</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n', '<p><strong>Casing&nbsp;</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>ABS plastic casing.</li>\r\n	<li>Dimensions: L 120mm x&nbsp; H 26mm x W 60mm</li>\r\n	<li>Weight (without cables): 110g</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Electrical Characteristics</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>Input voltage: 8V to 30V</li>\r\n	<li>Power consumption: from 10mA to 80mAH (depending on communication channel)</li>\r\n	<li>Output current (USB host) up to 200mA</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Operating Temperature Range</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>-10&deg;C, +50&deg;C</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n', 6, 'Yes', '2021-01-06', '<p><strong>TapNPass Fixed BLE and NFC (Type5) wireless adapter for local connection of mobile devices to electronic systems via RS-232, RS-485 or USB fieldbus. Supports Modbus.</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>TapNPass Fixed</strong>&nbsp;adapters provide a permanent wireless interface for connecting mobile devices to a target system&nbsp;with an accessible serial fieldbus or Modbus port. They integrate into and are powered by&nbsp;the target system.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>All TapNPass products are easily configured to control access by different types of users who conduct&nbsp;or supervise&nbsp;servicing of the target system. They facilitate&nbsp;rapid creation of user interfaces that run on Android, iOS and Windows-based mobile devices.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Wireless Channels</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>Near Field Communication (NFC) Type5 tag (ISO/IEC 15693)</li>\r\n	<li>Bluetooth Low Energy (BLE) 4.1</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Supported Serial Connections</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>RS-232, RS-485 et USB (protocoles CDC, FTDI and Silabs CP210x).</li>\r\n	<li>Transparent or Modbus service modes.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Mobile Platform Support&nbsp;</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>HTML5 generic applications</li>\r\n	<li>API for Cordova (Android, iOS, Windows 10) or Android native (Java)</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Security</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>Configurable access profiles&nbsp;</li>\r\n	<li>Configurable, encrypted passwords</li>\r\n	<li>AES-128/256 module-level data encryption</li>\r\n	<li>Configurable secure pairing with NFC</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Compliance</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>CE (Europe), FCC (USA), IC (Canada).</li>\r\n	<li>REACH</li>\r\n	<li>RoHS</li>\r\n	<li>WEEE</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Ordering Information</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p>SKU:&nbsp;TnP-FSR103<br />\r\nMOQ: 1<br />\r\nPrice&nbsp;includes:</p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li><strong>TapNPass-F NFC/BLE to Serial fieldbus adapter</strong>&nbsp;pre-programmed and ready to configure</li>\r\n	<li><strong>RS-232 serial cord</strong>&nbsp;(RJ45 to DB9)</li>\r\n	<li><strong>RS-485 serial cord</strong>&nbsp;(RJ45 to DB9)</li>\r\n	<li><strong>Modbus adapter</strong>&nbsp;(RJ45 to RJ45)</li>\r\n	<li><strong>IoTize Tap Toolbox Serial/Modbus utilities app for Android and iOS</strong>&nbsp;mobile devices</li>\r\n	<li><strong>IoTize Studio configuration and testing software</strong></li>\r\n	<li><strong>Cordova support</strong>&nbsp;for mobile HMI development and customization</li>\r\n	<li><strong>IoTize Cloud MQTT infrastructure</strong>&nbsp;(open source)</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n', 'SKU: TnP-FSR103', 219.95, 0, 0, 1, 2, 0, 2),
(155, 'TapNPass Nomad NFC-BLE adapter for Modbus®, Serial', 169, 'Active', '<p><strong>TapNPass Nomad BLE and NFC (Type5) wireless adapter for local connection of mobile devices to electronic systems via RS-232, RS-485 or USB fieldbus. Supports Modbus protocol.</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>TapNPass Nomad</strong>&nbsp;products provide&nbsp;portable, wireless interfaces for connecting mobile devices to target systems with serial fieldbus or Modbus interface. To facilitate use as a portable tool, Nomad products include:</p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>Rechargeable&nbsp;battery power supply ensuring more than&nbsp;8 hours of autonomy in continuous communication</li>\r\n	<li>Magnets to hold the product against a support while in use</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p>All TapNPass products are easily configured to control access by different types of users who conduct&nbsp;or supervise&nbsp;servicing of&nbsp;target systems. TapNPass facilitates rapid creation of user interfaces that run on Android, iOS and Windows-based mobile devices.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Wireless Channels</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>Near Field Communication (NFC) Type5 tag (ISO/IEC 15693)</li>\r\n	<li>Bluetooth Low Energy (BLE) 4.1</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Supported Serial Connections</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>RS-232, RS-485 et USB (protocoles CDC, FTDI and Silabs CP210x).</li>\r\n	<li>Transparent or Modbus service modes.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Mobile Platform Support&nbsp;</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>HTML5 generic applications</li>\r\n	<li>API for Cordova (Android, iOS, Windows 10) or Android native (Java)</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Security</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>Configurable access profiles&nbsp;</li>\r\n	<li>Configurable, encrypted passwords</li>\r\n	<li>AES-128/256 module-level data encryption</li>\r\n	<li>Configurable secure pairing with NFC</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Compliance</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>CE (Europe), FCC (USA), IC (Canada).</li>\r\n	<li>REACH</li>\r\n	<li>RoHS</li>\r\n	<li><strong>WEEE</strong></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Ordering Information</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p>SKU:&nbsp; TnP-NSR103<br />\r\nMOQ: 1<br />\r\nPrice&nbsp;includes:</p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li><strong>TapNPass-N NFC/BLE to Serial fieldbus adapter</strong>&nbsp;pre-programmed and ready to configure</li>\r\n	<li><strong>RS-232 serial cord</strong>&nbsp;(RJ45 to DB9)</li>\r\n	<li><strong>RS-485 serial cord</strong>&nbsp;(RJ45 to DB9)</li>\r\n	<li><strong>Modbus adapter</strong>&nbsp;(RJ45 to RJ45)</li>\r\n	<li><strong>Micro USB cable</strong></li>\r\n	<li><strong>Li ION rechargeable batteries</strong>&nbsp;</li>\r\n	<li>IoTize&nbsp;<strong>Tap Toolbox Serial/Modbus utilities app for Android and iOS</strong>&nbsp;mobile devices</li>\r\n	<li><strong>IoTize Studio configuration and testing software</strong></li>\r\n	<li><strong>Cordova support</strong>&nbsp;for mobile HMI development and customization</li>\r\n	<li><strong>IoTize Cloud MQTT infrastructure</strong>&nbsp;(open source)</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n', '<p><strong>Casing&nbsp;</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>ABS plastic casing with rechargeable Li-Ion batteries.</li>\r\n	<li>Dimensions: L 105mm x&nbsp; H 33mm x W 46mm</li>\r\n	<li>Weight (without cables): 110g</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Electrical Characteristics</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>Input voltage: 5V (micro USB connector)</li>\r\n	<li>Battery capacity: 1300 mAH</li>\r\n	<li>Power consumption: from 10mA to 80mAH (depending on communication channel)</li>\r\n	<li>Output current (USB host) up to 200mA</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Operating Temperature Range</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>-10&deg;C, +50&deg;C</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n', 7, 'Yes', '2021-01-07', '<p><strong>TapNPass Nomad BLE and NFC (Type5) wireless adapter for local connection of mobile devices to electronic systems via RS-232, RS-485 or USB fieldbus. Supports Modbus protocol.</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>TapNPass Nomad</strong>&nbsp;products provide&nbsp;portable, wireless interfaces for connecting mobile devices to target systems with serial fieldbus or Modbus interface. To facilitate use as a portable tool, Nomad products include:</p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>Rechargeable&nbsp;battery power supply ensuring more than&nbsp;8 hours of autonomy in continuous communication</li>\r\n	<li>Magnets to hold the product against a support while in use</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p>All TapNPass products are easily configured to control access by different types of users who conduct&nbsp;or supervise&nbsp;servicing of&nbsp;target systems. TapNPass facilitates rapid creation of user interfaces that run on Android, iOS and Windows-based mobile devices.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Wireless Channels</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>Near Field Communication (NFC) Type5 tag (ISO/IEC 15693)</li>\r\n	<li>Bluetooth Low Energy (BLE) 4.1</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Supported Serial Connections</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>RS-232, RS-485 et USB (protocoles CDC, FTDI and Silabs CP210x).</li>\r\n	<li>Transparent or Modbus service modes.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Mobile Platform Support&nbsp;</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>HTML5 generic applications</li>\r\n	<li>API for Cordova (Android, iOS, Windows 10) or Android native (Java)</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Security</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>Configurable access profiles&nbsp;</li>\r\n	<li>Configurable, encrypted passwords</li>\r\n	<li>AES-128/256 module-level data encryption</li>\r\n	<li>Configurable secure pairing with NFC</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Compliance</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>CE (Europe), FCC (USA), IC (Canada).</li>\r\n	<li>REACH</li>\r\n	<li>RoHS</li>\r\n	<li><strong>WEEE</strong></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Ordering Information</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p>SKU:&nbsp; TnP-NSR103<br />\r\nMOQ: 1<br />\r\nPrice&nbsp;includes:</p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li><strong>TapNPass-N NFC/BLE to Serial fieldbus adapter</strong>&nbsp;pre-programmed and ready to configure</li>\r\n	<li><strong>RS-232 serial cord</strong>&nbsp;(RJ45 to DB9)</li>\r\n	<li><strong>RS-485 serial cord</strong>&nbsp;(RJ45 to DB9)</li>\r\n	<li><strong>Modbus adapter</strong>&nbsp;(RJ45 to RJ45)</li>\r\n	<li><strong>Micro USB cable</strong></li>\r\n	<li><strong>Li ION rechargeable batteries</strong>&nbsp;</li>\r\n	<li>IoTize&nbsp;<strong>Tap Toolbox Serial/Modbus utilities app for Android and iOS</strong>&nbsp;mobile devices</li>\r\n	<li><strong>IoTize Studio configuration and testing software</strong></li>\r\n	<li><strong>Cordova support</strong>&nbsp;for mobile HMI development and customization</li>\r\n	<li><strong>IoTize Cloud MQTT infrastructure</strong>&nbsp;(open source)</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n', 'SKU: TnP-NSR103', 219.95, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 0),
(156, '4 Port Gigabit Ethernet FMC Module', 159, 'Active', '<p>The FMCETHX001 Ethernet Expansion Module features RTL8211E-VB-CG which is a highly integrated Ethernet transceiver that complies with 10Base-T, 100Base-TX, and 1000Base-T IEEE 802.3 standards. It provides all the necessary physical layer functions to transmit and receive Ethernet packets over CAT 5 UTP cable or CAT 3 UTP (10Mbps only) cable.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>The RTL8211E-VB-CG uses state-of-the-art DSP technology and an Analog Front End (AFE) to enable high-speed data transmission and reception over UTP cable. Functions such as Crossover Detection &amp; Auto-Correction, polarity correction, adaptive equalization, cross-talk cancellation, echo cancellation, timing recovery, and error correction are implemented in the RTL8211E-VB-CG to provide robust transmission and reception capabilities at 10Mbps, 100Mbps, or 1000Mbps.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Data transfer between MAC and PHY is via the Reduced Gigabit Media Independent Interface (RGMII) for 1000Base-T, 10Base-T, and 100Base-TX.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Features</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>4 High-Performance 10/100/1000Mbps Ethernet Transceiver</li>\r\n	<li>Dimension: 76.50mm x 69.00mm</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Applications</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>Network Interface Adapter.</li>\r\n	<li>MAU (Media Access Unit).</li>\r\n	<li>CNR (Communication and Network Riser).</li>\r\n	<li>ACR (Advanced Communication Riser).</li>\r\n	<li>Ethernet hub.</li>\r\n	<li>Ethernet switch.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n', '<table>\r\n	<thead>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Attribute</th>\r\n			<th>Value</th>\r\n		</tr>\r\n	</thead>\r\n	<tbody>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<td>Weight</td>\r\n			<td>0.6 lbs</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<td>Number of Ethernet Ports</td>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>4</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<td>Ethernet PHY</td>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>RTL8211E</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<td>Interface</td>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>RGMII</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<td>RGMII Voltage</td>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>3.3V</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<td>Supported Speeds</td>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>1000BASE-T, 100BASE-T, 10BASE-T</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<td>Dimensions</td>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>76.50mm x 69.00mm</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n	</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n', 1, 'Yes', '2021-01-08', '<p>The FMCETHX001 Ethernet Expansion Module features RTL8211E-VB-CG which is a highly integrated Ethernet transceiver that complies with 10Base-T, 100Base-TX, and 1000Base-T IEEE 802.3 standards. It provides all the necessary physical layer functions to transmit and receive Ethernet packets over CAT 5 UTP cable or CAT 3 UTP (10Mbps only) cable.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>The RTL8211E-VB-CG uses state-of-the-art DSP technology and an Analog Front End (AFE) to enable high-speed data transmission and reception over UTP cable. Functions such as Crossover Detection &amp; Auto-Correction, polarity correction, adaptive equalization, cross-talk cancellation, echo cancellation, timing recovery, and error correction are implemented in the RTL8211E-VB-CG to provide robust transmission and reception capabilities at 10Mbps, 100Mbps, or 1000Mbps.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Data transfer between MAC and PHY is via the Reduced Gigabit Media Independent Interface (RGMII) for 1000Base-T, 10Base-T, and 100Base-TX.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Features</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>4 High-Performance 10/100/1000Mbps Ethernet Transceiver</li>\r\n	<li>Dimension: 76.50mm x 69.00mm</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Applications</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>Network Interface Adapter.</li>\r\n	<li>MAU (Media Access Unit).</li>\r\n	<li>CNR (Communication and Network Riser).</li>\r\n	<li>ACR (Advanced Communication Riser).</li>\r\n	<li>Ethernet hub.</li>\r\n	<li>Ethernet switch.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n', 'SKU: NLFMCET001', 299.95, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 0),
(157, 'FMCADCX002: Dual AD7616 FMC ADC Expansion Module', 159, 'Active', '<p>The Numato Lab FMCADCX002 ADC Expansion Module features two Analog Devices AD7616 ICs. Each IC has a 16 channel, 16-bit, dual simultaneous sampling ADC with a sampling rate of up to 1 MSPS, thus providing a total of 32 analog input channels. The AD7616 is designed to support communications applications where low cost, small size, wide bandwidth, and versatility are desired. This module is designed to be used with Numato Lab&rsquo;s FPGA boards featuring FMC connectors, and can additionally be used with any FPGA board supporting the FMC LPC connector. Numato Lab FMCADCX002 ADC Breakout Board with MMCX connectors (Manufacturer Part Number: 0734151471) is to be used along with this module to provide analog inputs.<br />\r\n<strong>Features</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>FMC LPC connector for mating with compatible FPGA carrier cards</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p>Two dual simultaneous sampling AD7616 ICs</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p>32 Analog input channels with selectable input range (&plusmn;10 V, &plusmn;5 V, &plusmn;2.5 V)</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p>16-bit resolution with 1 MSPS maximum sampling rate</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>2 trigger inputs, 2 trigger outputs and 4 IOs</li>\r\n	<li>No external power supply is needed. Uses 12V&nbsp;supplies from Carrier boards through FMC LPC connector</li>\r\n	<li>Dimension: 84.01mm x 68.99mm</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Applications</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>Digital Instrumentation</li>\r\n	<li>Product prototyping</li>\r\n	<li>Low-Cost Digital Oscilloscopes</li>\r\n	<li>Data acquisition</li>\r\n	<li>Electronic test and measurement equipment</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n', '<table>\r\n	<thead>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Attribute</th>\r\n			<th>Value</th>\r\n		</tr>\r\n	</thead>\r\n	<tbody>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<td>Analog Input Resolution</td>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p><a href=\"https://numato.com/analog-input-resolution/16-bits/\" rel=\"tag\">16 Bits</a></p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<td>Analog Inputs(Max)</td>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p><a href=\"https://numato.com/analog-inputs/32/\" rel=\"tag\">32</a></p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<td>Analog Input Type</td>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>Differential</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<td>Max Sampling Rate</td>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>1 MSPS</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<td>Analog Input Range</td>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>Selectable (&plusmn;10 V, &plusmn;5 V, &plusmn;2.5 V)</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<td>Data Interface</td>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>SPI</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n	</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n', 2, 'Yes', '2021-01-08', '<p>The Numato Lab FMCADCX002 ADC Expansion Module features two Analog Devices AD7616 ICs. Each IC has a 16 channel, 16-bit, dual simultaneous sampling ADC with a sampling rate of up to 1 MSPS, thus providing a total of 32 analog input channels. The AD7616 is designed to support communications applications where low cost, small size, wide bandwidth, and versatility are desired. This module is designed to be used with Numato Lab&rsquo;s FPGA boards featuring FMC connectors, and can additionally be used with any FPGA board supporting the FMC LPC connector. Numato Lab FMCADCX002 ADC Breakout Board with MMCX connectors (Manufacturer Part Number: 0734151471) is to be used along with this module to provide analog inputs.<br />\r\n<strong>Features</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>FMC LPC connector for mating with compatible FPGA carrier cards</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p>Two dual simultaneous sampling AD7616 ICs</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p>32 Analog input channels with selectable input range (&plusmn;10 V, &plusmn;5 V, &plusmn;2.5 V)</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<p>16-bit resolution with 1 MSPS maximum sampling rate</p>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>2 trigger inputs, 2 trigger outputs and 4 IOs</li>\r\n	<li>No external power supply is needed. Uses 12V&nbsp;supplies from Carrier boards through FMC LPC connector</li>\r\n	<li>Dimension: 84.01mm x 68.99mm</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Applications</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>Digital Instrumentation</li>\r\n	<li>Product prototyping</li>\r\n	<li>Low-Cost Digital Oscilloscopes</li>\r\n	<li>Data acquisition</li>\r\n	<li>Electronic test and measurement equipment</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n', 'SKU: NLFMCADC002', 974.95, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 0),
(158, 'Mimas A7 Mini FPGA Development Board', 81, 'Active', '<p><strong>Features</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>Device: Xilinx Artix 7 FPGA (XC7A35T-1FTG256C)</li>\r\n	<li>DDR3: 2Gb DDR3 (MT41J128M16JT-125 or equivalent)</li>\r\n	<li>Built-in programming interface. No expensive JTAG adapters needed for programming the board</li>\r\n	<li>Onboard 128Mb flash memory for FPGA configuration storage and custom user data storage</li>\r\n	<li>High-Speed USB 2.0 interface for On-board flash programming. FT2232H Channel B is dedicated to JTAG Programming. Channel A can be used for custom applications</li>\r\n	<li>100MHz CMOS oscillator</li>\r\n	<li>8 LEDs, 1 RGB LED and 4 Push Buttons for user-defined purposes</li>\r\n	<li>FPGA configuration via JTAG and USB</li>\r\n	<li>Maximum IOs for user-defined purposes\r\n	<ul>\r\n		<li>FPGA &ndash; 70 IOs (35 professionally length matched Differential Pairs) and two 2&times;6 Expansion Headers</li>\r\n	</ul>\r\n	</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Applications</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>Product Prototype Development</li>\r\n	<li>Accelerated computing integration</li>\r\n	<li>Development and testing of custom embedded processors</li>\r\n	<li>Communication devices development</li>\r\n	<li>Educational tool for Schools and Universities</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n', '<table>\r\n	<thead>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Attribute</th>\r\n			<th>Value</th>\r\n		</tr>\r\n	</thead>\r\n	<tbody>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<td>Dimensions</td>\r\n			<td>6 &times; 4 &times; 1 in</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<td>FPGA</td>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p><a href=\"https://numato.com/fpga/xc7a35t-1ftg256c/\" rel=\"tag\">XC7A35T &ndash; 1FTG256C</a></p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<td>Memory</td>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p><a href=\"https://numato.com/memory/ddr3-2gb/\" rel=\"tag\">DDR3 &ndash; 2Gb</a></p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<td>Configuration Options</td>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p><a href=\"https://numato.com/configuration-options/jtag/\" rel=\"tag\">JTAG</a>,&nbsp;<a href=\"https://numato.com/configuration-options/usb/\" rel=\"tag\">USB</a></p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<td>Host Interface</td>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p><a href=\"https://numato.com/host-interface/usb-2-0/\" rel=\"tag\">USB 2.0</a></p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<td>Primary Clock Frequency</td>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p><a href=\"https://numato.com/primary-clock-frequency/100mhz/\" rel=\"tag\">100MHz</a></p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<td>Number Of GPIOs (Max)</td>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p><a href=\"https://numato.com/number-of-gpios/70/\" rel=\"tag\">70</a></p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<td>Number Of Diff Pairs</td>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p><a href=\"https://numato.com/number-of-diff-pairs/35/\" rel=\"tag\">35</a></p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n	</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n', 2, 'Yes', '2021-02-04', '<p>Mimas A7 Mini is an easy to use FPGA Development board featuring Artix 7 FPGA (XC7A35T &ndash; FTG256C package) with FTDI&rsquo;s FT2232H Dual-Channel USB device. It is an Artix-7 based replacement and upgrades of&nbsp;<a href=\"https://numato.com/product/mimas-spartan-6-fpga-development-board/\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Mimas Spartan 6 FPGA Board</a>. It is specially designed for the development and integration of FPGA based accelerated features to other designs. The USB 2.0 host interface based on popular FT2232H offers high bandwidth data transfer and board programming without the need for any external programming adapters.</p>\r\n', 'SKU: NLFX1008', 128.99, 0, 0, 1, 3, 3, 0),
(159, '32 Channel USB GPIO Module With Encloser', 69, 'In-Active', '<p>Numato&rsquo;s 32 Channel USB GPIO module is low cost easily deployable solution for connecting your PC to other electronic circuitry through USB. No USB specific knowledge is required to set up and use this module. Numato Lab&rsquo;s GPIO devices provide an interface that looks like a Serial Port on your Operating System and thus effectively hiding the complexity of USB. All that you need to operate GPIOs is a standard Serial Terminal Emulator such as HyperTerminal/Teraterm or your favorite programming language such a C/C , Python, Perl, etc. Besides providing standard General Purpose IOs, this product has multiple Analog Inputs as well. With the help of appropriate sensors, these Analog inputs can be used to read Analog quantities such as temperature, pressure, distance, sound, etc.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Features</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>32 TTL (3.3V) compatible GPIOs available</li>\r\n	<li>All GPIOs can be individually configured as input or output</li>\r\n	<li>Can be controlled by using standard serial console applications or custom applications</li>\r\n	<li>No USB protocol knowledge required</li>\r\n	<li>Onboard controller can be reprogrammed for custom applications</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Applications</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>Home Automation</li>\r\n	<li>Lighting Control</li>\r\n	<li>Garden Equipment Control</li>\r\n	<li>Industrial Automation</li>\r\n	<li>Test Fixtures</li>\r\n	<li>DIY and Hobby</li>\r\n	<li>Add more IOs and Analog channels to industrial/modular computers</li>\r\n	<li>Add more IOs and Analog channels to Raspberry Pi, Intel Edison, BeagleBone and similar CPU boards</li>\r\n	<li>Add IOs to Android-based systems (Smartphones, Tabs and custom devices)</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Supporting operating systems</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>Windows XP</li>\r\n	<li>Windows 7</li>\r\n	<li>Windows 8/8.1</li>\r\n	<li>Windows 10</li>\r\n	<li>Linux</li>\r\n	<li>Mac OS X</li>\r\n	<li>Android</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n', '<table>\r\n	<thead>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<th>Attribute</th>\r\n			<th>Value</th>\r\n		</tr>\r\n	</thead>\r\n	<tbody>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<td>Weight</td>\r\n			<td>0.15 lbs</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<td>Dimensions</td>\r\n			<td>5 &times; 3 &times; 1 in</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<td>Product Dimensions</td>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>3.66 x 1.84 x 0.55 in</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<td>Number Of GPIOs (Max)</td>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p><a href=\"https://numato.com/number-of-gpios/32/\" rel=\"tag\">32</a></p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<td>Analog Inputs(Max)</td>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p><a href=\"https://numato.com/analog-inputs/7/\" rel=\"tag\">7</a></p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<td>Analog Input Resolution</td>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p><a href=\"https://numato.com/analog-input-resolution/10-bits/\" rel=\"tag\">10 Bits</a></p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<td>IO Voltage Max</td>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p><a href=\"https://numato.com/io-voltage-max/3-3v/\" rel=\"tag\">3.3V</a></p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<td>Communication</td>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>USB</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n		<tr>\r\n			<td>Packaging</td>\r\n			<td>\r\n			<p>Without Enclosure, With Enclosure</p>\r\n			</td>\r\n		</tr>\r\n	</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n', 6, 'Yes', '2021-02-04', '<p>Numato&rsquo;s 32 Channel USB GPIO module is low cost easily deployable solution for connecting your PC to other electronic circuitry through USB. No USB specific knowledge is required to set up and use this module. Numato Lab&rsquo;s GPIO devices provide an interface that looks like a Serial Port on your Operating System and thus effectively hiding the complexity of USB. All that you need to operate GPIOs is a standard Serial Terminal Emulator such as HyperTerminal/Teraterm or your favorite programming language such a C/C , Python, Perl, etc. Besides providing standard General Purpose IOs, this product has multiple Analog Inputs as well. With the help of appropriate sensors, these Analog inputs can be used to read Analog quantities such as temperature, pressure, distance, sound, etc.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Features</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>32 TTL (3.3V) compatible GPIOs available</li>\r\n	<li>All GPIOs can be individually configured as input or output</li>\r\n	<li>Can be controlled by using standard serial console applications or custom applications</li>\r\n	<li>No USB protocol knowledge required</li>\r\n	<li>Onboard controller can be reprogrammed for custom applications</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Applications</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>Home Automation</li>\r\n	<li>Lighting Control</li>\r\n	<li>Garden Equipment Control</li>\r\n	<li>Industrial Automation</li>\r\n	<li>Test Fixtures</li>\r\n	<li>DIY and Hobby</li>\r\n	<li>Add more IOs and Analog channels to industrial/modular computers</li>\r\n	<li>Add more IOs and Analog channels to Raspberry Pi, Intel Edison, BeagleBone and similar CPU boards</li>\r\n	<li>Add IOs to Android-based systems (Smartphones, Tabs and custom devices)</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Supporting operating systems</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>Windows XP</li>\r\n	<li>Windows 7</li>\r\n	<li>Windows 8/8.1</li>\r\n	<li>Windows 10</li>\r\n	<li>Linux</li>\r\n	<li>Mac OS X</li>\r\n	<li>Android</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n', 'SKU: GP320001E', 62.99, 0, 0, 0, 33, 22, 11),
(161, 'BPI-M5 ', 163, 'Active', '<ul>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<h4><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Amlogic S905X3 Quad-Core Cortex-A55</span></h4>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<h4><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Mali-G31 GPU</span></h4>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<h4><span style=\"font-size:12px\">4GB LPDDR4</span></h4>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<h4><span style=\"font-size:12px\">16GB eMMC onboard</span></h4>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<h4><span style=\"font-size:12px\">4 USB port</span></h4>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<h4><span style=\"font-size:12px\">HDMI out</span></h4>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<h4><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Gigabit network</span></h4>\r\n	</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n', '<p style=\"margin-left:0cm; margin-right:0cm\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana,sans-serif\"><strong>CPU</strong>: Amlogic S905X3 Quad-Core Cortex-A55 Processor</span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"margin-left:0cm; margin-right:0cm\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana,sans-serif\"><strong>GPU</strong>: Mali-G31 GPU</span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"margin-left:0cm; margin-right:0cm\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana,sans-serif\"><strong>Memory</strong>: 4GB LPDDR4</span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"margin-left:0cm; margin-right:0cm\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana,sans-serif\"><strong>Storage</strong>: 16G eMMC flash onboard MicroSD slot with support for up to 256GB expansion</span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"margin-left:0cm; margin-right:0cm\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana,sans-serif\"><strong>Network</strong>: 10/100/1000 Mbit/s Ethernet Optional WiFi USB dongle</span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"margin-left:0cm; margin-right:0cm\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana,sans-serif\"><strong>Video Output</strong>: HDMI 2.0 (up to 4K@60Hz with HDR, CEC, EDID)</span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"margin-left:0cm; margin-right:0cm\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana,sans-serif\"><strong>Audio Output</strong>: 3.5mm jack and HDMI</span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"margin-left:0cm; margin-right:0cm\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana,sans-serif\"><strong>USB ports</strong>: 4 x USB ports</span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"margin-left:0cm; margin-right:0cm\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana,sans-serif\"><strong>GPIO</strong>: GPIO (x28) Power (+5V, +3.3V and GND) UART, I2C, SPI or PWM</span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"margin-left:0cm; margin-right:0cm\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana,sans-serif\"><strong>Power Input</strong>: 5 volt @2A via Micro USB (TYPE C)</span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"margin-left:0cm; margin-right:0cm\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana,sans-serif\"><strong>Size&amp;Weight</strong>: 92x60mm, 48g</span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"margin-left:0cm; margin-right:0cm\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana,sans-serif\"><strong>OS</strong>: Android and Linux</span></span></p>\r\n', 1, 'Yes', '2021-06-07', '<ul>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<h4><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Amlogic S905X3 Quad-Core Cortex-A55</span></h4>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<h4><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Mali-G31 GPU</span></h4>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<h4><span style=\"font-size:12px\">4GB LPDDR4</span></h4>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<h4><span style=\"font-size:12px\">16GB eMMC onboard</span></h4>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<h4><span style=\"font-size:12px\">4 USB port</span></h4>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<h4><span style=\"font-size:12px\">HDMI out</span></h4>\r\n	</li>\r\n	<li>\r\n	<h4><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Gigabit network</span></h4>\r\n	</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n', 'BPI-M5', 114.95, 0, 0, 1, 1053, 1451, -398),
(162, 'BPI-F2P', 163, 'Active', '<ul>\r\n	<li><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana,sans-serif\">Sunplus SP7021 &ldquo;Plus1&rdquo; quad-core Cortex-A7 processor</span></span></li>\r\n	<li><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana,sans-serif\">128MB or 512MB DDR3 DRAM</span></span></li>\r\n	<li><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana,sans-serif\">8GB eMMC</span></span></li>\r\n	<li><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana,sans-serif\">2x 10/100M Ethernet</span></span></li>\r\n	<li><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana,sans-serif\">industrial grade:-40C ~ +85&deg;C</span></span></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n', '<p style=\"margin-left:0cm; margin-right:0cm\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana,sans-serif\"><strong>CPU</strong>: Quad-core 1GHz Cortex-A7 CPU, plus A926 and 8051 cores</span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"margin-left:0cm; margin-right:0cm\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana,sans-serif\"><strong>Memory</strong>: Built-in 128MB or 512MB DDR3 DRAM</span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"margin-left:0cm; margin-right:0cm\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana,sans-serif\"><strong>Storage</strong>: 8G eMMC flash onboard MicroSD slot</span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"margin-left:0cm; margin-right:0cm\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana,sans-serif\"><strong>Network</strong>: 2x 10/100M Ethernet RS-485 RS-232</span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"margin-left:0cm; margin-right:0cm\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana,sans-serif\"><strong>Video Output</strong>: HDMI 1.4 output</span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"margin-left:0cm; margin-right:0cm\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana,sans-serif\"><strong>Camera I/F</strong>: MIPI CSI connector</span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"margin-left:0cm; margin-right:0cm\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana,sans-serif\"><strong>USB ports:</strong> 2 x USB 2.0 ports. 1 x USB 2.0 OTG</span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"margin-left:0cm; margin-right:0cm\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana,sans-serif\"><strong>GPIO</strong>: GPIO (x28)</span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"margin-left:0cm; margin-right:0cm\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana,sans-serif\"><strong>Power</strong> (+5V, +3.3V and GND) UART, I2C, SPI or PWM</span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"margin-left:0cm; margin-right:0cm\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana,sans-serif\"><strong>Power Input</strong>: 12 VDC @2A PoE(need extra PoE module)</span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"margin-left:0cm; margin-right:0cm\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana,sans-serif\"><strong>Size&amp;Weight</strong>: 130x85mm</span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"margin-left:0cm; margin-right:0cm\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana,sans-serif\"><strong>OS</strong>: Linux</span></span></p>\r\n', 2, 'Yes', '2021-06-07', '<ul>\r\n	<li><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana,sans-serif\">Sunplus SP7021 &ldquo;Plus1&rdquo; quad-core Cortex-A7 processor</span></span></li>\r\n	<li><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana,sans-serif\">128MB or 512MB DDR3 DRAM</span></span></li>\r\n	<li><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana,sans-serif\">8GB eMMC</span></span></li>\r\n	<li><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana,sans-serif\">2x 10/100M Ethernet</span></span></li>\r\n	<li><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana,sans-serif\">industrial grade:-40C ~ +85&deg;C</span></span></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n', 'BPI-F2P', 78.99, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 0),
(163, 'BPI-F2S', 163, 'Active', '<ul>\r\n	<li><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana,sans-serif\">Sunplus SP7021 &ldquo;Plus1&rdquo; quad-core Cortex-A7 processor</span></span></li>\r\n	<li><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana,sans-serif\">128MB or 512MB DDR3 DRAM</span></span></li>\r\n	<li><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana,sans-serif\">8GB eMMC</span></span></li>\r\n	<li><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana,sans-serif\">2x 10/100M Ethernet</span></span></li>\r\n	<li><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana,sans-serif\">industrial grade:-40C ~ +85&deg;C</span></span></li>\r\n	<li><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana,sans-serif\">FPGA Interface</span></span></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n', '<p style=\"margin-left:0cm; margin-right:0cm\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana,sans-serif\"><strong>CPU: </strong>Quad-core 1GHz Cortex-A7 CPU, plus A926 and 8051 cores</span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"margin-left:0cm; margin-right:0cm\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana,sans-serif\"><strong>Memory: </strong>Built-in 128MB or 512MB DDR3 DRAM</span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"margin-left:0cm; margin-right:0cm\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana,sans-serif\"><strong>Storage: </strong>8G eMMC flash onboard<strong> </strong>MicroSD slot</span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"margin-left:0cm; margin-right:0cm\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana,sans-serif\"><strong>Network: </strong>2x 10/100M Ethernet<strong> </strong>RS-485<strong> </strong>RS-232</span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"margin-left:0cm; margin-right:0cm\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana,sans-serif\"><strong>Video Output: </strong>HDMI 1.4 output,camera I/F<strong> </strong>MIPI CSI connector</span></span></p>\r\n